\pard\qc\f0\fs28\b Correspondence Course in Astrology\par
\pard\qc\f1\fs22\i by Carl Payne Tobey\par
\pard\qc\f0\fs26\b Lesson #1\par
\pard\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain A Mathematical Study of Biological and Psychological DynamicsAstrology is a mathematical study of biological and psychological dynamics. It is the oldest\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain known science, and all other sciences appear to have been its children. It comes to us out of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain prehistoric times, and suggests the existence of a prehistoric civilization enlightened far\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain beyond our own in some respects. It was kept alive in the East, but it degenerated into much\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that was little more than superstition. It became associated with mysticism, fatalism and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain cultism, was taught only in secret schools, and was practically outlawed with the dawn of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Christian era.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Christianity taught a doctrine of free will. Fatalism was in conflict with this doctrine and since\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain it was believed that astrology was fatalism, it was outlawed. (See "THE STAR CROSSED\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain RENAISSANCE" by CAMERON ALLEN, DUKE UNIVERSITY PRESS). Although its funeral was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain held, its own dynamics would not allow it to die.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain A new word was coined. It was astronomy, a new science to take the place of astrology.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Originally, all astronomers were astrologers. The new science was to ultimately deny any\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain association between Planets and Man, but this did not come about immediately. In the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain beginning, it was merely the desire to deny astrology insofar as it might conflict with the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain freewill doctrine of the church. In the early 16th century, Paraselsus defined the difference\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain between astrology and astronomy of that time. He stated that astronomy confined itself to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain character delinations, while astrology was used to predict the future. He claimed that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrology could not predict for the individual because he had a choice that he could make\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that would affect the future, but he held that astrology could predict the future of the masses.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In effect, he was arguing that Man can live above his animal nature.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Modern textbooks carefully conceal the fact that the greatest minds they glorify are those of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the astrologers of history. It is regarded as "good taste" when textbook writers delete\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain anything and everything that demonstrates the part astrology has played in history. Some of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain these astrologers have been Aristarchus, Pythagoras, Ptoleiny, Copernicus, Kepler, Newton,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Paracelsus, Tycho Brahe, Benjamin Franklin and many others. Modern astronomers like to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain teach us that Copernicus discovered that the earth was not the center of the solar system,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain but Copernicus was merely going back to a defense of Aristarchus, who taught a heliocentric\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrology 200 years before the birth of Christ, and who learned it from the work of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Pythagoras who lived 500 B.C. While glorifying all these names, the astronomers try to claim\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain them as astronomers when they were actually astrologers.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain To study astrology, one has had to be an individualist, rugged enough to brush off the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain criticism of orthodox education. One could not study astrology and be a conformist.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Perhaps the three men who influenced the dawn of the 20th century astrology in a new\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain direction were Allen Leo, Sepharial and Llewellyn George. They provided enough printed\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain literature for new investigators ttal\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain One does not cause the other, but the same arithmetical principles that apply to the apples\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain apply also to the oranges. Mathematical principles are universal principles. They work\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain anywhere, any time. Astrology deals with these same principles.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There have been many attempts to explain astrology in terms of physical science, vibrations,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain electricity or light waves, but they are too simple, while astrology is too complicated and too\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain all-inclusive. Astrology seems to include everything. It involves the physical, the mental, the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain emotional, the vital, the concrete, the abstract. It even involves time and space, and strangely\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain relates all of these things to each other. It is the mathematics of Life. (Paul G. Clancy called it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the Algebra of Life.) It is a study of the abstract principles of existence, and there can be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain existence only in accord with those principles. Astrology explains life in terms of geometry.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It draws strange parallels that can never be found without it. What connection might there\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain be, for example, between executive ability and the sex organs, between interest in religion\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and the liver? We do not know, but astrology indicates that there is. There are many other\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain strange parallels. What you will learn here is merely what the writer has been able to dig out\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in 47 years. The principal thing he has learned in that time is that he hasn't scratched the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain surface. It is desirable that the student make no attempt to move too rapidly. There are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain certain basic factors that must be grasped. Speed may slow you down. Astrology is unlike\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain anything else you may have studied. We want you to prove every point to your own\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain satisfaction.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In the end, we want you to take our word for absolutely nothing. Astrology works, but it has\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to work exactly the same for you as it does for us. If we claim that 6 apples and 10 apples\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain equal fifteen apples, while you find that 6 oranges and 10 oranges equal sixteen oranges,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain there is something wrong. We must find agreement all the way.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In the writer's approach to this subject, he had to deal with many erroneous claims. He had to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain discover which claims were true and which claims were false. He was told that you have to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain accept astrology on faith. This was the most fabulous claim of all. Accept absolutely nothing\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain on faith. Astrology has to work in laboratory experiments. When you have finished this\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain course, you will merely have reached a starting point. You will be like the salesman who was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain trained in the New York office and then sent to Mexico City to start selling. Certain principles\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that worked in New York will also work in Mexico City, but down there folks speak Spanish.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Suppose we could say that there are twelve basic material elements and that all other\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain elements are combinations of these elements. It would simplify things. Astrology deals with\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain twelve basic principles, and everything grows out of intricate combinations and relationships\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain involving these twelve basic principles. The number of combinations may not be infinite, but\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain it might as well be. It is very great. An astrologer is only as good as his understanding of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain these twelve basic principles. Our greatest objective must be to learn as much as possible\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain about these twelve principles. You will not know all there is to know from us, because we do\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not know that much.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There is evidence that the ancients may have known that civilization was going into an\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain eclipse, and that they tried very hard to put certain information, hidden away in symbol form,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain where it could ultimately be found, interpreted and revived. There are some who believe that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the construction of the Great Pyramid was for the purpose of preserving mathematical and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrological knowledge during the dark ages until new initiates with an ability to understand\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain abstract principles could decipher the information that is hidden away in the dimensions and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain measurements of the pyramid. The Mexican Calendar Stone was carefully buried, only to be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain found many centuries later and to reveal a calendar more perfect than any then known to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain modern science. The first Spanish explorers, arriving in a new and unknown land, found the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain symbols of the signs of the zodiac carved on stone throughout Mexico, Central and South\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain America. (See "RED MAN'S CONTINENT" by ELLSWORTH HUNTINGTON, YALE\par
\pard\f0\fs22\b UNIVERSITY PRESS.)\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It would seem that all religious writers were attempting to get across the significance of two\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain numbers -- 12 and 7. Twelve tribes of Israel, twelve disciples of Christ, the Book with the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Seven Seals, etc. The Sphinx is an astrological symbol. Ancient religious works are filled with\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain terms which have an entirely different meanings in astrological terminology. This includes the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Bible. If you possessed information, it was necessary to hide it in order to avoid persecution.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain These facts need not seem strange when you realize that there are towns in the United\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain States today which have laws forbidding anyone to teach astrology. The Federal\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Communications Commission uses its pressure to keep it from being taught on the air, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain radio and television stations live in fear of having their license revoked if they disobey the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain wishes of those non-elected persons who constitute a Washington bureaucracy. As a result,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrological groups have sometimes incorporated as a religion, because under the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain constitution, you can't outlaw religion. This same procedure has been followed by advocates\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of Dianetics, who have changed their subject to Scientology and called it a religion to avoid\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain persecution by the American Medical Association, an institution bent upon a monopoly of all\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain things related to human health and even social relationships. The ultimate goal of socialized\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain medicine would achieve such an aim, but it has been opposed by a great part of the medical\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain profession because it might take control away from the A.M.A.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It is unlawful to ship astrological literature to Russia. It was a paradox to see an astrological\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain convention opened in Los Angeles, where astrology has been outlawed, but openly\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain practiced, by the man who was the Lieutenant Governor and later Governor. You can practice\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrology anywhere in the United States if you call it a religion. We practice it throughout the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain United States, and we do not call it a religion. The Post Office Department has no objection\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to astrology You can practice astrology anywhere in the U.S., if you call it a study of cycles.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain While the FCC bars astrology by name, they daily utilize data furnished by the Radio\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Corporation of America predicting magnetic storms from a study of the planets. Although we\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain point out these facts and inconsistencies, they should not bother you. We have been in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain business for 37 years, and they have neither bothered nor hindered us. It will take time and a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain great deal of money to eradicate ignorance from high places.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Astrology bases everything on the numeral 12, while mathematicians long claimed that the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain most perfect system of mathematics would be based on twelve instead of ten, the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain duodecimal system, instead of the decimal system. This fact appears to have significance. To\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain understand the significance of the seven throughout ancient literature, it is only necessary to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain realize that in ancient mathematics, there was no zero. That was later invented by the Hindus.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain When a circle was cut in twelve parts, and the lines between the parts were numbered, there\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain was no zero point. The first line was numbered as one instead of zero, and therefore, the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain halfway mark was seven, not six. Seven is not one-half of twelve, but you start counting the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain second half with seven, just as you start counting the first half with one. Astrology's seventh\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain principle is a very dynamic one, as we will later see. It deals with time and change, for without\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain change time ceases to exist. In the abstract world, there is no time. Time is merely an\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain expression of matter and space. There is psychological time, but it is unlike clock time. (In\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain recent years, many mathematicians have shifted their faith to the binary system of math,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain based on 2, but this is probably a fad, based on the fact that modern electronic calculators\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain employ the binary system plus another system based on 16, because 16 is the 4th power of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 2. The binary system was discovered by Leibnitz who lived 1646 to 1716 A.D. and who\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain employed it to try to convert the Emperor of China to Christianity.)\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Although the material parts of the solar system are the only material factors with which\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrology deals, there are many other factors, but they are geometrical and in the realms of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain pure abstraction. It should be mentioned that there are schools of astrology attempting to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain deal with fixed stars, but we recommend that the student stay away from any such theories\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain until he has finished Lesson Eleven of this course. After that, he is on his own. You will find\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that the astrologer speaks of things such as the signs of the zodiac as if they were as real as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the Empire State Building. They are as real, but they are not material. They are mere\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Geometrical angles and mathematical points. In his early days of investigation the writer tried\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to visualize the zodiac as a possible magnetic field, but this conception breaks down, unless a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain magnetic field is something quite different from what we suppose it to be. Also, the poles of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the earth's magnetic field do not conform to the poles of the zodiac.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The average astrology student of today has no clear conception of what the zodiac is. He\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain may view it as something extending far out in space, but it isn't. It is all right here. It doesn't\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain necessarily extend beyond the surface of the earth. It has no connection with the fixed stars.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It is an abstraction. It is a group of mathematical points which can be found from the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain relationship of the earth's equator to the earth's orbit. It would have no significance for a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain being born on Mars or any other planet. It is purely a product of motion -- the earth's motion\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain -- two earth motions, the rotation of the earth on its own axis and the revolution of the earth\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain along its own orbit. It is geometry, involving two planes of space, the plane of the earth's\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain equator and the plane of its orbit. To determine the zodiac, it is necessary to consider no\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain other factors in space, except for the fact that there are two foci to the ellipse of the earth's\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain orbit, and we must know which of these is occupied by the Sun.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It is important that you have a clear conception of what the zodiac is, and what it is not, for\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain then you can be saved many arguments with yourself or others as to why certain Systems of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrology being practiced are without valid foundation. Attempts to use a heliocentric (Sun as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain center) zodiac fall down, because there is nothing about the zodiac that is heliocentric. We\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain cannot draw a heliocentric zodiac, because we know too little about the path the Sun is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain taking through space. Each planet would have its own zodiac, which would have to be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain calculated from the relationship of its equator to its orbit and it would be quite different from\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain our zodiac. Its twelve points would not be in the same place. The zodiac, as we use it,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain constitutes a series of dynamics. If either motion of the earth were to suddenly cease, the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain zodiac would also cease to exist. Remember that. The zodiac is a product of motion alone.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain When you realize this, you will not be harboring the illusions concerning it that are prevalent\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in many minds today. Everything in astrology concerns dynamics and kindred phenomena.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Without motion, astrology would not exist.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Just as Euclid's geometry failed to meet the requirements of a mechanical and atomic age,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain some of the old conceptions of astrology must give way to the new geometry of dynamics.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Euclid's geometry failed to consider dynamics. Einstein and Relativity have changed things.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There is evidence that the arctic may have, at one time, been tropical, meaning that the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain equator was across a different part of the earth's surface At such a time, the zodiac may have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain been different from what it is today. We have a diagram that follows.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It will require some explanation. It is intentionally drawn out of proportion in order to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain illustrate and emphasize certain factors. You will see four large circles and one small circle.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The small circle represents the Sun, which is actually many, many times the size of the earth.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The four larger circles represent four positions of the earth in its trip around the Sun, spring,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain summer, autumn and winter. If you turn the diagram sideways, spring will be at the top,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain summer at the left, autumn at the bottom and winter at the right.. Note the odd fact that the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain earth is nearer to the Sun when we, in the Northern Hemisphere, have winter, farthest away\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain from the Sun when we, in the Northern Hemisphere, have summer. The reverse would be true\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain for people living south of the equator in the Southern Hemisphere. If heat is really something\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that travels through space from the Sun to the earth, then the average temperature south of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the equator should be warmer in summer and colder in winter than summer and winters in the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Northern Hemisphere. It is believed by some, however, that because there is far more ocean\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain south of the equator than north of the equator, the ocean absorbs heat from the Sun in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain summer and gives that heat off in the winter, modifying temperatures south of the equator\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain from what they might be otherwise. It does seem odd that when we, north of the equator,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain have winter, the earth is 3 million miles closer to the Sun than in summer. There is the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain alternative possibility that heat as we know it may be generated here at the earth AFTER\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain light from the Sun reaches the earth, in which event, distance of a planet from the Sun might\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain have no bearing on the temperature of that planet, a possibility that materialists, dogmatists\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and astronomers would hate to entertain.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain This diagram will emphasize the fact that the earth travels in an ellipse, not in a circle and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that it is closest to the Sun when we have winter. Now, we run into the difficulty of trying to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain illustrate a 3- dimensional factor on a. 2-dimensional piece of paper. Each circle representing\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the earth has a solid straight line representing the axis of the earth, with the north pole at the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain top, the south pole at the bottom. However, for the pole to be at this angle, you would have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to be looking at the earth with your eyes in the plane of the earth's orbit. Suppose you hold\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the earth in the position given, but drop the spring position of the earth down so that it is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain behind the Sun, raising the autumn position so that it is in front of the Sun. You would no\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain longer be able to see the Sun because it would be concealed by the autumn position of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain earth, which would also conceal the spring position of the earth, which would be behind both\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the autumn position of the earth and the Sun. Then, you would find the poles of the earth\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain exactly as given. The north pole would always tilt toward the right. It would not turn around\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain as the pole of a spinning top would do. It would not tilt to the left when in its summer\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain position The dotted straight line across the earth represents the equator. Note that in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain summer, the northern hemisphere tilts toward the Sun, while in winter it tilts away from the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Sun. This angle at which the hemisphere tilts seems to be the most important factor in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain determining temperature.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain However, there are only two moments out of a year when a straight line drawn from the Sun\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to the earth will also pass through the plane of the earth's equator. At those two moments\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and only during those two moments, can a straight line pass through both the plane of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain earth's orbit and the plane of the equator. These two moments are known as the spring and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain autumnal equinoxes, and they become the markers upon which we can base the whole\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain zodiac. Draw a straight line from the earth to the Focus occupied by the Sun at one of these\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain moments, and allow it to point always in the same direction. The earth moves on. This line no\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain longer points to the Sun, until six months later, the other end of the line will point to the Sun.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The line will point at no specific point on the earth's surface, because the earth itself is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain rotating within its zodiac. Temporarily, and for a matter of years, the line will point at some\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain fixed point in space, like a star, but even this is not permanent. The line points at absolutely\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain nothing material permanently. It is purely an abstraction, and yet, upon this abstraction all\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain else is based.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain This could all be wild dreaming except for one fact. Conclusions based on this line function.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain They work. They can be depended upon. This brings up the great question. How did men of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain an unknown time in history figure all this out? It seems impossible that it could have come to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain light through observation. It must have been calculated by some master mathematician who\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain knew something about human dynamics and mathematical principles that we do not know\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain today. His discovery eclipses the discovery of the atom by modern scientists. Next, using this\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain abstract line, he drew a circle around the earth in the plane of the earth's orbit, and divided it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain into twelve equal parts, and these became the signs of the zodiac. He knew something about\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain twelve that we do not know. He may have been a student of the duodecimal system.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We have reached the point where we have a circle divided into twelve equal parts. Up till\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain now, it is a mathematical figure -- no more, no less. The astrologer finds it related to twelve\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain principles in nature, quite extraordinary principles. We are going to devote a great deal of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain time to these principles. In fact, you can devote the rest of your life to them, and you will\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain always be learning something new. They are the principles of human dynamics. It would be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain truthful to say they are the principles of biological dynamics, for they do not confine\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain themselves to humans. They apply for a dog or a cat, but we cannot study astrology without\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain considering two other factors, evolution and heredity. As the writer has stated elsewhere, a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain horse can never become an accomplished pianist because of his heredity. Heredity is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain definitely a limiting factor. There is more fatalism to heredity than to astrology.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Throughout your study of astrology, this mathematical figure is going to be your ruler. You\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain are going to use it for purposes of measurement. The zodiac is not the only place where you\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain will use it. It will be used elsewhere. In fact it can be used in so many different places that it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain knocks any idea of a magnetic field into a cocked hat, unless there are millions and millions of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain magnetic fields all around us, and there may be, we do not know.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Mathematical rules work regardless of time or space. They are abstractions. They are, in no\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain way, affected by circumstances. They do not change. Observations made by Euclid or\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Pythagorus 2500 years ago can be made today. Even the mountains and fixed stars have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain changed in certain respects during that time, but not the rules of mathematics.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We need an illustration that will furnish us with a parallel, and we are going to utilize a well-\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain known mathematical formula for that illustration. Please don't run away. We will make it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain simple.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We have stated that astrology is a study of biological dynamics. Perhaps we should purify this\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain even more. Although we use astrology to grasp and understand biological dynamics, there is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain a part of astrology which can only be classified as a higher branch of mathematics. Now, let\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain us strike our parallel. We are going to use the Pythagorean Theorum.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Why not draw a right-angled triangle, meaning one where one of the angles is 90 degrees,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain like the corner of a square. Around this triangle, draw three squares. As a unit of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain measurement, use \'bc inch. The sides of this triangle are 3, 4 and 5 units. The longest line in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain this triangle is known as the hypotenuse. That is the one marked 5. Pythagorus discovered\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that in any such triangle, the area of the large square is exactly equal to the area of the two\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain smaller squares. Ever since his time, this has been known as the Pythagorean Theorum.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain (However, it was actually known by the ancient Chinese earlier.) The size of the triangle, or\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the relative length of the two legs (short sides) of the triangle will never alter the rule. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Theorum is expressed: (a * a) + (b * b) equals (c * c).\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain To demonstrate the universality of the law, we ask you to draw a triangle, where the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain dimensions are 5, 12 and 13. You can make up millions of such triangles of all sizes, and the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain law will always work. In some cases, you will deal with fractions, but you can use any odd\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain number for the short side and work out a triangle where all sides can be expressed in positive\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain integers (whole numbers). To get the other two sides, all you need do is square the first side,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and cut the result in half. Since the result is an odd number, and not divisible by two, you have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to have an answer that is a positive integer (whole number) plus 0.5. Now add 0.5 to get the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain longest of the two sides, and deduct 0.5 to get the other side. In other words, if the short\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain side of the triangle is 7, the square of 7 is 49, and when we cut 49 in two, we get 24.5. Add\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 0.5, and we get 25. Deduct 0.5, and we get 24. Thus (7 * 7) + (24 * 24) equals (25 * 25).\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Even using all the odd numbers to infinity in this way will not give you all the possible\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain triangles that can be made out of positive integers (whole numbers). There is an infinite\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain number of others. You will also note that in this particular series of triangles, the sum of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain two longer sides is always the square of the shorter side.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Having given this illustration, we have a very important point that we want to get across. In\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain fact, this is vital to any real understanding of astrology. When all right-angled triangles\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain conform to this law, we have coincidence. This does not mean that there is any cause-and-\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain effect phenomenon involved. One triangle is not the cause, nor is another triangle the effect.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Just as this rule will work for all possible right-angled triangles, the division of a circle into\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain twelve equal parts will work in astrology under many different unrelated conditions. Later,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain you will see that the right-angled triangle itself is very important in the study of astrology.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In mathematics, there are undoubtedly infinite other rules similar to the Pythagorean\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Theorum that can be applied to triangles in which no angle is 90 degrees. No mathematician\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain has ever taken the time to work them out. Perhaps the idea has never entered his head.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Never gain the impression that mathematicians have ever scratched more than the surface of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain their subject. There is so much about which we have never thought to inquire.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Everything, absolutely everything, in astrology is a study of angles and, mathematical points.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We will even find that certain angles have some mysterious connection with the distance of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain an object from the central point of a sphere. The inference is that an object cannot move\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain without setting in motion some very complicated system of dynamics. Time and space may\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain assume entirely new meanings to you. The solar system is one monstrous atom, and Heaven\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain knows what might happen if one of its electrons (planets) was pulled away. This is new\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain geometry, but it is a dynamic geometry, not the dead geometry of Euclid.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We will save ourselves much trouble and many sleepless nights, if we start out by considering\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrology, not as a cause-and-effect phenomenon, but as a system of higher mathematics. Do\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not let this scare or drive you away. It is important to your understanding, but there are vast\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain numbers of students, using astrology from a practical point of view, who have almost no\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain education whatever in the field of mathematics. One such student, doing very well otherwise,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain told the writer, "You know, I can't tell you how much is 9 X 9, without working it out in my own\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain way."\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Many students catch and grasp the basic principles with almost no knowledge whatever of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the mathematical side of astrology. Yet, such people have helped to keep astrology alive\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain down through the centuries. It must be stated, however, that under these circumstances,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain many errors, some of a mathematical nature, have crept into astrology as it has been taught\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain over the last few hundred years. These must be brought to light and corrected. Under those\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain circumstances, to think that the combined efforts of all its materialistic enemies have been\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain unable to dent interest in the subject might almost be interpreted to mean that some guiding\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain principles never intended to allow it to die out. This fact is as mysterious as the man who\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain worked out these laws originally. It has been as diffIcult to wipe out astrology as to wipe out\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain religion. There are some things that refuse to die. Astrology is one of them. It has outlived\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain every enemy it ever had. It has outlived the civilizations of its enemies.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Thus, we have reached a point where we have a circle divided into twelve equal parts. Let us\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain go on from there.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Because of the ancient's plan of hiding knowledge behind symbols many weird\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain interpretations have sprung from their writings. We are going to take four ancient terms and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain tell you what they mean. The terms are FIRE, EARTH, AIR and WATER. Because of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain constant use of these terms, which were astrological, moderns have convinced themselves\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that these ancients were under the impression that there are only four elements. In\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain "Mathematics for the Million", Hogben points out that Pythagorus associated these words\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain with triangles, and Hogben thought it was quite silly but amusing. So, let us tell you what\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain these words mean. They are psychological terms.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain \u8226?\par
\pard\f0\fs22\b FIRE means VITAL\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain
\pard\f1\fs20\plain \u8226?\par
\pard\f0\fs22\b EARTH means PHYSICAL\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain
\pard\f1\fs20\plain \u8226?\par
\pard\f0\fs22\b AIR means INTELLECTUAL\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain
\pard\f1\fs20\plain \u8226?\par
\pard\f0\fs22\b WATER means EMOTIONAL\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The twelve signs of the zodiac were divided into four groups. There were FIRE signs, EARTH\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain signs, AIR signs and WATER signs. The three signs of a group were always spaced 120\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain degrees apart, so that each group formed a perfect equilateral triangle, and the four groups,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain when fitted together formed the circle divided into twelve equal parts.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Do not lose sight of the fact that we are still in the realms of the abstract, because all this\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain grows from that mathematical point in time, when it is possible to draw a straight line\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain through both the plane of the earth's orbit and the plane of the earth's equator. We measure\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain from there.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Biological dynamics have to do with a circle divided into twelve equal parts, representing the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain vital, the physical, the intellectual and the emotional -- four equilateral triangles, with three\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain corners each, adding up to twelve, the base of the duodecimal system of mathematics. As we\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain go along, you will find that the pieces all fit together perfectly, and everything always comes\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain out even.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There were three more words--CARDINAL, FIXED and MUTABLE.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The zodiacal signs were also divided into four CARDINAL signs, four FIXED signs, and four\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain MUTABLE signs, making up the twelve. This gave one Cardinal sign of each element, one\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Fixed sign of each element and one Mutable sign of each element.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Just as the zodiac can be divided into four equilateral triangles, it is also divided into three\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain squares, one representing four Cardinal signs, one representing four Fixed signs, and one\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain representing four Mutable signs.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We have expressed this in our diagrams with geometrical figures. Throughout astrology, you\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain will always be dealing with geometrical figures. You will always be dealing with 12-sided\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain figures or divisions thereof. This appears to be a basic principle of nature known to the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ancients, but, let us point out that you can find this division of a circle into twelve parts\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain elsewhere in nature. It is common to say that a snowflake has six sides, a pattern repeated six\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain times. Actually, however, each one-sixth is the same pattern repeated twice, once mirrored.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Therefore, like the zodiac every snowflake has TWELVE sides. Here again, we see the base\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of the duodecimal system.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain To think of the zodiac and its implications as ridiculous is to think of a snowflake as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain riducu1ous. What is more ridiculous than that all snowflakes should have the same number of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain sides. Because we find that all snowflakes do have the same number of sides, we recognize\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that a principle of nature is at work, and we accept the result. Crystals also form with six\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain sides, and various types of rock formations do the same thing. Nature functions\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematically. In the zodiac also, we find a principle of nature at work, and we have to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain accept the result.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Some writers have drawn attention to the symbol of the Christian religion -- the cross -- and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain they maintain it to be the astrological square. The Bible is filled with astrological terms and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain symbology. The symbol of the Jewish religion is the six-pointed star, two equi1atera1\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain triangles. Actually, there should be no conflict between astrology and religion. There is no\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain conflict between astrology and any legitimate branch of science. There may be conflict\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain between astrology and unproved theories and dogma but unlike astrology, scientific theories\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain are often in the realm of fashions. They have no permanence. We need think only of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain billiard ball conception of the atom that was prevalent not so long ago. The modern theory of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the atom conforms more to the ancient's saying,"as above, so below." Because RCA set up\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain their own investigative and research department, their Propagation Department, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain dropped accepted and fashionable theories, they found that geometrical figures formed by\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the planets can be used to predict the condition of terrestrial magnetism at any and all times.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The geometrical figures established by their research were the same established by the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrologers long before the dawn of any written history. The Astrological Alphabet There are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 31 principle letters in the astrological alphabet. Ultimately you will have to memorize these,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and we present them herewith.\par
