\pard\qc\f0\fs28\b Correspondence Course in Astrology\par
\pard\qc\f1\fs22\i by Carl Payne Tobey\par
\pard\qc\f0\fs26\b Lesson #6\par
\pard\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The Reform Dynamic Guides, Part 1Part One In Lesson Two we dealt with the Survival Dynamics. In Lesson Three we dealt with\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the Survival Dynamic REACTORS. We illustrated that the Survival Dynamic REACTORS are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain always opposite the Survival Dynamics in the zodiac.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In Lesson Five we dealt with the Reform Dynamics. Opposite each Reform Dynamic we find a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Reform Dynamic GUIDE.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Hidden within the unconscious, within the superconscious of each and every one of us, are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain three GUIDES. A study of these Reform Guides is a study of the DESIGN of the intellect.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain A natural ability to predict or calculate the future is inherent in Man, but it does not function\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in the majority of people. This is partly due to education, which has placed this talent beyond\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain society's frame of reference. It is also partly due to mental and emotional indigestion on the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain part of society and its individuals.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We have been taught to be practical rather than intellectual. The Greeks were well on their\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain way in the culture of Alexandria. They produced the greatest of mathematicians. They had\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain made remarkable progress with their mechanical inventions, but in 148 B.C., their great\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain library was destroyed by the Christians to abolish pagan science. That which is practical is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain often a matter of perpetuating the past on the theme that it is safe to do things as they were\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain done yesterday. The Greek philosophers and mathematicians were true intellectuals. They\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain saw DESIGN in nature and throughout the abstract world. The materialists never see\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain DESIGN. They have no contact with the world of the abstract.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We must all understand what is meant when we use the words INTELLECT and ABSTRACT,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain because modern usage of these words is very loose. We have passed through an era when\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain people have been taught to think objectively in terms of things and their size, rather than in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain terms of abstractions and overall principles which never change. The materialists do not see\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the abstract as something of itself, and are unable to visualize it except in material terms.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Psychology's Watson, and the whole behaviorist school of thought demonstrated an inability\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to visualize abstract principles. They were completely unable to distinguish the observed\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain from the observer. The tiniest particles have been picked apart in an effort to discover life\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain itself as a piece of matter hidden behind a piece of matter. Even the Spiritualist finds it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain necessary to explain the departed as function- ing in an astral body, which is merely a body\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of more rarified material, like that of a giant star. Almost nowhere do we find any effort to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain discover life as an abstraction. Most modern religious conceptions are materialistic\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain conceptions. Materialistic interpretations have grown up around conceptions that were\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain originally abstractions.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Mathematics is a science of ABSTRACT DESIGN, although it is often taught merely as a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain science of measurement. Size and measurement are elastic and relative. You can measure\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain something only as it relates to something else. The laws of mathematics are in no way\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain dependent on matter for their existence, but matter is completely dependent upon the laws\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of mathematics for its existence. They are abstract laws. In the abstract world nothing ever\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain changes, and where there is no change, there is no time. Although some materialists claim\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that a mathematical formula is non-existent until Man thinks of it, this is the same as saying\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that Neptune was non-existent until we thought of it. This is a way of making Man the creator\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of what he only discovers.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In our use of the word INTELLECT, we will mean that part of the MIND (not brain) that is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain capable of seeing or visualizing the ABSTRACT as something separate and apart from the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain material. ABSTRACT will mean existing independently of the material.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain To all great mathematicians of all times mathematics has been a science of DESIGN, and they\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain have all described it as something beautiful. The average student may see nothing beautiful\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain about his mathematical textbook. Instead, it may represent drudgery and confusion. This is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain merely what textbook writers have made of mathematics. To Pythagoras, Aristarchus, Euclid,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Khayyam, Copernicus, Kepler, Fermat, Einstein and others, mathematics was a thing of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain beauty. They saw SYMMETRY and DESIGN. Some were seeking a divine plan, for nothing\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain exists or functions except in accord with mathematical design. The men who have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain revolutionized scientific thought have usually been those who could visualize COSMIC\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain DESIGN. They are followed by materialists who explain their discovery in warped\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain materialistic terms. The materialist is a non-intellectual who can judge the future only by the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain past. He can explain anything after it happens. He never discovers abstract principle because\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain he is unaware of its existence. It is beyond his frame of reference.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We have earlier explained how astronomy broke away from astrology with the Christian era\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and became a materialistic science. As written, the modern history of astronomy is largely\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain fiction. It would have us believe that the ancients were little above animals in their mental\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain conceptions, and that their astronomy came about merely as a result of their wanting to know\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain when to plant crops. All of this fiction has been a part of the effort to promote materialism.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The astronomer would have you believe that until 1543 A.D., people believed the earth to be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the center of the solar system. Nothing could be further from the truth. The idea that the Sun\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain traveled around the earth was a product of Christianity. It was called the realistic view of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain things. Materialists always have a "realistic" view of things.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Discovery of the Sun as the center of the solar system is attributed to Copernicus. Actually,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain when Copernicus published his DE REVOLUTIONIBUS in 1543, he did not present his views\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain as original. He merely employed mathematics to prove that one obtained more perfect\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematical DESIGN when one went back to the pre-Christian, pre-astronomy, astrological\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain point of view, and considered the Sun as the center. He was defending the ideas and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain conceptions of Aristarchus, who lived more than 200 years before Christ. He was upsetting\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the geocentric (earth-as-the-center) views of Ptolemy, who lived in 150 A.D. It was the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematicians who came to the defense of Copernicus (not the astronomers), because they\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain recognized that he had found more perfect abstract DESIGN. Mathematical history indicate\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that before Aristarchus, Phythagoras also taught a heliocentric (Sun-as-the- center) system in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 500 B.C. Thus, as usual we find the astronomers were 2000 years behind in adopting a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain heliocentric system. This is probably an under estimation, because there were other\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain civilizations thousands of years before the Greeks, and nowhere do we find evidence that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain they taught that the earth was the center of the solar system. In another 2000 years,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astronomers may teach that we believed the earth to be square, because Rand McNally\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain publishes their maps within a square frame.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Because he believed in COSMIC SYMMETRY AND DESIGN, Copernicus sought more perfect\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematical design, and he found the design to be more perfect mathematically when he\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain adopted the views of the pre- Christian Greeks and considered the Sun as the center.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Kepler lived 1571-1650. He was a German astrologer who wrote books on astrology. Modern\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astronomical textbooks claim him only as an astronomer. He believed in a divine plan, and as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain a result of his belief, he attempted to find more perfect mathematical DESIGN in the solar\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain system. He discovered the three laws of planetary motion. He discovered that if you draw\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain two lines from the center of the sun to two points on the orbit of a planet, the motion of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain planet from one point to the other will have a definite relationship to the area enclosed.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Sir Isaac Newton was also an astrologer, who refused to argue astrology with Halley because\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Halley had never studied the subject. He was a mathematician who saw beauty, symetry and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain design in the universe, as a result of which, he discovered the mathematical laws of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain gravitation. To this day, neither astronomers nor physicists have been able to fit gravitation\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Into their materialistic scheme of things. They have been unable to explain gravitation in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain terms of cause-and-effect, because there is a complete absence of a time factor.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Albert Einstein never studied astrology, but he was a mathematician and an abstractionist as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain well as an intellectual. Like others before him, he was seeking beauty, symmetry and design\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in the universe. He discovered relativity.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The atom is a blow to all cause-and-effect conceptions. We refer to the mathematical\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain conception of the atom, because we know only about the mathematical conception of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain atom. No one has ever seen an atom. According to this rnathematical conception of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain atom, an electron can leave one orbit and appear in another orbit simultaneously. There is no\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain time factor for the electron to pass from one orbit to the other. It does not traverse the in-\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain between space. For the electron, that "space" is nonexistent. To materialistic science, this is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain both a shock and a new principle, but it is an old principle to the world of psychic\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain phenomena, where there has long been a word for it that does not appear in the writer's\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain dictionary. The word is TELEPORTATION, and it is frequently found in literature dealing with\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain psychic phenomena. Physical science is now up against the fact that it finds itself completely\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain unable to explain matter except in abstract mathematical terms. The causal hypothesis and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the whole materialistic conception of things is ripping at the seams.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We have described the zodiac as an abstraction rather than as something material. We have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain described astrology as something abstract rather than as something material, just as we have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain described mathematics as pure abstraction. It is vitally important that we get across to you\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain what we mean when we speak of the abstract, because you are not going to understand\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain what we are about to explain unless you grasp our meaning. So let us take another example\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of something that is completely abstract rather than material.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain A number is an abstraction. Each number has limitless characteristics, but no two numbers\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain anywhere to infinity will have EXACTLY the same characteristics. 510,510 is the only number\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain under a million that can be divided by the first seven primes. Thus, if we were to give you a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain problem, and you discovered that the answer would have to be under a million and also that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the answer was divisible by the first seven primes, you could know at a glance that this is the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain only possible answer to the problem. It would save you a lot of work. These facts are pure\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain abstraction. Their truth is not dependent on anything material, but material things can be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain employed to illustrate the abstraction for those who cannot visualize the abstract.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Materialists are those in whom the INTELLECT does not function.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Occasionally we find an individual who appears born with a knack of computing mathematical\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain problems in his head more quickly than can be accomplished with an electronic calculator.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There have been children who beat the greatest chess players, until they were educated and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain learned to do things the hard way. These people never seem able to explain their methods,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and "science" has always found It more convenient to ignore such cases than try to explain\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain them. There is an explanation, however, because if you determine the characteristics of an\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain unknown answer to a problem the answer can be obtained much more simply than any\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain methods found in a mathe- matical textbook, and in much less time. The human mind is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain capable of solving problems that no man-made calculating device can approach.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In this presentation of astrology, we are presenting an abstract mathematical pattern of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain zodiac. Life functions only in accord with this abstract mathematical design. It is the abstract\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain design of life, life itself being considered as abstract. We find the INTELLECT represented by\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the AIR signs of the zodiac, which we have termed the Reform Dynamic GUIDES. In the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain zodiac, the INTELLECT is represented by another perfect equilateral TRIANGLE. (It should\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain be realized that the triangle is the simplest possible two-dimensional figure. You cannot have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain a two-dimensional figure of less than three sides, but you can have one with any number of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain sides if the number is greater than three.) There is a GUIDE opposite each Reform Dynamic\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in the zodiac. The three GUIDES and their zodiacal counterparts are as follows.\par
\pard\f0\fs22\b GUIDE- ZODIACAL EQUIVALENT\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain
\pard\f0\fs22\b INDIVIDUAL REFORM DYNAMIC GUIDE- AQUARIUS\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain
\pard\f0\fs22\b FAMILY REFORM DYNAMIC GUIDE- LIBRA\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain
\pard\f0\fs22\b SOCIAL REFORM DYNAMIC GUIDE- GEMINI\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain
\pard\f1\fs20\plain As we have pointed out previously, the Survival Dynamics and the Survival Dynamic Reactors\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain go around the zodiac counterclockwise, while the Reform Dynamics and the Reform Guides\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain go around the zodiac clockwise. Remember this, and it will give you a more graphic picture.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain By visualizing the abstract, it is possible to visualize the future, providing you do nothing now\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that would change the future, but this visualization may not be in the conscious but in the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain superconscious. It is necessary to calculate the future, but this process need not necessarily\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain be a conscious one. Just as we find an unconscious interpretive apparatus associated with\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the subconscious, we find an unconscious calculating apparatus associated with the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain superconscious.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The GUIDES do not function for a great many people, who. have been hypnotized into the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain belief that there are no such guides, for these guides are contrary to the doctrine of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain materialism in both the scientific and religious worlds. Although we have cut ourselves off\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain from the guides in order to adapt ourselves to our prevalent social structure, they sometimes\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain work in spite of us. Neither do the guides function in the face of mental and emotional\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain indigestion. Neither do they work in the face of fear. Fear belongs to the Water and Earth\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Signs. It is never found in the Fire and Air Signs. Fear causes one to cling to material security.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We can see why Christ placed such great emphasis on FAITH in God. The man who really has\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain faith harbors no fear, and the GUIDES have a better opportunity to function. An over-\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain emphasis of WATER and EARTH in a chart or horoscope may make faith extremely difficult\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain unless mental and emotional digestion can be effected. Mental and emotional indigestion is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the principle cause of many varieties of illness.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The subconscious of the average person is filled with experience that has never been\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain digested mentally and emotionally. It has been our experience that when emotional\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain indigestion is cleared up, the GUIDES begin to function normally. Suddenly, there is no\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain indecision. The individual knows what he wants to do, knows what he should do, and does it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain without hesitation. Emotional indigestion is the cause of many hidden unconscious fears.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain With a healthy being, there are no hidden fears. His view is always of the future, and it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain becomes necessary for him to utilize every waking moment either altering that future or\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain harmoniously fitting himself into it.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain However, we will later see that there are astrological times when the GUIDES are clouded,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain other times when they work in spite of us, just as we might say that there is a time to be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain awake and a time to be asleep. If we are asleep when the GUIDES are clouded, we will be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain less inconvenienced. It is our view and experience that there is much that we can do to clear\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain up emotional indigestion, and much that we can do to cooperate and allow the guides to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain function as they were intended to function. There may be little the individual can do until he\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain overcomes his materialistic education, which has taught him to ignore and never investigate\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain anything lying outside the frame of reference of modern religion, education and science.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Through religious creeds, scientific hypotheses and education, the masses have been\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain hypnotized to hold their attention within the frame of reference of modern educational\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain limitations. One of the principle aims of our research, at the present moment, is to find the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain means of clearing up mental and emotional indigestion, and in some cases, we have had\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain remarkable result.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It is interesting to note that just as it was the mathematicians who came to the rescue of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain claims of Copernicus, 4OO years later, it was the mathematicians who came to the rescue of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the work of Dr. J.B.Rhine of Duke University, when it was being attacked almost universally by\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the psychologists, biologists and physicists of the United States and Canada. It is possible\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that after the mathematicians endorsed the methods of Rhine in open convention, the critics\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ran to their seclusion because as materialists they were completely unprepared and incapable\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of dealing with the mathematical side of the picture due to their inability to deal with the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain abstract. Insofar as the materialists were concerned, extrasensory perception could not be,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain because a thought would have to be something material that would travel through the air and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ultimately make a landing. The mathematicians took an abstract view of the evidence, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain asserted that it was impossible to obtain the Rhine results by chance. The materialists ran to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain cover, because they did not have the mental equipment to deal with abstract mathematics.\par
\pard\f0\fs22\b THE INDIVIDUAL REFORM DYNAMIC GUIDE\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The Individual Reform Dynamic Guide is represented by AQUARIUS. Its symbol was a man\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain pouring water from an urn, and it is possible that this symbol was intended to portray the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain separation of the abstract from the material. It could represent the "soul" leaving the material\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain body. Aquarius was associated with the ankles and with the blood. In its negative phases, it is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain associated with paralysis. This can apply biologically or when a labor union goes on strike in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain an effort to force an issue. The Aquarian is an abstractionist who sees things, not as they\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain were, not as they are, but as they will he. He unconsciously senses the trend ahead. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain process of unconscious calculation is ever going on. Instead of identifying security with the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain past, he sees only the imperfections of the past, taking the good for granted. The past and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain present stimulate only restlessness and irritability. He never figures that it can't happen here.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Instead, he is sure that it will, and he is alert for it. He is inclined to view material things as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain responsibilities rather than as assets. If they hold him down or limit him, he wants to break\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain away from them. He harbors the spirit of the hobo. He likes to keep on going on. Because he\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain always sees how things could be done, he is inventive. Evangeline Adams wrote that these\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain people tend to live a hundred years ahead of their times. They often accomplish the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain impossible. Let us see who some of these people have been.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Among persons who had Aquarius on the ascendant at birth, we might list Abdul Baha\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain (mystic), Charles de Gaulle (and many other successful military leaders), Havelock Ellis (ahead\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of his time with sex), George Washington Goethals (who built the Panama Canal after others\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain had failed), Osa Johnson (explorer), Dr. Carl Jung (pioneer in psychiatry and in questioning\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the causal hypothesis), Ana Nonus Kingsford (mystic), Andre Lamont (occultist)~ Abraham\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Lincoln (who started a job the world hasn't yet finished), David Lloyd George, William G.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Macdoo (who built the first tunnel under the Hudson River), Karl Marx (about whose\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain originations we are still fighting), Meher Bab (mystic), J.P.Morgan, Sr., (who gave us our\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain railroads), Emmeline Pankhurst (one of the original suffragists), Wiley Post (first man to fly\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain around the world solo), H.G. Wells (whose novels were an uncannily accurate portrayal of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain future), Paul Whiteman (pioneery in music), Sir George Wilkins (explorer), and the Duke of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Windsor (who couldn't stand the old style limitations and confinements of being an old\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain fashioned king).\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Among persons having the Sun in Aquarius, we might name Evangeline Adams (astrologer),\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Roy Chapman Adnrews (explorer), Sidney K. Bennett (astrologer), Jack Benny, Edgar Bergen,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Eddie Cantor (and many other comedians whose role is surprise), Charles Dickens (and many\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain other authors), "Diviner" (German astrologer), Louis DeWohl (astrologer), Thomas Edison\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain (and many other inventors), Havelock Ellis (again), Clark Gable (and many successful actors\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and actresses), John Barrymore, Rupert S Gleadow (astrologer), Augusta Foss Heindel\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain (occultist), Blanca Holmes (astrologer), L. Johndro (astrologer), John L. Lewis and Samuel\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Gompers (the strike was their weapon), Abraham Lincoln (again), Douglas McArthur (who\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain couldn't conform to Harry Truman), S.R.Parchment (occultist), both Jean and Auguste Picard\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain (balloon pioneers), Sir Ernest Shackelton (explorer), Frederick Spenceley (occultist), Sir Henry\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Morton Stanley (explorer), Hugo Stinnes, Jules Verne (whose fiction predicted the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain submarine), Franklin D. Roosevelt (who revolutionized the U.S. Government and almost\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain revolutionized the U.S. Supreme Court), Adlai Stevenson, Evarts C. Walton (astrologer),\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Charles Darwin (who made us evolution conscious and changed the course of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain biology),Chaales Lindbergh (first to fly the Atlantic alone), and "wrong way" Corrigan.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain One does not have to study these names long to know that these people are different. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrologers and occultists were not stopped by the blind conventionalism of the educational\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain world. All of these people were ready to investigate or plunge into the unknown. They were\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not hampered by insecurity. They were not trying to perpetuate the past. They were non-\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain conformists. They were never willing to leave well enough alone. They were not content to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain live and let live. Their purpose could hardly be called survival. They fear not what is ahead.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain They do not fear death, nor are they worried about starvation. Ties are easily broken. Time is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain change, and they want change. They think in terms of motion, not in terms of stationary\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain objects. They love action and excitement. There is a sadistic delight in seeing the old order\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain destroyed. Ideas are more important than money. The two together can do extraordinary\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain things. One man is tied to a certain place because that locality is his home. His family and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain friends are there. He has a job which he cannot leave. This man is not likely to be an\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Aquarian. An abstractionist, Aquarius is not tied to material things. He sees more reality in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain abstract ideas.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The material world is in a state of constant flux, but not the abstract world. It is important not\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to mistake the world of imagination for the world of the abstract. The world of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain imagination is merely a place where material things are shifted around visually and mentally.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The world of the abstract, as found in the laws of physics and mathematics, never changes. It\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is without time. From one millennium to another, everything remains exactly the same.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Although you may learn about the abstract world from others, you can have a direct contact\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain with that world within yourself. Did anyone tell Pythagoras about the Pythagoean theorem?\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Did anyone tell Kepler about the laws of planetary motion? Did anyone tell Newton about the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain laws of gravitation? Most discoveries appear to be accidental, but actually, the individual is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain looking for something he feels. Something within himself leads him to the point where the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain discovery is made. His conception of things may not have been exact before he made the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain discovery, but there was a general pattern or design. He may not have been conscious of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain what he was seeking, but in his superconscious, this was known.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain To go on strike seems to be an Aquarian idea. It isn't just a means of forcing action on an\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain employer. It is also an outlet for the worker, a break in the killing routine, a bit of excitement,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain an opportunity for a change of pace, a means of mental and emotional digestion.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Unlike Cancer or Capricorn, Aquarius is not conservative. He is radical. All men who turn up\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain with a new and better idea are looked upon as radicals in their time. They are not considered\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain as intelligent, but are 1ooked upon as "crackpots." Fulton with his steamboat was a crackpot.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The early rnotorists were crackpots. This writer can recall when, as you drove for a Sunday\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain spin through the country in a motorcar, the whole family of a farmer would run out to yell,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain "Get a horse." We were told that an auto-mobile would never be practical. There was nothing\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain like a good, old, reliable horse. If the teachings of Christ are studied, we find this Aquarian\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain principle strong, but we often find the Christian church standing for the very opposite\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain principles. The past is worshipped. If a couple make a mistake and get married only to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain discover incompatibility, they are denied the right to correct the mistake. They are told that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain marriages are made in heaven, which considerably detracts from the advisability of going to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain such a place. Christ was an intellectual, but many of his followers can interpret his teachings\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain only in materialistic terms.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain All of the astrologers and the mystics were seeking a better way of life. Most everything the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Aquarian accomplishes is regarded as impossible until he does it. It is not so far back when\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the great majority of both sexes did not regard women as sufficiently intelligent or well\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain informed to be qualified to vote for public officers. Why did men like the Wright Brothers,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Wiley Post, Lindbergh, Corrigan, and so many others, want to fly when it was safe to stay on\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the ground? Men like H.G.Wells and Jules Verne had. only their intellect to guide them in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain accurately portraying the future. To them, it was probably the only way that things could\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain happen. They had to go that way.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We see a different principle working in connection with British royalty, where tradition is far\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain more important than human happiness. Surprisingly, however, they do not insist that their\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain navy fight with the same old wooden ships.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The success of Aquarian comedians seems to be based on the fact that they can follow the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain functioning of the average human mind. They know it will follow a pattern of habit, and they\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain inject an element of surprise, which is mental and emotional relief to the audience. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain conventional routine of thinking is broken, with the result that there is exhilaration which\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain expresses itself in the form of laughter. The humor of a joke disappears after it has been told\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain a number of times.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain To the Aquarian, evolution is too slow, and he finds he can do much to speed it up. We fight\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain against taxes and government payrolls, but these things take people out of circulation and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain leave more business and more ways of making money for the taxpayers. They can sell things\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to those on the government payroll. What if all those on the government payroll suddenly\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain became farmers?\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Leo likes change and excitement just as much as Aquarius, but he does not have the same\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ability to see where it is leading. There is need for the guide, but a long time might elapse\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain before change make this need ap-parent. Leo may have calculated the change differently. He\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain may often get opposite results to those he expected. A good example of such opposite\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain results would be when a Leo, Herbert Hoover, met up with the 1929 stock market crash. He\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain was unprepared for it. On the other hand, when an Aquarian, Franklin Roosevelt, met up with\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the bank holiday four years later, he rose to the occasion. He solved the problem by altering\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the laws and principles of the government, of the banks, and of the stock market. Twenty-\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain three years later, we have had no recurrence of a panic, while prior to 1933, panics arrived\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain cyclically. We have had the same cycles since, but we have had no panics.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain If the Individual Reform Dynamic Guide is harmonious in a horoscope, there is the tendency\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to harmoniously design the life in accord with what is about to happen. This is not necessarily\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain done consciously. It is done superconsciously. The individual merely follows his urges. He\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain needs no guide other than the one that is hidden in his own unconscious.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain When the Individual Reform Dynamic Guide is inharmonious, there may be just as much\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain genius, just as much ability to see ahead, but the individual sees too far ahead for all practical\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain purposes. We might say that he is several cycles ahead of himself, and this is as disastrous as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain being several cycles behind. Before the stock market crash in 1929, there were many in Wall\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Street who "knew" that the crash had to come. Some sold the market short too soon and lost\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain their shirts. Others sold their stocks too late and lost their shirts. A song or a book is often\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain written and ignored because the world isn't ready for it. The same song or book becomes\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain very popular after the writer is dead.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Lancelot Hogben, the mathematician, wrote, "The most brilliant intellect is a prisoner within\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain its own social inheritance." The intellectual is seldom appreciated in his own day. After he\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain dies, a materialistic conception of him is prepared, and we worship that materialistic\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain conception.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain When the ISD Guide is afflicted, the result is terrific impatience and irritability with the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain present form, and the individual is called destructive. A boy may have a yen for throwing\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain rocks through plate glass windows. There can be sarcasm and a critical attitude toward\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain everything anyone else may do. To destroy is a thrill. We often see a person destroy himself\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain by means of an "accidenta1". Unconsciously, he wants to get on with things, which he cannot\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain do in his present form. When studying accidents or illness astrologically, it is always well to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain look carefully to see what purpose has been served by the accident or illness. You will often\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain find that a very definite unconscious purpose has been served.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It is quite apparent that the list of names we have given might be considered as a group of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain non-conformists, people who were unwilling to accept things as they found them. Many of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain these people were way ahead of their time. They were conscious of the future rather than of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the past. We could also have included many statesmen whose views were condemned as too\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain radical. While it is the nature of Aquarius to touch off dynamite to see what will happen, in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain these people, we find selfishness at a low ebb. An Aquarian may destroy himself for a cause.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain His security is not in material things but in abstract things. The most revolutionary labor\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain leaders have been born under this sign. They destroyed old conceptions of servitude.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Aquarius is unorthodoxy. The Aquarian, within himself, is not sensitive to what society thinks\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of him, because he looks upon society as dull and stupid.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Both marriage and divorce are associated with this guide. Each is a means of changing one's\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain individual life. There is a take-a-chance attitude, because one thing will always lead to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain another. The hobo attitude prevents one from definite attachment to environment. This\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain principle would not apply to a marriage that is based solely on a desire for security.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Just as the Water and Earth signs are locked in the past, Aquarius and the other Air and Fire\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain signs are locked in the future. If you know what is coming next, it is difficult to wait for it. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Aquarian is not susceptible to mob psychology. He thinks for himself and often has a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain hypnotic effect on others. We often find an excellent sense of humor when he can point out\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the obvious that others never see, with the result that it lends surprise and strikes people\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain funny.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The three Guides exist in each and every one of us, but they are often subdued. When the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain unconscious is too clogged with the past, with mental and emotional indigestion, the GUIDES\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain become dormant and will not function.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain To predict the future is to understand the functioning of nature. A good chess player\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain calculates his own moves far ahead, and is able to predict what a poor chess player will do\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain next. The bull fighter knows in advance that the bull will go for red. It is the nature of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain beast. In predicting the future by astrology, we must not be misled by the so-called favorable\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and unfavorable aspects. The next man to be elected President need not be the one who has\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the more favorable aspect, but the one whose chart best fits or blends with the interval\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ahead. Too many people consider a day as favorable if they can do what they want to,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain unfavorable if they can't. Many an individual has been murdered because he was able to what\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain he wanted to do. You might have considered the victories of Hitler as favorable for him, but\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain see where they led. Neither must we lose sight of the fact that we can make the future. Too\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain many people are dissatisfied with the kind of a future they made for themselves. In a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain revolution, the wealthy are often the first to be murdered. The poor man is never murdered\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain for his riches. Thieves are not attracted to paupers.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain You change yourself when you change your environment, because you react differently You\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain also react differently when in the presence of different people. You may be at ease in the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain presence of one person, nervous and restless in the presence of another. You select\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain associates in whose presence you have the kind of a reaction that suits you. You are a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain different person in the wilderness than in the city. Change of environment is a means of not\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain surviving as you are. Change is a means of individual Reform. When you change your\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain environment radically, you change your inner self. For this reason, we usually find that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Aquarius likes to meet new people. He is happy in public office or in public work, because he\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is always contacting new faces and personalities. He is changing himself. Large corporations\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain have caught onto this principle, and they keep shifting their men from one part of the country\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to another.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Cancer and Capricorn do not force change because, to them, it suggests insecurity. It is not\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the true nature of either Leo or Aquarius to resist change. There is a lack of fear of the result.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain If the Aquarian is discharged from his job, he is likely to react with a feeling of relief and a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain sense of freedom. Change is always an opportunity. Cancer or Capricorn might immediately\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain explore the possibilities of getting the job back again.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We often find the Aquarian unconsciously training himself for a job that doesn't exist. A few\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain years later, that kind of a job comes into existence, and he is ready for it. In some cases, we\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain find him training himself for a job that will not exist during his lifetime.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Just as any mathematical problem has to have an answer containing certain characteristics,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain there is often but one way in which the future can happen, for the future also has to have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain certain characteristics, and astrology will ALWAYS tell us the characteristics of the future.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Although the astrologer may err in his details of the future, there is never reason why he\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain should err in his calculations of the characteristics of the future. These are always plainly\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain written.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In Lesson Four we discussed TIME. To understand Aquarius and the Individual Reform\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Dynamic GUIDE, it is necessary to grasp a new conception of TIME. Time is elastic and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain relative. Dr. Carl Jung has asserted that time has quality and that whatever is born at a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain particular moment has the characteristics of that moment. Of itself, TIME is non-existent. It is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain but a way of describing a relationship among things. As conventionally used, time is merely a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain planetary relationship, the relationship of the earth to the sun. An instant of time is a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain planetary relationship. A planetary relationship is a mathematical DESIGN and that design is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain what we call the horoscope.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain I might refer to the moment of time when a certain plane will land at an airport in New York.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The plane finally lands, but due to a storm, the time does not coincide with the anticipated\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain planetary time. The time is nevertheless just as real as any planetary moment. It is still the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain time when that plane lands in New York. If suddenly, the earth were to stop turning on its\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain axis, and remain with one side facing the Sun, tomorrow's noon would never arrive. On the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Moon, noons are about 28 of our days apart.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Time is adjustable. Our inventors have changed the time it takes to cross the continent in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain relation to planetary time. Verne and Wells had the ability to grasp the DESIGN of the future.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There are people completely unable to visualize the future. As an example, during the 90's,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the astronomical department of Harvard College published a "scientific" paper "proving\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain conclusively" that it is physically impossible for a gasoline- driven mechanical device to fly\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain through the air and carry the weight of a motor, fuel and one man.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The Survival Dynamic Reactors often outweigh the Reform Dynamic Guides. At such times,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain progress is difficult. We are living in an era when the Reform factors outweigh the Survival\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain factors, insofar as the horoscopes of the people of the age where they can affect our destiny\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain are concerned. When the reverse is the case, time tends to stand still. People attempt to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain maintain order, but this is never more than partially and temporarily possible. Yet, in the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain design of the abstract world, there is perfect order, and there is neither time nor change. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain number 2311 is prime. It always was and always will be. It can never change into a composite\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain number It is the inherent nature of matter and life that it changes The only true security lies in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the abstract, where there is no change. The Christian world visualizes a "time" when there will\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain be no "time," when the struggle will end. This is their heaven. It is eternal. Only in the abstract\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain world, where everything is eternal, is this possible, but there are always materialists to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain interpret such things in a material frame of reference.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In the material world there is constant change that is not constant. It speeds up and slows\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain down if we use the rotations of the earth (days) as a constant. Even the speed of a planet is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not constant. It is more rapid in one part of its orbit than in another part. If we were to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain employ the speed of the earth or another planet as a constant, days would not be equal but\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain would vary in length. So-called "time" is always dependent upon a frame of reference. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain speed of light is determined only by employing the Sun as a frame of reference, which the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Sun itself is moving at the rate of 150 miles per second.\par
