\pard\f1\fs20\plain Design in the Solar SystemIt has already been emphasized that the greatest mathematical and astronomical discoveries\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain were made by men who were seeking cosmic design. It is quite apparent that the ancients\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain knew about, or were seeking a design in the solar system (If they were seeking it). We do not\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain know whether they found it, We do know that the design was there. It is possible that they\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain may have known about it and concealed the truth in the same manner that we tried to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain conceal the truth about atoms. We fear that information about atoms in the wrong hands may\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain destroy the earth. It would appear that the ancients may have had some similar fears. There\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain was some belief that knowledge was for the chosen few. Although there is no indication that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Pythagoras held such views, his followers did, and Pythagorean schools were secret schools.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Those taught were sworn to secrecy. The Pythagoreans were mighty serious about this, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain violations were subject to the death penalty. In the fourth century, B.C., Hippasus, a member\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of one of the Pythagorean societies, made a public announcement that he had discovered a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain solid with 12 faces (12 again). Because he offered this information to the public, the death\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain penalty was immediately imposed. He was drowned in his bath for giving away mathematical\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain truths. (In our own day the Rosenbergs were executed for a similar offense.) Insofar as can be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain determined, such a 12-face solid (with 5-sided surfaces) was unknown to Pythagoras himself,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain unless he, too, was holding out.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Since we must consider all possibilities, we must also consider more ancient ancients than\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain those we know anything about may have that known far more than the particular ancients we\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain do know something about. Knowledge may have become lost, just as a lot of people today\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain are wishing the secrets of the atom could get lost.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain However, we do have the fact that the ancients saw a significance in numbers or integers that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain modern mathematicians have ignored as mystic. The numbers 7 and 12 were very important\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to them. Later in these less6ns, we will show how, in astrological geometry, 7 becomes 12.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Let us quote a paragraph from Hogbens popular, Mathematics for the Million. "When we\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain amuse ourselves at the expense of these early societies struggling to lisp the language of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain number in the childhood of civilization, it behooves us to ask whether we ourselves have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain completely grown out of magic. Caution is all the more pertinent when were call the queer\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain theosophical preoccupation's of Pascal and Newton, who contributed so much to the sort of'\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematics which is most useful in solving problems of measurement in the age of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain machinery. For European civilizations the numbers in which magical properties reside are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain more particularly seven and three. Theology bequeathed to us the seven golden candlesticks\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the seven evil spirits cast out of Magdalen, the seven sorrows, the seven deadly sins, the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain seven (deadlier) virtues and the sevenfold amen. The number seven has not been neglected\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain by the unofficial theologians, more usually referred to as philosophers. In the year that Piazzi\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain discovered Ceres (an asteroid), seven planets were known: namely, Mercury, Venus, Earth,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus. In the same year the Prussian philosopher Hegel wrote\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain upbraiding scientists for the neglect of philosophy. He illustrated his disapproval of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain amount of time astronomers wasted in looking for a new planet when philosophy clearly\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain established the only possible number as seven. Since then other planets have been\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain discovered. Neptune followed shortly after (l876). Pluto was discovered in 1930, because\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain stronomers are materialists so long as they remain in their observatories."\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Actually, in seeking more planets, astronomers were keeping an open mind, which is very\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain helpful to science but very rare for astronomers. Hogben himself discloses that he is locked\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain within a frame of reference brought about by the mental limitation he imposes on himself\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain when he defines mathematics as a mere science of measurement. What we wish to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain emphasize is the religious and philosophical determination to keep alive the significance of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the integers 7 and 12. Without this determination, astrology would have died out completely,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain because the division of a circle into twelve equal parts is our most basic key. Had it been\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain divided into 11 or 13 equal parts, everything would have been lost. We agree with Hogben\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that astronomers are usually materialists, but mathematics is not materialism. It is completely\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain a study of abstractions, and because Hogben limited himself to a conception of mathematics\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain as it might be applied to material things, his frame of reference did not permit him to view\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain more than a very small part of the whole. Some of the greatest facts of all had to be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain excluded. Modern science works within a relatively narrow frame of reference which makes it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain necessary to constantly exclude a very large ratio of the facts. If the scientist loves his wife,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and her affections are stolen by another man, he encounters what was left out of his\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain textbook. He encounters emotion. We will find it hard to convince himself that his emotion is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain less real than the materials he has been measuring, but none of his formulae will help him\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain when it comes to measuring his emotions, much less controlling them. Theologians,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain philosophers and astrologers have made errors, but that would appear to identify them with\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain so-called "scientists." We will show later in these lessons there was a definite reason for\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain keeping. alive the significance of 7 and 12, and we will show how these two numbers relate\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to each other.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain First, let us get a picture of the solar system. We have the Sun as the center, surrounded by\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain circles of various sizes called orbits. Although these are not really circles but ellipses, they are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not too eccentric and they are almost circles. These imaginary ellipses are the paths over\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain which the planets travel. It should be realized that they do not lie in the same plane of space.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The orbit of Pluto is inclined to that of the earth by 17 degrees, that of Mercury by 7 degrees.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The others are closer. The orbit of Pluto has the greatest eccentricity, that of Venus the least.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In the following diagram, our relative distance between orbits is highly inaccurate, because\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain we are only concerned with the order of the orbits.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We want to call your attention to the order of these planetary orbits. This is one thing you\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain will want to learn, if you do not already know it. Starting at the center and going out into\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain space it runs: Sun, Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, Neptune, Pluto, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain whatever may exist beyond Pluto. Between the orbits of Mars and Jupiter, there are hundreds\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of little objects called asteroids or planetoids which also revolve around the Sun, but we\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain know of no astrological significance they may have. The biggest would make only a good\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain sized mountain on the earth. We will ignore them because we know nothing of any\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain consequence about them. You don't have to ignore them, but we will for now.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The ancients made an association between the planets and the signs of the zodiac. They\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain called the planets The rulers of the zodiacal signs. We do not know for certain how that word\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ruler crept in here, but let us point out that the word has a double meaning. A ruler may be a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain king who rules over a land, or it may be something with which you measure. If we employ the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain second meaning of the word it takes on an interesting significance in astrology.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Each zodiacal sign had a ruling planet. There is another object nearby that we did not\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mention. It is the Moon. The ancients employed the Moon as one of these rulers. Insofar as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain we know, the ancients knew nothing about planets beyond Saturn. Any planet beyond Saturn\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is invisible to the naked eye. If you are on the earth, that leaves SEVEN visible bodies: Moon,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Sun, Mercury, Venus, Mars, Jupiter and Saturn. If you were on the Moon, there would still be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain seven visible bodies, because you would view the earth instead of the Moon. The ancients\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain had a definite way of assigning these seven bodies to 12 zodiacal signs. The Moon was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain assigned to Cancer, the Sun to Leo, Mercury to both Virgo and Gemini, Venus to both Libra\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and Taurus, Mars to both Scorpio and Aries, Jupiter to both Sagittarius and Pisces, Saturn to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain both Capricorn and Aquarius. In this way, they had seven bodies ruling twelve signs. There is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain an odd factor here which, to our knowledge, had never been noted by modern astrologers at\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the time when the writer began in- vestigating astrology. Although he spotted it in 1933, he\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain originally called attention to it in 1938 in a book entitled, A New Experiment In Astrology.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The book was more or less ignored by the majority of astrologers, and reviews pictured it as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain claiming almost everything on earth except what it did claim. To this day, the content of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain book has not been grasped. If it had been, much of astrology as it exists would be different.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Elbert Benjamine, founder of a theological school of astrology, made alleged quotations from\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the book, and when he was asked to explain where he had found the various statements\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain quoted, he admitted that he couldn't find them anywhere in the book. At the time when he\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain made the quotations he had never read the book.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain This is the incomplete design left to us by the ancients, and for thousands of years nobody\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain noticed that the rest of the design could be filled in, could be completed, when the key was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain realized. The key is mean distance from the earth. The numbers indicate the order tin which\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain each planet appears when mean distance of the various bodies from the earth is considered.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It is known that the ancient mathematicians prepared magic squares where several numbers\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain were purposely omitted. One person who was seeking design would immediately understand\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and could detect the missing factors. The above diagram carries the subtle suggestion that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ancients far back may have known more about the solar system than astronomers know\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain today. The diagram suggests the existencse of two undiscovered planets beyond the orbit of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Pluto. Because people did not thin in terms of cosmic design, the significance of the above\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain diagram remained secret for thousands of years.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain If you will look at the above diagram, you will note that beginning in Cancer and running\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain counterclockwise to Capricorn, the ancients assigned the planets IN EXACT ACCORDANCE\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain with the bodies' mean distance from the earth. Because the Moon is nearest, we have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain assigned it the number I, the Sun-2, Mercury-3, Venus-4, Mars-5, etc. Mercury, Venus and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Mars can be nearer to the earth than the Sun, but when we consider the average distance,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the Sun is closer.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain If we start in Gemini and go around the circle clockwise to Aquarius, we find the same kind of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain sequence The order coincides with mean distance from the earth. This gives us an interesting\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain problem in mathematical probability. We have part of an arithmetical pattern here. What is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the probability that these planets were arranged in this fashion by chance?\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There are 5040 ways in which the planets could have been arranged in those signs from\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Cancer to Capricorn, but only two of those would have coincided with the factor of mean\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain distance. (The other way would be to start in Capricorn and finish in Cancer, going clockwise.)\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Cutting 5040 in half, this makes the odds 2519 to 1 against this arrangement being due to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain chance.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Considering the five remaining spaces, what are the odds against those also being assigned\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in accord with mean distance? There are 120 ways in which 5 planets could have been\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain arranged in 5 spaces, only 2 of which would have conformed to the pattern, making the odds\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 59 to I. When we consider the odds against the second arrangement applying after the first\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain arrangement had already applied, the odds are (2520 x 60)-l to 1, or 151,199 to 1.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Here is one of the most extraordinary facts of astrology that has been overlooked and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ignored for the last 2500 years. An astronomer can ignore a fact of this kind, but a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematician cannot. However, this is but a tiny part of the coincidence. Even greater odds\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain are involved. The symmetry, the mathematical design, does not stop here. It continues. You\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain will note that by putting Mars in both Scorpio and Aries, the ancients were associating what\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain we have described as the FAMILY SURVIVAL DYNAMIC with the FAMILY REFORM\par
\pard\f0\fs22\b DYNAMIC.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain
\pard\f1\fs20\plain By associating Jupiter with both Pisces and Sagittarius, they were associating the SOCIAL\par
\pard\f0\fs22\b SURVIVAL DYNAMIC with the SOCIAL REFORM DYNAMIC\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain
\pard\f1\fs20\plain By placing Saturn in both Capricorn and Aquarius, they associated the INDIVIDUAL\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain SURVIVAL DYNAMIC REACTOR with the INDIVIDUAL REFORM DYNAMIC GUIDE.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain By placing Mercury in both Virgo and Gemini, they associated the SOCIAL SURVIVAL\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain DYNAMIC REACTOR with the SOCIAL REFORM DYNAMIC GUIDE.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain They neglected to put the Sun or Moon in both Cancer and Leo, which was the only\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain necessary step left to complete this particular symmetry. Then they would have associated\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the INDIVIDUAL SURVIVAL DYNAMIC with the INDIVIDUAL REFORM DYNAMIC. We have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not reached the end of the design.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain When Uranus was discovered, the materialists accepted the event with great glee. This, the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astronomers told us, disproved astrology. Instead of seven Solar Bodies, there were eight.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The magic qualities of 7 were disproved, or so they thought. There was a bit of confusion in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the world of astrology also. This did not appear to upset things, but unlike the astronomers\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain who are supposed to make so many millions of observations but yet fail to observe, the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrologers began making observations, and in time, they came up with a conclusion. It had\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain been a mistake to put Saturn in Aquarius. It belonged to Capricorn. Uranus was the ruler of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Aquarius. Strange as it may seem. all astrologers soon agreed on this. In studying Uranus,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain they found the same qualities that they found in studying Aquarius. Still unconscious of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain factor of mean distance, they had placed an 8 in Aquarius and thus continued the sequence.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain This increased the odds against the first part of the pattern being due to chance to 20,159 to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 1.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In time, Neptune was discovered, and after some years of observations, the astrologers\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain agreed that Neptune and not Jupiter belonged in Pisces. Still unconscious of the factor of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mean distance, they had again continued the sequence and had placed 9 in Pisces, and this\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain time they increased the odds to 181,339 to 1.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In 1930, Pluto was discovered. This time, there was some disagreement. Some astrologers\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain placed Pluto in Scorpio, others in Aries. Placing it in Aries conformed to the pattern again,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and drove the odds to 1,814,399 to 1. Oddly, placing it in Scorpio also conformed from the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain other point of view. When you count the other way, 10 falls in Scorpio.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Even more strange is the fact that the astrologers who identified Pluto with Scorpio were an\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain occult group and their conclusions came out of study of Greek mytho1ogy. Even these\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain methods brought about an unconscious conformance with the arithmetical pattern that was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain piecing itself together.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The writer first observed that this connection between planets and zodiacal signs conformed\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to the mean distance in late September 1933, and from that time on assigned Pluto to Aries.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The student may later find it of interest to note that Jupiter, Mercury and Sun were in Libra at\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that time, the sign that we identify with an understanding of mathematics More interesting\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain might be the fact that the whole idea just popped into the writer's head while in bed, dozing\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain off to sleep. He suddenly saw the pattern of the whole, and forced himself out of bed to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain write it down, in fear that he might not remember it the following morning.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The pattern is not yet complete, but only two pieces are missing from the jigsaw puzzle, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain we know what they are like and where they belong. To complete the pattern, there we must\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain be two more planets outside the orbit of Pluto, and the first must be assigned to Taurus, the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain last to Gemini.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The zodiac is an abstract mathematical pattern. It is divided into l2 equal parts. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain association of planets with abstract signs of the zodiac implies there are 12 objects other\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain than the earth in the solar system when the Noon is counted. On another planet, our Moon\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain would have no significance, and the number of signs of the zodiac for another planet like\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Jupiter which has its own 12 (at least) moons, could vary, just as the number of electrons in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain atoms of different metals vary. Thus life on another planet could be expected to be quite\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain different from life on earth.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain For the benefit of the mathematically minded, we would like to explain the computation of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain odds referred to above. The astrologers have unconsciously fitted ten planets into ten spaces\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in one of only two ways that would conform to the mean distance of the bodies from the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain earth. The number of ways that ten numbers can be arranged in ten spaces will be 10! or\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain factorial 10, which means (10 X 9 X 8 x 7 X 6 x 5 x 4 x 3 X 2 X 1).\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain You can multiply these out if you choose. The answer is 3,628,800. Since two of these ways\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain would conform to the pattern, one counting Clockwise, the other counterclockwise the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain chances are 2 in 3,628,800 or 1 chance in 1,814,400. This gives odds of 1,814,399 to 1\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain against this pattern having been an accident. With the discovery of two more planets the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain pattern will be complete. However, we are already close enough to visualize the complete\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain design, and that means close enough to give the astrological characteristics of the two\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain missing planets. The first planet beyond Pluto must have the same characteristics as. Taurus,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain while the last planet Out must have the same characteristics as Gemini.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Just as there are seven visible bodies in the solar system, as viewed by Man on the earth,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain there are seven white keys in an octave on a piano. Just as there are five black keys in the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain octave, there would appear to be five planets invisible to Man's naked eye. This does not\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mean that the planets cause the keys on the piano or that the keys on the piano cause the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain planets. It merely illustrates an a causal relationship in the coincidence, the same\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematical design.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We offer another diagram above showing the planets and their numbers going around the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain circle both ways, starting from Leo and going clockwise, starting from Cancer and going\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain counterclockwise. This is a perfectly symmetrical pattern. It is a mathematical design. In all of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain their associations of planets with zodiacal signs, the astrologers of all known times have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain unconsciously conformed to this design. We have added two theoretical planets and have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain called them "Y" and "Z".\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Now let us look at the above diagram . Here we have merely drawn lines to connect the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain numbers in the clockwise, count with the numbers in the counterclockwise count. We get an\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain interesting design. It is a design that closely resembles that of a magnetic field. That does not\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mean that it IS a magnetic field any more than the solar system is a piano. If you study this\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain design, you will find that a SURVIVAL DYNAMIC is always connected with a corresponding\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain REFORM DYNAMIC, and a SURVIVAL REACTOR is always connected with a corresponding\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain REFORM GUIDE. An INDIVIDUAL factor is connected with an INDIVIDUAL factor. A FAMILY\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain factor is connected with a FAMILY factor. There are no exceptions to the rule. The pattern is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain complete symmetry. There are no missing pieces. The jigsaw puzzle has been put together.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain As you grow more familiar with the pattern, it will become simplicity itself. It is nothing but an\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain abstract mathematical figure, but the only such figure that has ever caused us to find a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain connection between distance from a center and divisions of a circle into twelve equal parts.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain These two factors appear to involve a factor of coincidence, but it may be only the a causal\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain coincidence that we find connecting a piano and the solar system. We can employ white keys\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to represent visible planets, the black keys to represent invisible planets. As you will later see,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain both counts, the clockwise and the counterclockwise, have a very definite significance, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain each is to be employed under different circumstances.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We will not need to devote much space to an explanation of what the planets mean, for the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain simple reason that they mean the same thing that is meant by .the signs of the zodiac The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain same twelve basic principles expressed in the zodiacal signs are expressed in the planets.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Just as you have lined a basic principle with a particular zodiacal sign, you will now link the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain same principle with a planet. The following table will show the manner in which this applies.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The numbers at the right side of the page are the same numbers that appear in our diagrams.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The first column of figures represents mean distance from the earth insofar as the named\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain planet is concerned. The figures in the second column represent the count the other way\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain around the zodiacal circle. In this way, 1 is joined with 2, 3 with 12, 4 with 11, 5 with 10, 6\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain with 9, and 7 with 8. It will be necessary to retain both of these counts as we will later see.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Each has a significance. If you omit one and substitute 13 (for the 1 would become 13 if you\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain continue counting), the two integers joined each time will always total 15.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We have shown that there is only 1 chance in 1,814,400 of the counterclockwise count of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain planets in the zodiacal signs being due to chance. We have also shown that there was 1\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain chance in 60 of the as astrologers hitting the target five consecutive times relative to the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain clockwise. count, but the target was hit again when the occult group associated Pluto with\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Scorpio. There are 720 ways in which 6 planets can be arranged in 6 spaces (6 x S X 4 X 3 X 2\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain X 1), only 2 of which would conform to the mean distance, meaning that there is 1 chance in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 360 that these selections were due to chance alone.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Now, to determine the probability that the entire mathematical pattern was a matter of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain chance, we can say there is one chance in 360 x 1,814,400 or 1 chance in 653,184,000. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematical odds against the possibility that the astrologers were deceiving themselves are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 653,183,000 to 1. In\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Lesson Four, we presented a diagram identifying time with the signs of the zodiac. This was a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain pattern. Patterns are not due to chance. They involve abstract laws. They are called natural\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain laws because we find them in nature, but what we find in nature is not the mold. The mold is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the abstract law itself. In nature, we find only what has been formed by the mold. However,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain by making the identification of planets with signs of the zodiac as we have done in this\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Lesson, we encounter a new association, because we can now associate time with the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain planets in the same manner as we have done with the zodiacal signs Certain solar bodies are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain related to the perpetuation of forms of the past, while other bodies are to be identified with\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain destroying the form of the past that the pattern of the future may come into being. So, if we\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain arrange the solar bodies in the order of their mean distance from the earth and relate them\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to past and future, we will come up with the following table.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The symbols "Y" and "Z" represent two hypothetical planets out beyond the orbit of Pluto. We\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain have never seen these planets. Their existence is merely a matter of calculation. Neither have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain we seen an atom. Its existence is merely a matter of calculation. However, we have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain demonstrated that the probability of those planets being there is 653,183,999 to 1. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrological pattern is not complete until these two missing pieces of the jigsaw puzzle are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain added.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It is extremely diffIcult for the writer to visualize how the whole superstructure of astrology\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain could have been discovered by Man except in the same manner that the atom was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain discovered, by calculation. If the original knowledge came from the calculations of super-\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematicians, who were they? Surely, no one that history can tell us anything about. If\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain these super-mathematics knew from their own astrology that civilization was to go into a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain decline for thousands of years, it might account for much that was done. Why do we dig up\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the twelve symbols of the signs of the zodiac carved on stone throughout the world? The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain conception that the great pyramid was a tomb motivated by a king 5 vanity is childish when\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain we consider that it is a mathematical figure involving facts of astronomy. When we pat\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ourselves on the back while observing the great structures, buildings and dams we have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain constructed, we ignore the fact that no modern structure compares in cubic yards with the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain wall that surrounded the ancient city of Babylon. The ancients left behind them their\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain messages in the form of design and symbols which have remained uninterpreted for\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain thousands of years. After the tremendous amount of labor that was employed in carving the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Aztec Calendar Stone, what was done with it? It was hidden. It was buried in the ground\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain where it was not discovered until more than a century after Cortez entered Mexico City. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain diameter of the large circle is 12 feet. (Do not place significance on 12 here because the foot\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is an arbitrary measurement.) The stone is three feet thick, and its weight is over 20 tons In\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the center of the circle is the symbol of the Sun (not the earth). Around it are the symbols of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain FIRE, AIR, EARTH and WATER. Other markings represent such cycles as days, weeks and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain months in the Aztec calendar system. At the time it was found, it was a more perfect calendar\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain than any that had been designed by astronomers of the time. Interesting is the fact that after\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the stone was found by the Spaniards, it was hidden again by the church, in the fear that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain knowledge of the symbols and the story told by the stone might cause people to abandon\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the church. It was buried by the theologists for another 150 years.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain What Hogben describes as the cradle of civilization may actually have been the tomb of a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain former civilization. Of course there are legends about Atlantis and Lemuria, sunken\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain continents which supposedly held more advanced civilizations than ours. We are not\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain authorities on Atlantis and Leniuria, but speculations on the possible existence of such\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain civilizations are interesting, and even if these speculations contain a vast amount of false\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain information, they should be combed for any few threads of fact which may possibly exist.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain One such speculation contained the claim that the Lemurians colonized the east coast of Asia\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and the west coast of South America before the continent sank into the Pacific, and that after\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the disaster, those on the coast of Asia thereafter bowed to the east to the former\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain motherland in their religious cults. This conforms to the curious fact that the religious cults of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain South America bowed, not to the east, but to the west, in their religious ceremonies.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The ancients have been described as being superstitious by some of the moderns, but they\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain could have described our moderns as being superstitious. The nebular hypothesis and many\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain so-called scientific theories are actually superstitions. The astronomers are busy making\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain observations. They are busy counting the number of stars in the heavens, and they might as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain well count the grains of sand on the earth.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We associate the survival factors with stability, the non-survival factors with instability. Oddly,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the stability of an atom is said to have a relationship with whether the number of electrons is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain odd or even.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It will help your astrology if you begin early to think of astrology as a science of design rather\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain than a science of cause and effect. It is a science of design in the same way that mathematics\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is a science of design. Your personality and your character is a design. It is actually different\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in some respect from the design of another person. The design of the solar system at this\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain particular moment is also the design of whatever is born at this particular moment. In\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrology, you are always comparing the design of one moment with the design of another\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain moment Two moments of time can be harmonious or discordant to each other. In that respect\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain some days may appear harmonious or discordant for you. That which may appear discordant\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain may be more harmonious when you understand it. It is necessary for you to become familiar\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain with your own design.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Much of your own character is invisible to you. There are parts of your nature that may never\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain have had an opportunity of expressing themselves. Some hidden part of your nature may\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain suddenly be stirred tomorrow, because the design of tomorrow attunes to the design of your\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain birth. in a way that has not previously occurred. All astrological designs resemble dials, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain you can think of the dials on your radio or television sets. A slight twist of the dial may tune\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain out Kansas City and tune in Chicago. The astrological dial is more complicated. It is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain constantly turning. It is ever tuning things in and tuning other things out. That is why your\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain interests shift from year to year, from day to day, from minute to minute. We are always\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain comparing designs, one with another. The man who experiences a sudden sweep of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain popularity has merely run into design that allows his own personal design to express itself.\par
