\pard\qc\f0\fs26\b Lesson #13\par
\pard\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The Art of InterpretationThe application of any science becomes an art. This is true of mathematics, and the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematician can make mistakes. The mathematical machine or "brain." may not be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain regarded as practicing an art, but the machine is a product of Man, and it can do only what\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Man has provided for it to do. It has no originality, and it is in no sense a brain. It can do\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain nothing its inventor could not do if he wanted to make the effort and had enough time, but\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain inventors are often lazy, and that is why they invent. There is an important difference\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain between the electronic calculator and Man. The machine has no intuition. It is fairly common\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain for modern teachers of science to praise the discoveries of such men as Pythagoras,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Copernicus, Kepler and Newton and simultaneously condemn the methods by which those\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain discoveries were made. Man can reach out and explore abstract realms, while the machine\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain can do this only to the extent that Man has provided. For the machine, there is a god, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that god is Man. The machine is limited to the pattern that its creator provided.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Theological writers have often pictured Man as half god and half animal. From an astrological\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain viewpoint, that part of Man that is represented by the Water and Earth signs is the animal,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain while that part represented by the Fire and Air signs is the god. The machine operates\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain automatically. That part of Man that operates automatically is the animal. That part that does\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not operate automatically is the god. It would appear that the ancients saw more god in the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Air signs than in the Fire signs, for you will note that in no instance is an Air sign represented\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain by an animal. Man always represents God as similar to Man. He always creates God in his own\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain image.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Before leaving Lessons Ten to Twelve, the student should make certain that he knows the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain technical factors of erecting charts of the heavens. Practice and checking is going to bring\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain perfection. If you have other students around you, you should check each other. Whenever\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain you have doubts, you should write to us and let us do the checking.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There is one simple rule that will help you. If you have a chart drawn for 6:00 A.M., the Sun\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain must be on the east side of that chart. If you have a chart drawn for noon, the Sun must be in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the upper part of that chart. If you have a chart drawn for 6:00 P.M., the Sun must be on the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain west side of the chart. If you have a chart drawn for midnight, the Sun must be in the lower\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain part of the chart.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The most common error is to draw a chart that is exactly twelve hours out of the way.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Students often get A.M. and P.M. mixed up, or they use the Sidereal Time for noon as the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Sidereal Time at midnight, or vice versa. When you look at such a chart, this error is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain immediately apparent, because the Sun will be in the opposite place from where it should be.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain If you draw a chart for noon, do not expect the Sun to be exactly at the cusp of the 10th\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain House, because in the kind of a chart we are employing, you are not looking at the chart from\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain your birth place, but from a point at right angles to the earth's orbit. You are looking south\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain from a celestial point of view, and not from an earthly point of view. You may be looking\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain more to the southeast in the morning, more to the southwest in the afternoon, or vice versa,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain depending on the seasons from an earthly viewpoint.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain As we go into the second half of this Course, we are going to deal with interpretation, which,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain although it is an art, can be based on certain well defined and systematic principles. We\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain receive a good many letters from students who tell us that they can erect charts, and they ask\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain whether they can begin the second half of the Course and skip the first half. We turn down all\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of these request. Some of you who have been through the first twelve lessons will know why.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain These students have usually learned too many things that are not so, and for us to grant their\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain request would mean a continuation of errors and the mental confusion that would have to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain result.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There are some students to whom interpretation comes easily, others for whom there are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain obstacles, but the student who overcomes his obstacles may be the best astrologer in the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain end.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We do not like to interfere with a student's natural abilities of interpretation. When you reach\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain correct conclusions by your own original methods, we are not going to interfere. If this seems\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain logical and apparent, one should note that astronomical and mathematical writers constantly\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain condemn such men as Pythagoras, Kepler and Newton because they made their discoveries\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain by certain methods that proved successful, and the writers advocate methods that are often\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain unsuccessful. If you develop original methods that prove successful, we will never quarrel\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain with you about them. Instead we will try to learn from you.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It may be that these words should be directed more to the female of the species, because it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is a fact of our own experience, that many women develop the art of interpretation more\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain rapidly than do men. This becomes troublesome only when they cannot tell us by what\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain method they reached their correct conclusions. Actually, this sort of thing is often due to the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain fact that women observe many things that men do not, a strange motion of the hand, an odd\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain habit, etc. In our thirty years of experience with astrology, we have learned a great deal from\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain women who were untrained observers, but who habitually and automatically observed many\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain things that trained observers never see. The existence of this unorthodox power of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain observation often comes to the surface only after much in the way of painful questioning. A\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain woman detects something the rest of us have missed. She can't explain how she detected it,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain because she never thought about the matter. To her, it seemed natural. Although it can be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain called intuitional, it is unconsciously as systematic as any other kind of thinking. The world of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain science just hasn't taken the trouble to examine the System. An example may help to clarify\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the point.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Sitting in a restaurant and watching a stranger at another table, a lady suggested that he\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain must be born on May 19th. Startled by this assertion, the science editor of a New York paper\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain rose, walked to the stranger, apologized for the intrusion and asked the man for his birth\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain date. The man replied that it was May 19th.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The lady could not explain why she thought the stranger was born on May 19th but this was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain unsatisfactory to a science editor and others present. She was questioned at great length.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Finally she named off a number of other people born on May 19th and pointed out that they\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain all had a certain odd habit. She had noted that this stranger had the same odd habit. All this\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain careful observation and the resultant conclusion appeared to have been something that went\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain on in the girls unconscious realm, and until pressed by painful questioning she appeared\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain unconscious of her own methods.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We do not condemn such methods. We do strongly suggest determining what the methods\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain are and how they work, and this can be accomplished. After discovering that he had an ability\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to solve mathematical problems in his sleep and awaken with the answers, the writer could\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not rest until he discovered how this was done. He would try to remember further and further\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain back into dreams that preceded the solution, and he soon realized that in his sleep he had\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain been looking at an abstract design. Everything in mathematics is design, cosmic design, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain these designs can be seen in a waking state as well as in sleep. The difficulty lies in our\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain inability to eliminate the objective from the subjective during the waking state. The three\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mentioned mathematicians were so interested in the abstract world that they could blot out\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the objective world and see clearly into the abstract.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The schoolchild is told that Sir Isaac Newton discovered the law of gravitation when he saw\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain an apple fall from a tree. This is one of the tales of fairytale textbooks. Newton never claimed\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that gravitation was a property of matter. He described it as mathematical expression, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain when other scientists of the day began describing it as an inherent characteristic of matter,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain he wrote to Bentley, "You sometimes speak of gravity as essential and inherent to matter.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Pray do not ascribe that notion to me; for the cause of gravity is what I do not pretend to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain know, and therefore would take some time to consider of it."\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There are hints that Newton discovered gravitation, not as a property of matter but as a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain property of an abstract ellipse. The apple may have demonstrated what he already knew.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Newton did not perform experiments to get the answers He first calculated the answers and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain then performed the experiments to verify his conclusions.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain This discussion is brought forth because we want the student to be a free thinker and to learn\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain how to use the best that his own mind has to offer. When the student begins thinking in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain terms of authorities, he blocks his own best mental abilities. We will teach you our own\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain methods of interpretation, but we expect you to improve upon them wherever you can. Just\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain as a single symbol may tell a mathematician a story that might require pages of the figures,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain so a single planetary configuration can tell an astrologer a story which might fill a book. No\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain student will live long enough to digest everything that his own individual horoscope can tell\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain him. There will always be more, for it is one of those things that goes on to infinity. You will,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain then, realize that no other astrologer could have the time to interpret everything that your\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain own birth chart can tell you. You can be unfolding that for the rest of your life. It goes on and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain on, but the more charts of other people you study the more you will learn about yourself. This\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is the most important reason why we would prefer to teach you astrology instead of merely\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain writing pages about what your own individual horoscope means. It is not our desire to make\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain you dependent on us, but to make you independent and able to do your own thinking and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain your own interpreting.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Whatever natural abilities of interpretation you may have, use them to the full, but do not be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain content to use them without understanding them. Find out what you are doing and how you\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain are doing it. If the work is being done down (or up) in the unconscious, find out how. Then\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain you can call forth the ability at will without being dependent on its working on one day and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not on another, although you will always have some days that are better than others.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Any planet in any sign of the zodiac has a specific meaning. Every person with a specified\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain planet in a particular sign of the zodiac will have a certain basic characteristic. A hundred\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain people born with that planet in that sign of the zodiac will have the same characteristic, but it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain will be altered, adjusted and sometimes disguised by other factors in the horoscope. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain same will apply for a specific aspect between two planets, and it will apply for planets in the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrological houses. In introducing the art of interpretation, we will begin with three specific\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain categories of information.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 1--Planets in the signs of the zodiac\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 2--Aspects between the planets\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 3--Planets in the astrological houses\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There are many other factors to be interpreted. This is the starting point. There are many\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain other divisions and mathematical points to be considered. Let us simplify things by not trying\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to take in too much territory at one time. You can broaden your frame of reference as you go\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain along.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It will be a great help if you become systematic, if you organize your knowledge as you go\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain along, and in that connection we suggest some notebooks. Suppose you take one notebook\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and have a page for every planet in every zodiacal sign. For Moon, Sun, Mercury, Venus,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Mars, Jupiter, Saturn and perhaps Uranus. You will need twelve pages for each planet.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Depending on your age, you may not have known people born with Uranus in all of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain zodiacal signs, but you will ultimately. This will mean that you will need 96 pages to cover the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain above planets. The writer has known people born with Neptune in all the zodiacal signs from\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Aquarius around counterclockwise to Scorpio. That is ten signs. He never knew anyone born\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain with Neptune in Sagittarius or Capricorn. We can meet such people when we study history,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain however, and it would be well to have a page for Neptune in all twelve signs, and the same\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain with Pluto.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Characteristics of these slow moving planets in a particular sign have to do with all of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain people born during a certain period of years. One generation thinks differently from the next\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain generation, and consequently these qualities are not as apparent because we see nothing\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain unusual in a generation of people all of whom have certain characteristics that exactly match\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain our own. This seems natural until you have given the matter a great deal of study. The empire\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain builders born during the time when Neptune was in Aries saw nothing odd about themselves\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain but they considered their children mighty peculiar. We never understand why our children\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain think differently than we do. We are always wondering what is wrong with the new\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain generation instead of wondering what is wrong with ourselves. You will probably reach a time\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain when you will see it in a new light. It will become a hundred times more interesting to you.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain As this is written, Neptune is just beginning its transit of Scorpio, and if we want to know\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain what Neptune in Scorpio means, we may want to go back and study what was going on the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain last time it was there --165 years ago. Scorpio represents the Family Survival Dynamic. It is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the sign of sex, while Neptune represents the Social Survival Dynamic. The Social Survival\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Dynamic comes under the domination of the Family Survival Dynamic or sex. What happened\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the last time it was there? Joseph Smith and Brigham Young were born. They gave birth to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Mormonism and a plurality of wives. The Mormon Church was organized on April 6th, 1830,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain with Mars (ruler of Scorpio) conjunct Neptune (ruler of Pisces) in the sign of Capricorn (the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain legal sign). On June 27th, 1844, with Jupiter, Uranus and Pluto in the pioneering sign of Aries,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the Mormons were driven from Illinois by mob violence. In 1847 they established themselves\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in Utah. Polygamous Mormonism is still practiced in some parts of the west where official\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain sources close their eyes to it, and it will be interesting to observe what the re-entry of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Neptune in Scorpio will bring about for Mormonism. What will it do for matters pertaining to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain desegre- gation, where the old white South fears that desegregation will lead to greater\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mixing of the sexes between the two races?\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain This is merely an example of the kind of things that will ultimately interest you about history.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Very often, you will better understand history and the people of a particular era when you\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain see the pattern as described by the planetary conditions of the time. When you have a page\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain entitled Venus in Aquarius, each time you come upon a birth date showing Venus in Aquarius,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain you will write the persons name on that page. After a while, you will have quite a number.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain This will enable you to see what characteristics these people have in common which are not\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain common to other persons. You can test both theory and experience simultaneously. You will\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain need another notebook dealing with all the possible planetary aspects, such as Mars square\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Uranus, Mars Opposite Neptune, etc.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain When you encounter a new person with Mars square Uranus, you can immediately compare\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that person with all the other persons you have met having Mars square Uranus. It would be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain well to have all Mars-Uranus aspects on a group of pages together, because you will find\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain certain qualities in Mars-Uranus aspects whether they are so-called favorable or unfavorable\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain aspects. For example, you will find that all such aspects appear to be accompanied by\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mechanical ability but the so-called unfavorable aspects are more accident prone.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain You will need another notebook dealing with the planets in the various houses. A word or\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain caution in this connection, however, for you will want to be very careful about placing\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain information in this notebook unless you are positive that the birth time is correct. Otherwise\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain you are apt to have a notebook containing much in the way of faulty information, and this\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain would mislead you. It is better not to know than to think you know something that is wrong.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain First, you should get to understand what the planets in the various signs of the zodiac mean,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain because in most cases this information will be definite and not dependent on an exact\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain moment of birth except in those few cases where a planet is changing from one sign to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain another during the actual date of birth.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Finally, you will want to know what the transits mean. In astrology, the word transit has a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain different meaning than in astronomy. In astrology, the word transit means the relationship of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the planets on a particular date after birth to the planetary pattern on the date of birth. In\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astronomy, a transit merely means the passage of a celestial object across the disk of another\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain object, over the meridian of a place, or across the field of a telescope. Thus, in astrology, the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain word transit has a much broader meaning.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain From the moment of birth, all the planets as well as Sun and Moon are changing their relative\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain positions, and as this happens, different parts of what is represented by the horoscope have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain an opportunity of manifesting in different ways. A powerful Family Survival Dynamic can\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain manifest in many different ways during a lifetime. What is assumed to be love under one\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain planetary setup at one time may be hatred or indifference under another planetary setup.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain That explains with one swoop why people do not stay in love. The planets change their\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain positions, and the love that lasts longest is often one that is a subconscious expression of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain insecurity. The child may love the parents to the extent that the parents represent security.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There are other binding factors, but most of them do not require monogamy. These include\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain loyalty and platonic relationships. Platonic relationships do not involve insecurity, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain therefore, for some persons are non-existent. On the other hand, not all insecurity is in-\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain volved with monogamy Neither is insecurity always binding. An insecure woman may leave\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain her husband because she believes she can find greater security in another man.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Almost at a glance, to the experienced observer, the planets and their constantly changing\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain relationships explain why our thoughts, feelings and emotions are constantly in a state of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain flux.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In basic principle, the notations of the astrologer are akin to those of the mathematician.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain When the astrologer writes (the glyphs), he means Venus-in-Pisces, but he also means a long\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain group of characteristics and possibilities as well as a certain potential. He means that the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Family Reform Dynamic Guide is under the domination of the Social Survival Dynamic.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain A person born at such a time will have strange social urges. He is attracted to unusual types\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of people due to a deep sympathetic urge that carries him in a certain direction. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain injustices of society are more apparent to him. He is likely to be attracted to those who are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ostracized from orthodox society, those for whom orthodox society has prepared no place,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain those who have been overlooked. He is compassionate. He does not take the rules of society\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain seriously, for he sees injustice in them. He doesn't really care whether something is proper or\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not, because proper doesn't make it right. He may have a special interest in the criminal, the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain sick person, anyone who is operating out side the correct ions of organized society, the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain "crackpot," the pauper or the beggar. He may show more respect for the prostitute than for\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the ladies who live on Snob Hill. There is something about her that interests him. What made\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain her what she is? (A limited number of birth dates of prostitutes on hand shows them also\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain having Venus in Pisces more often than in any other sign). He feels both sorry for her and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain sentimental about her. We may find him having many secret friends. In the presence of these\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain "unfortunate" people, he relaxes. He can say what he thinks with no fear of criticism. He\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain knows he will be understood. There is no need for being a hypocrite. He is quite apt to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain regard drinking as a form of relaxation, and we are apt to find him in the association of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain people who drink a good deal. It is all an escape from the artificiality of organized society\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain which is always a strain. He has a broader conception of things, because he is not limited in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain his thinking by any accepted frame of reference, for a frame of reference itself is a mental\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain limitation, sometimes useful but often a means of justifying faulty conclusions.Because Venus\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain represents the Family Reform Dynamic Guide, all of this is designed to inject a new strain into\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the hereditary factors of the future. The thinking and the reasoning is on the unconscious\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain level, but it comes to the surface in the form of sentiment, and it is the sentiment that is acted\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain upon, although it is the unconscious purpose that is being served. The family must not survive\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in its old form. The form must be changed. There is the urge to marry a person from some\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain other realm. This might mean a foreigner, one of another race, or one from some entirely\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain different level of society. Nature is at work to produce the mongrel. The mongrel will be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain frowned upon by the old family strain, but experience has taught us that mongrels often have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain superior intellectuality, are more brilliant. Most Americans are mongrels. As in mathematics,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain when you put strange combinations together, it may be difficult to predict the result. We are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain dealing with the chemistry of characteristics.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain This is merely an example of what one little symbol like can mean. Each planet in each sign of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the zodiac has such a meaning of its own. You are going to learn them, and the more you\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain learn them by yourself by experience, the better it will be. This is the type of knowledge you\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain shouldn't memorize. Let the pieces fit together and crystallize in your mind as you go along.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In explaining the principles represented by the planets and signs of the zodiac in earlier\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain lessons, we have supplied you with the tools.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Always remember one thing. THAT REPRESENTED BY THE PLANET IS DOMINATED BY\par
\pard\f0\fs22\b THAT REPRESENTED BY THE ZODIACAL SIGN THAT IT OCCUPIES.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain
\pard\f1\fs20\plain When you work with astrological symbols, you are approximating what the mathematician\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain does when he works with algebraic symbols. The mathematician may say that x equals y,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain while the astrologer practically says that Venus in Pisces equals Neptune in the 11th House.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Here are two different astrological expressions that have the same meaning.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Then people having Venus in Pisces will not all be alike. One may have Mars in Taurus while\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the other has Mars in Scorpio. This brings in a variation. Yet, certain basic characteristics are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain present in each case. The person having Mars in Scorpio will express them with less caution\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain than the person having Mars in Taurus.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We have shown you what it means when Venus is in Pisces. What does it mean when Venus is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in Capricorn? We could write out an interpretation and ask you to memorize it. That would\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not make you a good astrologer. Instead, we are going to ask you what it means when Venus\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is in Capricorn. We want you to write out an interpretation of a person having Venus in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Capricorn, and we want you to mail it to us. Understand one thing. We do not care how\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain wrong you may be. If you prove to be close to 100% correct, well and good, but it is the error\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of your interpretation that will tell us what we have failed to make clear to you. Start out by\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain realizing that when Venus is in Capricorn, the Family Reform Guide is under the domination of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the Individual Survival Dynamic Reactor. Search the birth dates of your friends. You will not\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain have to erect any charts to determine whether they have Venus in Capricorn. The ephemeris\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain will tell you that, except in cases where the ephemeris shows Venus to be in the first or last\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain degree of a sign. In those cases, you would have to check the time of day the person was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain born to be certain.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Find as many persons having Venus in Capricorn as you can among people you know well.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Check yourself, and see whether your interpretation fits these people. Take as many liberties\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain as you wish in this respect. In other words, you will be writing up a theoretical interpretation\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain but you are privileged to check it against people you know to see whether it fits. This is a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain procedure you are going to be following from now on, so long as you deal with astrology.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain You are going to be working from a theoretical base that has not been previously supplied by\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain any other teacher of astrology, but it must always check with experience. You will be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain combining theory and experience. For a time, we would like you to forget everything else in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the horoscope and confine yourself to learning to interpret what each planet in each sign\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain means.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain This can keep you quite busy, because you can start some more notebooks. You can write out\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain your own theoretical interpretation of every planet in every sign. This will be a starting point.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain From this point on, you will constantly be adjusting your orginal interpretations. Your purpose\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain will be perfection of these interpretations. It is doubtful whether you will ever reach any\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain absolute perfection, but you will always be getting closer and closer.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It will be much as if you were adding a series of fractions such as 1/2, 1/4, 1/8, 1/16, 1/32,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 1/64, 1/128, etc. You will note that 1 always appears above the line in these fractions, while\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the numeral below the line is always double that below the line in the previous fsahion The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain more such fractions you add, the closer the sum will be to I, but it will never actually reach 1,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain except at infinity. We say that the sum of such fractions approaches 1 as a limit. No matter\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain how long you create and add more fractions, you can never reach or exceed 1.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In the same manner, although your goal is perfection, and although you constantly grow\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain closer and closer to that perfection, it is never actually reached. We do not ask absolute\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain perfection.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Again, let us quote Paul G. Clancy when he said that astrology is the algebra of life. All the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain symbols in a horoscope are employed in a similar manner to that in which we employ algebra.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain That doesn't mean that you need to know anything about algebra, but if you have studied\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain algebra it will help you to understand why we do not have to set up any causal hypothesis to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain explain astrology. Any causal hypothesis involves that man-made conception we call time.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain When we express the Pythagorean Theorem algebraically and say that (a2 + b2) - c2, we do\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not mean that a and b,, in any way, cause c, for all exist simultaneously. One does not come\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain before or after the other.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain When we consider a symbol such as (glyph for mars in Aquarius), we recognize a group of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain characteristics which in hemselves may be considered as causing certain results, but the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain results are dependent upon how well the individual understands his own characteristics and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain what he does to channel them to gain the results that he desires. Thus, the results can be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain quite different in the case of the individual who has studied and understands astrology than\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in the case of the person who blindly follows sentiment with no conception of what the origin\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of that sentiment may be nor where it may lead. You can see that where we deal with\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain horoscopes that contain factors of violence, the difference between the person who\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain understands his inner nature and the individual who does not is stupendous.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In many instances, the individual with no understanding of the nature the horoscope reveals\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain actually does face what we might call fate. The machinist in a machine shop may lose a hand\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain before he discovers that his periodic accidents are to be associated with his Mars-Uranus\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain opposition but also with his own irritability. His accidents are preceded by irritability, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain once he learns this he will think about it when he feels irritable, and it will remind him to be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain more careful. In his case, caution is required. In other cases, caution becomes an obstacle in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the way of success. Thus, we ultimately begin to draw a close parallel between the words\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain fate and ignorance. They go together. Where you have ignorance you have what has been\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain meant by fate. The greater your true knowledge of abstract principles, the greater your\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain freedom and the less your fate. The Christian church has tried to reverse this. It has been\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain assumed that knowledge is dangerous. This concept was prevalent among the members of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the Pythagorean school, although it does not appear to have been characteristic of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Pythagoras himself insofar as we can determine. Yet, it was this very conception that led to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the destruction of the Pythagorean school. There are some who suspect that Sir Isaac\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Newton may have detected the whole secret of the atom mathematically and that he\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain detected his solution from the work of Hermes, after which he was afraid to reveal the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain information to the world of science for fear of what scientists might do with it. At any rate, he\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain did not explode an atom bomb in order to confirm some of his view on alchemy. The man\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain whom some scientists describe as the greatest scientist of all believed in alchemy.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Mastery of astrology, like mastery of other subjects, helps you to overcome that man-made\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain conception we call time.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The writer lives on a ranch 19 miles from the heart of Tucson. Years back, the ranch was a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain stagecoach stop for traffic coming out of the mountains and headed west. It was an all day\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain trip over rocky desert roads from the ranch to Tucson. One late afternoon, the writer was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain relaxing while awaiting the arrival of a relative on a plane from New York. The passenger was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain making the trip from New York to Tucson, 2500 miles, in as little time as it formerly took the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain stagecoach to travel from the ranch to Tucson. Basically, what has made the difference is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain knowledge of mathematics and its working principles. We are left with the possibility that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain what can be accomplished in a millennium can be accomplished instantaneously when we\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain know more about mathematics and nature.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The student of astrology begins to learn of natural abilities that he did not know existed.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain When he knows about them he can use them. The possibilities that can be opened are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain practically unlimited.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain When you started in school, you were given a table of 26 symbols to memorize. They were\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the letters of the alphabet. Consider the number of words you can now form out of those 26\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain symbols. We furnished you with the letters of the astrological alphabet back in Lesson Three.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Now, you have reached a point where you can join two of these letters like \'df\'fd abbreviate the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain statement: THE FAMILY REFORM DYNAMIC IS DOMINATED BY THE SOCIAL SURVIVAL\par
\pard\f0\fs22\b DYNAMIC.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Utimately, you have the whole natal horoscope to consider. It is filled with symbols. You will\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain interpret them one by one, but you will be able to make an overall mathematical statement\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and say: THIS CHART IS JOHN. The accomplished and trained astrologer will often take one\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain look at a horoscope, more or less take in everything at one glance, and give a mathematical\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain expression to the whole which might be uttered in one word as WOW!\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In time, you will meet some stranger, and in talking with him, you will recognize certain traits\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and characteristics that you will be able to place and define astrologically. You will note a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain specific characteristic that belongs to Pisces or Neptune, and before you ever ask for a birth\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain date, you will have pegged and classified that characteristic. You will know that a certain\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain dynamic is over-expressed. You may know that something has to be in Pisces or that Neptune\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is strongly placed, but you will have more difficulty in determining what planet may be in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Pisces or in what way Neptune may be emphasized. However, the moment you look at the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain chart, you will see what you are looking for with one glance, and when you do so, you will\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain possess far more information than could possibly be obtained by observation. If you are a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain psychiatrist or a psychologist, you may, at one stroke, have more information than you could\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain obtain by days of probing and analysis.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Observation of these characteristics is where the female of the species so often rates at the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain top. But we beg of her to learn and understand more about her own intuitional powers of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain observation. We often call such unconscious powers of observation being psychic. It is our\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain view that these powers merely involve a process of unconscious calculation. The more you\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain learn about these unconscious functions, the more able you will become to control those\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain functions at will.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain You should be able to detect what we are attempting to do. We are trying to teach you our\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain own established methods of interpretation without allowing them to block the functioning of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain your own natural powers of interpretation. We are trying to teach you an organized system of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain interpretation, but we do not want to risk allowing that factor of organization to become a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mental block. We want you to think for yourself.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We want to supply you with the tools, but we want you to realize that you may ultimately\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain develop better tools of your own. It is not our purpose to make you as good as we are. We\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain want you to be better. We have often stated that mathematics is simple but Man has made it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain complicated. That is the case when people are afraid of mathematics. The complicated\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain nature of the Man-made side of mathematics drives the layman away. We are more\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain concerned in seeing you get the right answers than in seeing you get them in the right way.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain To us, the right way is the way that gets the right answers, just so long as you know how you\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain are doing it. The psychic often gets the right answers without knowing how he does it. That\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is quite unsatisfactory. On his off days, he gets wrong answers. Although it is our aim to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain develop interpretation as a science, we do not want to lose sight of the fact that it is also an\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain art. The good actress may have been trained, but she had to have natural ability that could\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain be molded. The art of astrological interpretation can be developed even when you may have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain had very little in the way of natural ability to start with. Today, we are able to teach all\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain children to read and write, despite the fact that some may have found it easier than others. If\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain you are hungry to interpret, you will learn to interpret more rapidly, because you will allow no\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain obstacles to stay in your way for long.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain How quickly you learn to interpret will he partly dependent upon the mount of time you\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain devote to it. Even if you find yourself being quite consistently wrong, this should not\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain discourage you. Even then, you will learn by the process of elimination. Every time you learn\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that something is not right, you are that much closer to what is right. If we want to know the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain temperature, we look at a thermometer. When we receive your written interpretation of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Venus in Capricorn, we will observe it in the same manner that we would observe the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain thermometer. It will show us what you are doing. It will enable us to detect whatever you\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain might be doing wrong. By observing one person having Venus in Capricorn, it is possible that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain you may pick up characteristics that do not belong to Venus in Capricorn but to some other\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain feature of the individual's chart. That is something that we can immediately detect and call to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain your attention. So, just go ahead and write your own conception of what you think Venus in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Capricorn means. Have no regard for how terrible you might think it to be. Send it right along.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain If it is really terrible, it will contain more clues. If it happens to be practically perfect insofar as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain we can see, there will be less that we can teach you. It is not the star scholar who needs our\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain help. It is the one who has hit a snag.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There is one common error made by students of astrology. If the student dislikes some\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain person who happens to have the Sun in Scorpio, he Is too apt to attribute all of the bad\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain characteristics of this person to all Scorpio people. It must be remembered that any planetary\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain configuration can have a negative and a positive side. Because you may have known a man\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain who was killed by being hit over the head by a hammer, you are apt to develop a prejudice\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain against hammers. Yet, thousands of carpenters are making good use of hammers every day.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain They are building homes for millions of people. Let's not throw away the hammer. Instead, let\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain us teach people the proper way to use a hammer. The same for astrology. Let us not assume\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that a person is bad because of his horoscope. Instead, let us teach people how to use their\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain own horoscopes, or what abilities the horoscope signifies for some good purpose. We are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain dealing with principles of cosmic design. Those principles are perfection themselves. All evil\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain must come from our failure to understand the cosmic design, from our failure to interpret it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain correctly.\par
