\pard\f1\fs20\plain Survival or ReformTo be a good astrologer, you must WANT to be a good astrologer. Some of our students with\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the least previous education are making the best progress, because they WANT to be good\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrologers. They are determined to conquer this subject. Others are dragging behind merely\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain because they have not yet decided that they WANT to be GOOD in this field. We have given\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the student every possible cooperation. We have never failed to answer questions nor\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain explain the answers. Yet, some students are not cooperating with us. For example, some have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not written that interpretation of Venus-in- Capricorn that we requested. Some of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain interpretations that have been written, by students to whom astrology is completely new, are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain among the best we have read, but if you can't write a GOOD interpretation, write a bad one,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and we will tell you. You are going to have to practice interpretation. If necessary you are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain going to have to make mistakes, but mistakes are valuable, because they show us what is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain wrong. Mistakes themselves always form a pattern, and it is our job to detect that pattern\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and explain it to the student. When the student understands the pattern of his own mistakes,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain he never makes those mistakes again.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Although we still have lots more to tell you, from now on, you are going to have to work at\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrology. You are going to have to collect charts and interpret them. You are going to have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to WANT to be a good astrologer. You are going to have to practice. You are going to have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to prove to yourself, by experience, that the principles work the way we say they do. You\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain must not be satisfied to take our word for it. When you see them working, you are not going\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to forget about them. You are going to remember.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain How good an astrologer do you want to be? How far are you willing to go? We asked you to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain write an interpretation of Venus-in-Capricorn. Why not write an interpretation of Venus in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain each of the twelve signs, a theoretical, analytical interpretation? What do you THINK each of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain these configurations should mean. Write the interpretations and send them to us. If they are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain good if you are on the right track, wetil tell you so If you are not on the right track, just let us\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain determine WHY you are not on the right track. Let us be responsible for finding the error in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain your work. That is our responsibility, and we are here to assume it. When you have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain succeeded in writing a good interpretation for Venus in each sign, you are going to be well\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain on your way. After that, other interpretations are going to be easy for you. After a while, you\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain will get so that you can look at a chart and see at a glance more information than you could\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain put in a novel length book. You will see the design of the whole.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Right now however, you are at a crossroads. Are you going ahead or are you going to fall\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain back? You have got to practice. You have got to work and let us criticise your work. We have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain let you go a long way by yourself, but no more of that. We have told you, but now you are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain going to have to start telling us. If there appear to be any obstacles in your path from your\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain point of view, you better start telling us about them now. This is where we begin to get\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain tough.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain After that little lecture, we will continue on our way. In correspondence, students have been\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain adopting a series of abbreviations, and without knowing each other, the students have all\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain gone forward with the same abbreviations. Therefore, we are going to adopt the set of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain abbreviations that have been universally introduced by the students themselves\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain independently of each other. In the future, we will save a lot of words by the use of these\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain abbreviations, and we will introduce them here:\par
