\pard\f1\fs20\plain Progressions, Transits and Horary AstrologyThere are two schools of astrology which have been rather antagonistic toward each other,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain those who follow "progressions" and those who follow "transits." First, let us explain what\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain progressions are. There are many schools of progressions. Progressionists do not agree\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain among themselves, but we will refer to the system employed most widely in this country and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that which was taught by Llewellyn George. This school assumes some relationship between\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain two time elements which appear unrelated otherwise, a day and year. It assumes a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain relationship between a revolution of the earth around the sun and a rotation of the earth on\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain its axis in relation to the sun.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It is the assumption that if you were born at 10:17 A.M. on June 16th, 1905, a chart drawn for\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 10:17 A.M. on June 27th, 1905 would indicate phases of your life during the year following\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain your eleventh birthday. The movement of the planets during the first day of your life would\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain have a relationship to the first twelve months or year of your life. The ascendent and cusps of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the chart will change at the rate of about a degree a year, although this can vary. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain movement of the cusps in relation to planets are called primary progressions and the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain movement of the planet in relation to each other are called secondary progressions.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain However, if the system of Lewellyn George's followed, you will have all these progressions in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain each chart. George was not an exclusive progressionist, because he employed both\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain progressions and transits. Transits are merely the relationship of planets now to their birth\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain position.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain About the year 1930, Sidney K Bennett (Winn) opened war on the progressionists, and his\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain magazine came forth with a headline stating that progressions do not work. An explosion\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain occurred around his head, because the majority of astrologers in the U.S. did not agree with\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain him, and he was attacked from all quarters. It is regrettable that the two groups of people\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain could not get together and test their view scientifically but the debate was too emotional for\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that. Each side protected their ideas like their children, and astrologers of one group were\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not to be seen where there were astrologers of the other group.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In his original attack, Wynn had given an example in his own life. He had been hit by an\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain automobile and spent many weeks in the hospital as a result. Everything in his life changed,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and he maintained there was nothing in his progressed chart to indicate an accident at that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain time. Actually, Winn had overlooked something. He had not checked progressed planets\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain against progressed planets but only progressed planets against natal planets. For the year in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain question, his progressed Mars was in opposition to Saturn, and if one were to consult the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain texts of Lewellyn George for the aspect he would find that just that sort of a condition was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain predicted. This was pointed out to Winn by the writer and published in THE NEW YORK\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ASTROLOGER, a student publication that existed at that time. Although Wynn admitted an\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain oversight, it did not alter his view of progressions because the whole idea of progressions\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain was ridiculous to him. From here on, for the next 27 years, the writer has remained silent on\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain progressions. Nevertheless, for that length of time he has continued observing. To say\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain anything for or against progressions during the last 27 years would have been to make\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain enemies on one side or the other. The progressionists and the transitists have hardly been on\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain speaking terms, although it is probably that most progressionists of today use both\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain progressions and transits as did Lewellyn George, so we should probably say that the quarrel\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is between the progressionists and the non-progressionists.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We cannot ignore the fact that there have been many students who have adopted\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain progressions because they claimed to have found they work, while there have been many\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain other students who discarded progressions because they claimed to have found they did not\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain work. Thus, we have confusion. The witnesses do not testify to the same thing. What\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain witnesses are we to believe? Throughout these 27 years, while the writer has been known as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain a transitist, it might be noted that he has never published an actual opinion relative to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain progressions. He has never said YES and he has never said NO, but there comes a time when\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain one must speak, and in putting out this Course on astrology, it becomes impossible to ignore\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the matter of progressions. Actually, we have seen progressions work and we have seen them\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain fail to work. In essence, what we should say is that they have not worked accurately.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In 1926, when first studying astrology in the form of the work of Llewellyn George, we looked\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ahead, and we read up what was supposed to happen to us a long time hence. According to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain George, the writer might become the father of a child after he was 40, when progressed\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Venus reached his natal Sun. At the time of making this study the writer was 24 and a child\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain had been born in that year. It is interesting to note that he had no more children until after he\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain was 41, when his only son was born. However, the birth was off by several years. This is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain typical of the writer's experience with progressions. He found that they worked but they did\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not work at the right time. There were broad inaccuracies. In some cases, they worked very\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain accurately, but in most instances, they did not. It is not the writer's nature to impulsively toss\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain this sort of evidence out the window and merely say that progressions do not work. There is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain nothing unusual about this kind of evidence. We find it everywhere in science. Scientists are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain always finding something that appears to work one moment and not the next. They keep\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain digging until they find out why. One of our greatest scientists, Charles F. Kettering recently\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain said, "From the time he goes to school, a child is taught that it is very dangerous to fail.... The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain inventor fails 9,999 times and if he succeeds once he is in. The one time you don't want to fail\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is the last time you try. Just the minute you get satisfied with what you've got, the concrete\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain has begun to set in your head." (Quoted from Collier's, October 26th, 1956.)\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The writer never used progressions in advising clients during all of the years of his\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain professional practice, because he found that he could not depend on their accuracy although\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain he could depend on the accuracy of transits. Nevertheless, he has always kept an open mind.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Where there is smoke, there might be fire. We will later discuss what might be wrong with\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain progressions and how they might possibly be found to work with accuracy. First, however, let\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain us take up the claim of some that progressions are ridiculous. How could the planets on the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 23rd day after your birth have anything to do with the 23rd year of your life? This question is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain based on the assumption that astrology is a causal phenomenon. We have held that it is not,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and when you stop assuming that it is, new avenues open up to you. There is the possibility\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that progressions might involve some form of mathematical expression, an abstract cosmic\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain design whereby there is a relationship between rotation and revolutions of the earth. We do\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not know. It is merely a possibility. If progressions work inaccurately, we should not toss them\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain out. We should investigate more thoroughly. We should try and find out why. The first\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain automobiles did not run very efficiently but we did not throw out the whole idea, although\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain there were many people who advised doing so. Progressions in the right hands might turn up\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain something we do not yet know.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain One of the great difficulties with many progressionists is that they are fatalistic in their\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain attitude and they work with an expected precision that does not exist. They try to calculate\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain an aspect such as one of Mars-Saturn down to an exact day when accuracy does not even\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain appear to be to an exact year. Some progressed aspects would be of very long duration, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain would not apply for a specific event to occur on a certain day. When the writer was a child,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain progressed Mars moved over his natal Sun, and that interval was certainly accompanied by a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain couple of years when he was always getting hurt through falls, etc. There was no other similar\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain period in his life. The opposition of progressed Mercury to Uranus in his chart coincided with\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain his editorship of the Long Beach (N.Y.) Sun, as a youngster, which resulted in a spectacular\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain editorial campaign against political corruption in Nassau County, which in turn lead to a state\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain investigation being ordered by Governor Alfred E. Smith, and this ultimately led to conviction\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of many public officials and the end of a political regime. You will realize that many enemies\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain resulted. Immediately thereafter, Mercury crossed the writer's 7th natal cusp, and he was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain married for the first time, while visiting in Palm Beach. When progressed Mercury reached the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain conjunction of Neptune in his chart, he began writing for astrology magazines. During the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain years when progressed Mars was squaring his Jupiter, he went through a period of terrific\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain gambling losses. In fact, almost anything he did businesswise lost money, but fortunately he\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain was very young. He was coming out of his teens. Things were more than tough when the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain progressed ascendent reached natal Saturn. When the progressed ascendent reached natal\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Jupiter he moved from New York to Arizona and began a new era.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain On the other hand, many of the most important events of his life were accompanied by no\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain significant progressions. Now and then, however, we have a case that baffles us, and we turn\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to progressions to see what they might show. Here is a lady who is seized with pain in the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain middle of the night, is rushed to a hospital and goes through an emergency appendectomy.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Mars was exactly on her natal Sun and Pluto, but it had crossed that point once every two\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain years of her life with no operation necessary and without any similar ailments. Why did it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain happen this time? We turn to progressions, and we find that her progressed Mars has\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain reached her natal Sun, so that the transit of Mars was over a progressed Mars conjunct her\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Sun-Pluto in Cancer. Such cases might be coincidence, but are they?\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It has been our experience that transits work to natal cusps of houses computed in the plane\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of the earth's orbit and not to the cusps of houses computed in accord with the Placidian\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain system. The progressed chart is computed in the Placidian plane, but the planets are then\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain placed in the chart in the plane of the earth's orbit which is mathematically incommensurable.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain What would happen if the planets were re-computed in the same plane as that in which the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain chart is drawn? Insofar as we know, this never been tried, but there is some hint that Johndro\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain was experimenting with such a system prior to his death. We are not sure. This would entail a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain very complicated set of recalculations. The question is, would progressions work if they were\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain correctly calculated? They are not correctly calculated at the present time, because you can't\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain take planetary positions from an ephemeris calculated in one plane of space and apply them\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to another plane of space. That is what the progressionists are doing now.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There is no question in our minds that the progressionists are partly in error, but we hesitate\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to say they are ALL wrong. They may be partly right. They may have something unperfected\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that could be perfected. To determine the answer to such a question will require a lot of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain research and a lot of money, money that is not available at the present time, but we feel that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain we should all keep an open mind on the subject until such a time as such research is within\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the realms of possibility. It is our advice to the student to stick to transits insofar as everyday\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain practice is concerned, but to experiment with progressions or anything else as much as you\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain like, AFTER you have mastered transits. We hope the student will avoid any dogma. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain great difficulty with most of those who have taken part in the battle for or against\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain progressions is that they have assumed a dogmatic stand on one side of the question and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain have failed to penetrate further. Each side has been unable to listen to arguments on the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain other side. If that is not where progressions end, it is where progress ends.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain If a progressed chart is drawn in the Placidian plane, and then the planets are computed in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that same plane, the planetary positions would vary considerably. What is the possibility that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the astronomical error in the erection of these progressed charts equals the inaccuracies that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain we find in the timing of progressions? In other words, what is the possibility that transits\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain work in the plane of the earth's orbit (which is the plane of the zodiac) and that progressions\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain work in the plane of the Placidian system? We have similar phenomena in mathematics all of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the time. The whole idea of computing a chart in the plane of the Placidian system and then\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain inserting the planets according to the zodiac is unsound. If you draw a chart in the Placidian\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain system, you should forget the zodiac, because it is in a different plane of space and would\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain have no application in the Placidian system. The two systems cannot be employed together.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain You have half of one thing and half of something else. It is as if a person was to dress like a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain man on one side, like a woman on the other. You can compute mathematically in the decimal\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain system or you can compute in the duodecimal system, and the results will be the same, but\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain you can't use the two systems at the same time. You have to use one or the other. In the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain decimal system, 2X8 =16, but in the duodecimal system, 2X8=14. However, 16 in the decimal\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain system means exactly the same thing as 14 in the duodecimal system. In the decimal system,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 16 means 10 plus 6, while in the duodecimal system, 16 means 12 plus 6.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Transits merely involve the relationship of the planets today to the date of birth. After birth,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain you retain the greater part of the characteristics with which you were born. A study of your\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain chart as it relates to the planetary positions of today, is a study of how you fit into the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain circumstances that exist today. Just as your birth date had characteristics, today has\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain characteristics, and they are different, although some of them might be similar. Neptune has\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain been entering Scorpio as we have been writing these lessons. None of us are old enough to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain remember Neptune having been in Scorpio before, because it takes 165 years for Neptune to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain go all through the twelve signs. None of us can base our judgment of Neptune-in-Scorpio on\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain personal experience, but we can judge it analytically. We know that Neptune represents the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain SSD and that Scorpio represents the FSD. We know that the Social Survival Dynamic comes\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain under the domination of the Family Survival Dynamic. What would ordinarily be the sympathy\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of the SSD is overcome by the jealousy and fear of the FSD. On the unconscious level, the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain family wants to survive in the old form. There is fear of any new pattern. There is fear of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain injecting new blood into the family stream. In extreme cases, the inclination will be toward\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain incest. We see the effects in the south where the segregation problem is accented. Among\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the whites, there is fear that segregation will involve a mixture of blood. The negro demands\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain his birth rights, and some of the whites are afraid to grant them for fear that the past pattern\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of the family might not survive. This will work elsewhere than in the south, and it will work in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain other ways. Races will want to protect their patterns and customs of the past. Families will\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain want to protect their own. Neptune subdued in Scorpio will not help the spirit of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain brotherhood of Man, because family and racial patterns will be very strong, and this will apply\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain throughout the world. Races can be more cruel to each other, and families can be more cruel\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to each other.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There will be other transits. The power of Neptune in Scorpio will be strengthened or\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain weakened by other transits. When Mars goes into Pisces for a short while, this will balance\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain off, because then Mars, representing the FSD will be in Pisces, representing the SSD, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain each principle will be, to some extent, under the domination of the other, but watch out when\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain planets gang up in Scorpio, as they will at times, because then the effect of the FSD will\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain become even more pronounced and powerful. From the unconscious will come the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain compulsions that demand greater survival for the old family pattern. As Neptune in Scorpio\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain forms aspects to planets the charts of millions of people, the FSD will do everything in its\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain power to manifest. This may create a great many strange developments in a great many\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain places and in a great many families. It will be likely to increase racial feelings and racial\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain prejudice. It is probably having a great deal to do with the situation in the Middle East as this\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is written, but Neptune's total stay in Scorpio will be about 14 years.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain This will be a good place to bring forth another controversial phase of astrology, that known\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain as Horary Astrology. The theme of horary astrology is not unsimilar to that of a crystal ball.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There are various textbooks on horary astrology, and it has been our experience that none of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the rules in them really work. Horary astrology is more or less a form of divination. When a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain client came to Evangeline Adams, she erected a chart for the moment of the interview,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain placed the client's birth planets in this chart, and gave her interpretations from the chart. Her\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain interpretations were usually very good, but we doubt that the chart had anything in particular\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to do with the interpretations. The indication was that Evangeline Adams was psychic. A\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain crystal ball would have done quite as well as the horary chart.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The spring 1957 issue of TOMORROW Magazine contains an interesting article by Dal Lee\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain speculating on some astrologers whose interpretations may be more psychic than\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrological. Some astrologers often use a horary chart to try and find the answer to a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain question that is propounded. When the Lindbergh baby was kidnapped in 1932, astrologers\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of this group all over the country erected horary charts. They all chose different moments to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain erect the chart, because they did not hear about the kidnapping at the same time. They all\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain came up with different answers.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Many years back, we studied the textbooks on horary astrology very carefully. We collected\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain over 3000 horary charts that pertained to questions involving the future. We kept these\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain charts until the answer to the question was decided by time, and then we checked to see how\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain closely the rules worked. It was our finding that the rules didn't work at all. We forgot the old\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain methods of horary astrology.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Yet, on the other hand, we have often made good use of such charts in another way. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain charts show the transits to the natal chart at a given time. There will be other transits in the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain future. In a great many instances a question can be answered by noting what the planets are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain going to do next, but this could hardly be termed horary astrology. A neighbor came in to see\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain us one day. She was very upset. An aunt had been very ill for some time. A look at the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain patient's chart showed heavy Neptunian afflictions, including a transit of Neptune over natal\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Saturn. These were to become worse within a few days, because the Sun was to conjoin\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Neptune on her Saturn. The neighbor wanted to know what the future held. In our mind, we\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain calculated the date when the Neptunian afflictions would reach a maximum. Then we gave\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ourselves a few days leeway, set a date, and said that if the patient could successfully pass\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that date, her condition would improve. The patient died two days prior to the date set. This\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain could not be considered a horary answer. It was merely a notation of when conditions would\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain be at their worst. The question remained as to whether the patient could make the grade.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It is entirely possible that some people possess a psychic sense that allows them to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain unconsciously select a time when a horary chart will give an answer according to some set of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain rules, whatever set of rules the individual is employing, but this is hardly to be considered\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrology in the sense that it is being taught in these lessons. Many times, a single aspect will\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain give you the answer to a question, If a woman had Mars right on Uranus in her chart and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain asked us, if I leave my husband now, can we patch things up later? We would say NO. If you\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain take action under bad Mars-Uranus afflictions, you burn your bridges behind you, and there is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain no going back. It's just that we have seen that sort of thing happen again and again.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In "A New Experiment in Astrology" published in 1938, we offered what we then termed a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain partial system of horary astrology, but if we are to stick to the old meaning of the term horary\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrology, then the system could not actually be considered as horary astrology. You may find\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain people who are seeking buried treasure or who want to find a way of beating the horses, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain they may want your help. We never even consider such cases. It is a negative way of living.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The world is full of grand possibilities for those who will follow a constructive course, and to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain those people, astrology can be very useful, but why try to help a person living a negative\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain existence to live a more negative existence. You won't be doing him a favor. Lots of people\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain go looking for gold for amusement, but if they really expect to find it, they are taking the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain matter too seriously. There is more money in a new invention. You can read all kinds of books\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain about the early search for gold in Arizona, but the facts are that today, with the most modern\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mining methods, there is only one commercially operating gold mine in Arizona. Its complete\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain find for 1955 was $20,000, and the men working could have made more money if they\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain worked as carpenters. The big mining companies do not even look for gold. They look for\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain copper. They find small quantities of gold and there, but they cannot be annoyed looking for\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain it. They consider it merely as a by-product. It holds little interest for them. By modern\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain methods, they sometimes take down a whole mountain, and if there is any gold, they'll find it.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Nevertheless, there are still long bearded prospectors roaming the mountains of Arizona,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ever in search of that great find but they just like to roam. They wouldn't be at home in a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain community. It is a lot of fun, for one who likes roaming.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There was an astrologer in New Mexico a few years back who advertised himself as a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain specialist in horary astrology. From a horary chart, he decided that oil was to be found on a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain certain property. He invested his every cent in the project. He talked clients into joining and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain investing more money. After drilling operations were complete, he committed suicide. There\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain wasn't any oil. The horary chart didn't work.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It is our advice to forget the old rules of horary astrology unless you are a psychic, and in that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain event you could do better to get yourself a crystal ball and forget astrology all together. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain rules of horary astrology might throw you off. There are no rules that go with a crystal ball.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Nevertheless, if you discover some new principle, we won't have a closed mind.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Visitors are often quite surprised that we do not maintain a greater astrological library than\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain we do. It is a little foolish to load yourself up with books filled with rules that do not work.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The majority of books on astrology were written by people who knew little about astrology\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain from actual experience. They read other books by other people with little knowledge on\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrology, and in that way qualified themselves to write more books by people who knew\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain little about astrology. If a New York publisher wants to publish a book on astrology, he merely\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain seeks somebody who can write a thrilling book. He does not want to know whether the rules\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in the book. All he wants to know is whether the book sells. In some cases, the worst books\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain on astrology have been good sellers. They have been Neptunian. They appeal to the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain pathological element in society. Don't forget that the books that sell best are those that are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain pure fiction Society is far more interested in reading fiction than fact. Just compare the sale\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of fiction with non-fiction. Nevertheless, there is hope, because as the ratio of educated\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain people increases, the sale of non-fiction increases also. We are actually developing a taste\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain for more factual material.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We have stated that there are many schools of progressions. It is probable that many\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain students have investigated progressions, found that they almost worked, and began making\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain changes to try and make them work better, with no better success. One astrologer writes,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain "One system seems to work in one case, another system in another case." Is this not merely\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain telling us that results are not wrong but are inaccurate. However, it would seem that every\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain new system holds just as many inaccuracies, and the system that we suggested for\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain investigation, erecting the chart in the Placidian system and also computing the planets in the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain plane of this system, might prove just as faulty. We do not know. It is merely a mathematical\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain suggestion which may or may not have merit.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Some systems attempt to use a degree for a year, but a degree of a circle has no factual\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain foundation. It is a purely arbitrary, man-made standard of measurement, like a foot. We know\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of no real basis for dividing a circle into 360 equal parts. It is supposed that this was agreed\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain upon because ancients believed that there were 360 days in a year, but this is probably some\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of the fiction of modern astronomy. The Aztecs had a more perfect calendar when it was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain discovered than the European astronomers did. The ancients knew more astronomy than we\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain think they did. Their knowledge was lost long before the birth of Christianity. How much was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain lost in the burning of the great libraries of Alexandria and China, and how much was lost long\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain before that is unknown. At any rate, we have no reason to believe that a degree or 1/360th\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of a circle has any meaning or significance. It is merely a handy way of measuring something,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain just as a foot rule is a handy way of measuring something so long as everyone is employing\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the same length foot rule.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain On the other hand, we have found the figure 12 or 1/12th of definite value and significance.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We divide the zodiac into 12 parts and we divide the horoscope into 12 parts or houses. All\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of our evidence seems to indicate that this division has a factual foundation. It works, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrologers have clung to it for centuries and centuries. That part tested by RCA\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Communications Inc. in its independent research also seems to stand up.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Astrologers have also employed what they call decanates or 10- degree areas. Such an area\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is 1/36th of a circle. We have never found that these areas stood up as entities in themselves,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and there does not appear to be any mathematical reason for them. 36 is rnerely 3 X 12 or 6\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain x 6. However, we have found significance in the square of 12, dividing the circle into 144\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain parts or 12 X 12 This has been done by others, but we have never found the interpretations\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain accompanying such division to be correct. We have found, for example, that the Sun in one\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain part of a sign has characteristics not found when the Sun is in another part of the same sign.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The key to this is another symmetrical pattern. Each sign is divided into twelve equal areas of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 21/2 degrees, making up 144 areas, 144 being the square of 12, or 12 X 12. One much used\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain system begins each sign with a pure type of the sign. The first 21/2 degrees of Aries is the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Aries division of Aries, the next 21/2 degrees the Taurus section of Aries, etc. We never\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain found that this system worked. Instead, we begin Aries with Scorpio. We are substituting\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain survival for reform. The first 21/2 degrees of Aries will be the Scorpio division, the next 21/2\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain degrees the Sagittarius division, the next 21/2 degrees the Capricorn division, etc. This gives\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain us an interesting mathematical pattern that is perfectly symmetrical. The last 21/2 degrees of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Aries will be the Libra division, and Taurus will begin with a Libra division, so that the end of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain one sign is always joined to the next sign by the same subsign. The last 21/2 degrees of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Taurus will be the Virgo division of Taurus, and the first 21/2 degrees of Gemini will be the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Virgo division of Gemini.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We often find some very Neptunian situations which are not experienced otherwise when the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Sun is between l71/2 and 20 degrees Cancer, the Pisces division of Cancer. There will be such\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain a point in each zodiacal sign. In Aries, it will be from 10 to l21/2 degrees, in Taurus, it will be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain l21/2 to 15 degrees, in Gemini 15 to l7 degrees, etc. You will see above how Cancer fits in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain next. This is something we spotted way back in the early 30's, but we have never published\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain anything on it, although we have been using it since that time. You will see that it is merely\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain one more step in figuring out the design in the solar system. However, it might be interesting\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to note just how we came upon the idea.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There is a very interesting book on the characteristics of the degree written by an Australian\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain named Kozminsky. It is probably out of print. Sidney K. Bennett prized this book highly, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain he once reprinted the whole book serially in his magazine. One day, Bennitt brought the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain book, well marked up, to the writer. He was fascinated. "There must be a key to this fellow's\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain interpretations," he said, "You will note that this division of this sign definitely has the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain characteristics of Mars in it. I have marked some of these divisions with the planet that seems\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to be the key. See what you make out of it."\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The writer marked up the divisions further and finally noted that all the pieces fitted together.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain All we had to do was to fill in the missing pieces of the puzzle with a symmetrical design.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain However, the catch was that Kominsky was using degree areas, and the 3rd degree of a sign\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain was part of one division and part of another. We had to make an allowance for this\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain discrepancy, but when we had finished doing so, we had a perfectly symmetrical pattern. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain big question is, how did Kominsky gain the original interpretations which appeared so\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain authentic in most cases. For the answer, we will have to ask him. It is his claim that he wrote\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the interpretations psychically. They just came to him. In other words, the author wrote the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain book, unknowingly, to a mathematical pattern which he did not know to exist. For hat reason,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain he followed convention and divided the zodiac into 360 equal parts instead of 144 equal\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain parts. The result might have been even more interesting had he started out with 144 equal\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain parts. This brings up another interesting question. Nobody has ever been able to explain\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain psychic phenomena, extrasensory perception or precognition, because it defies time and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain space, as has been proved in laboratory experiments at Duke and other universities. What is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the possibility that these phenomena merely involve unconscious tuning into abstract,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematical, cosmic design? This would explain everything with one swoop. In the abstract\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain world, there is no time and no space. Neither time nor space can exist except by relativity.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The above is one more instance where our own discovery of design in the solar system was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain stimulated by something that was actually started by Sidney K. Bennett, and we might never\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain have hit upon the answer had we not been fortunate enough to have known him. We began\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain by taking pot shots at each other in two opposing magazines when we were both a lot\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain younger and wound up very good friends. In fact the greatest element of the writer's own\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain success in the astrological field was his ability to gain the co-operation of his competitors.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Without the help of his competitors, he would never have gotten into business, and without\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the help of his competitors, he would never have stayed in business. Competitors can be very\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain valuable to one if his FSD is not so strong that he excludes them as members of his family.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain When you have no competitors, life can get very dull.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain A new question arises. If the zodiac can be divided into 12 parts, and then can be subdivided\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain into 12 X 12 or 144 parts, can it now be divided into 12 X 12 X 12 parts? This would be l728\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain sub-sub parts. It is an interesting question, but we have not had time to investigate its\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain possibilities. We mention it, because it might have possibilities and we hope it will give\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain somebody something to do, just as Sidney K. Bennett gave us a lot to do in our earlier days\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in astrology. Another question that rises and has never been tested is thi5. If' the zodiac can\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain be divided into 12 X 12 parts, can an astrological house be divided into twelve parts, each of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain which would be 1/144th of a circle. We do not know, but the thought may give somebody\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain else something to do. There is lots to do. It might prove much more interesting and successful\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain than trying to find a system of beating the horse races or than searching for gold in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mountains where gold is very scarce. If the medical profession can't cure your wife of cancer,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain gold isn't going to do it either, but there is always a possibility that more knowledge might.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Gold is only a medium to get other people to work for you, and you can often get people to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain work for you by merely getting them interested in what you are trying to do.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Coming back to progressions, our conclusion is that they are inaccurate. We do not claim that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the idea of progressions is wrong or that there is no foundation for them. We suspect that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain there may be. However, the progressionist will have a difficult time trying to make them\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain reasonable if he sticks to a causal hypothesis for astrology. We don't thing he should stick to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain a causal hypothesis. We think it breaks down. Reconsidering astrology as merely\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematical expression re- opens the door to progressions. They might involve a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematical pattern, and if they do, there is nothing strange about them. There are stranger\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain things throughout mathematics and nature. We have not yet found any mathematical\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain relationship between rotations and revolutions of the earth, but there might be one, and if\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the progressionists can develop the fact that there IS, then they will have made the greatest\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain scientific discovery of the age. It would open up the possibility that there is also a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematical relationship involving all the motions of all the planets. Thus, although we have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain found progressions inaccurate a good part of the time, our own investigations lead us to the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain suspicion that we might make a very serious error if we were to throw them away altogether.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In working with transits, so long as the natal chart and the planets are in the same plane of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain space, you have a relatively simple matter to deal with. Astronomical tables are accurate. You\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain know where the planets are. You are not dealing with two different things at one time and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain trying to make two things fit together that do not fit together. If there are two roads from\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain New York to Boston cannot travel over both of them simultaneously. You have to make up\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain your mind which you are going to take, but you might bake one going and come back the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain other way. If one is going to use progress-ions one must make up his mind in what plane of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain space he is going to calculate. We have tried the plane of the zodiac and the result is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain inaccuracies.\par
