\pard\f1\fs20\plain The Secondary ChartIn presenting the Secondary Chart, we offer our own term for a product of the ancients little\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain used by astrologers of today, dropped because of the inclination of modern astrologers to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain attempt to fit their work into the dogma of a fiction-loving academic world endeavoring to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain blend everything into a causal hypothesis, and audaciously and perhaps criminally labeling\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the package "Science." There has been the unfortunate attempt to fit into a world where\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain every effort has been made to reach a truth by locking one series of errors into another\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain greater series of errors.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It is not too unusual to hear an astrologer make reference to the "Pars Fortuna" or "Part of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Fortune", with no particular conception of what such a thing might be, and without making\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain any particular effort to find out. Like house cusps or sign cusps or aspects, the Pars Fortuna is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain a mere mathematical point and only one of a whole series of mathematical points. It is a tiny\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain part of a pattern. It is as significant as the last numeral on an automobile license tag, which\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain will classify it as not belonging to 90 percent of the automobiles, but it will not identify the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain car insofar as the other ten percent of cars is concerned. The Pars Fortuna is a single point in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the secondary Chart, just as the Moon is a single point in the horoscope of birth.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Let us assume that you have a natal chart before You, and let us assume that you have all the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain planets attached to each other by some means whereby you can move them all at once\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain without moving the signs of the zodiac or the houses, but you move the planets within the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain zodiac and within the houses. As you move one body, you move all bodies, and you move\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain them all an equal distance when you move one. If you had the planets on a separate piece of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain paper that would turn and if you had the planets and the degrees between the planets\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain accurately drawn to scale, this would be quite easy.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Now, you move or twist all the planets as you might move or twist a radio dial. Let us say that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain you are "tuning" so to speak. You twist the dial until the Sun coincides with the ascendent..\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain You stop there and all the other bodies have fallen into place. This is the Secondary Chart.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain You have maintained the original planetary pattern. You have not changed that but you have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain adjusted it to allow measurement from the Zodiacal position of the ascendent instead of from\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the Zodiacal position of the Sun. This was a procedure followed by the ancients thousands of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain years ago, and such an operation furnishes us with ample proof that the ancients were\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain employing astrology as pure mathematics, and if their procedure was unsound, then it is just\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain as unsound to employ algebra, because an algebraic equation is a mere pattern of an\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain abstract principle, and the Secondary Chart is a mere pattern of an abstract principle. When a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain child is taught that 9X9 equals 81, it makes no difference whether the truth is applied to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain horses or cans of preserved peaches; the abstract truth is there. It is something that can be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain applied in a material or any other kind of a world, and we do not hesitate to argue if\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain someone claims that just because 9 rows of 9 horses total 81 horses, that does not prove that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 9 rows of 9 cans of preserved peaches total 81 cans of preserved peaches.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain If the Moon happened to be 120 degrees west of the Sun in the original birth chart, it will\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain remain 120 degrees west of the Sun, but now it will be exactly on the cusp of the Ninth\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain House, because the Ninth House Cusp is 120 degrees west of the ascendent and the Sun has\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain been moved to the ascendent.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In the birth chart, the Moon was not at the cusp of the Ninth House, but because in this\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Secondary Chart, the Moon is at the cusp of the Ninth House, this mathematical point\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain becomes attuned to transits. The position of the Moon in the Secondary Chart is that which\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain we have called the "Pars Fortuna" or "Part of Fortune." The fact that we have already\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain associated the Moon with the Individual Survival Dynamic and with money should be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain sufficient to explain why the ancients called this point the Part of Fortune.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There will be a similar point in the Secondary Chart for each of the planets. If Jupiter was 3\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain degrees east of the Sun in the natal chart, it is now 3 degrees east of the ascendent or right\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in the middle of the Second House of the Secondary Chart. If the original chart had 13\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain degrees of Libra on the ascendent, we now find Jupiter at 28 degrees of Scorpio. Remember\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that we do not change the natal ascendent We do not change the degrees of the Zodiac on\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the House Cusps. We merely change the planets within the chart. By this means, the ancients\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain set up a whole series of mathematical points in addition to the regular planetary positions.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Unfortunately, it is impossible to determine these additional points that make up the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Secondary Chart unless the exact time of birth or the exact degree of the zodiac that is on\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the ascendent at birth is known. If your ascendent is in error by one degree, then all of these\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematical points will be in error by one degree. However, the experienced astrologer will\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain discover that these points furnish an excellent means of further checking the tine of birth,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain because once they have been reliably established, transits to these points appear every bit as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain important as transits to other factors in the natal chart.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Little or almost no work or research in connection with this Secondary Chart has been\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain accomplished in modern times, and it is doubtful whether the student can go very far with\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain research except in those few cases where there can be some degree of certainty about the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ascending degree of the chart. If the student feels certainty about his own ascending degree,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain then there will be an exciting bit of experimentation ahead. If the chart is correctly timed,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain then a whole new realm of transits is opened up for inspection. By the time the student\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain reaches this lesson, there will be a good deal of familiarity with the author's writing, thinking\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and style, and the student may be interested in noting that his Secondary Chart places\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Mercury at 21- Sagittarius, where it will be conjunct his natal Uranus at 20- Sagittarius.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain When you are satisfied that your own birth time has been established correctly, insert the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain secondary positions into that same chart in red or a different colored ink, and see what\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain happens. The results will often prove startling, because important conjunctions or other\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain aspects between secondary and natal positions can occur for a particular time of day that will\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not exist for any other time of day, and stupendous differences can exist for persons born\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain less than an hour apart. The above mentioned conjunction of secondary Mercury and natal\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Uranus would not apply for any persons born at another hour of the same day.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Allow us to emphasize that the Secondary Chart is an almost unexplored matter insofar as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain modern astrology is concerned. Nothing could offer more definite proof that the ancient\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrologers were not causalists. They were mathematicians. Astrology was a study of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematics, geometrical principles and functions, strictly a study of abstract realms. This is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain something a mathematician can grasp. Mathematics is pure abstraction and astrology is pure\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain abstraction. Both are keys to the cosmic design of life itself.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We think we have progressed, and we have to some extent, but when we view the last 2500\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain years, progress has been slight due to the heavy load of dogma we have had to drag along.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain To a considerable extent, education has been a hindrance rather than a guide, for the better\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain part of education during 2500 years has been blind perpetuation of dogma. We are only\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain beginning to seek freedom from the chains of politically organized religion and academics. It\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain may yet take many years, but when actual enlightenment comes, when it is finally realized\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that astrology is mere mathematical expression, there is bound to be a terrific impact, for\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrology itself opens the door to unlimited realms of mathematical knowledge.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It has been our experience that when the true natal chart has been satisfactorily established\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to allow consideration of the Secondary Chart, a completely new phase of things is opened\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain up. The value of the natal chart has suddenly been doubled, for half of the whole (If this is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the whole). has been previously and subtly concealed. A great deal more of the design has\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain been revealed.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain More important than anything else, insofar as this Secondary Chart is concerned, is the fact\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that it opens up a whole new realm of thought. If we can measure in terms of patterns to this\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain extent, how far can such a principle be carried? Please realize that from here on this\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain conversation must be considered as purely speculative, but let us assume that a person was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain born with Mars 90 degrees east of Saturn. Can we consider that for the life of that person,\par
\pard\f0\fs22\b Saturn is ALWAYS symbolically 90 degrees west of Mars?\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain
\pard\f1\fs20\plain This would mean that as Mars transits the heavens, insofar as that particular individual is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain concerned, figuratively speaking, a symbolical Saturn is always traveling 90 degrees behind\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Mars, and as Saturn transits the heavens, a figurative Mars is always traveling 90-degrees\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ahead of it. This would mean that the pattern of the birth horoscope works in many different\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ways, but the pattern always remains the same. This is the sort of thing that happens\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain throughout mathematics. It happens in physics, in biology and in psychology. Put steel filings\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain on a piece of paper and place a magnet beneath the paper. A pattern forms, a design, a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematical design. The steel filings obey a design. Biology always obeys designs, and the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain psychologist is ever observing patterns and designs that thoughts, emotions and behavior\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain follow. The formations of minerals obey design. Snow flakes obey design. Everything obeys\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain design. Life obeys design.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Although arithmetic was formerly regarded as a very simple branch of mathematics, it has\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain become one of the most involved and complicated since the introduction of number theory\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain by Fermat. During centuries of history of math, there was the inclination to emphasize Euclid\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and forget Pythagoras as a mystic. There are no greater mystics than the more advanced\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain modern mathematicians. Thus, today, interest in Pythagoras among modern mathematician\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain has been revised.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ;Pythagoras was a great mathematician 2500 years ago, but he thought in therms of design.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain To him, numbers were designs. The triangular numbers were numbers out of which triangles\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain could be formed.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Note that any two consecutive triangular numbers, when added together equal a square,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain which means that any square is the sum of two consecutive triangular numbers. Note also\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that if you set the smaller triangular numbers on the larger triangular numbers, in layers,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain consecutively, you form a tetrahedron or 3-sided pyramid, while if you do the same with the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain squares, you form a 4 sided pyramid. Today, the mathematicians deal with all sorts of these\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain series of numbers. The pentagonal numbers have very interesting characteristics. They are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain numbers that can be formed into 5-sided-designs. By playing with these designs, the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematician makes all kinds of discoveries, and he then finds counterparts of these\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain designs everywhere in nature, It was Euclid who said, "God geometrizes". The whole universe\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is put together according to geometrical design. The ancients knew this, but we have been\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain living through 2500 years of dogma, during which time our academicians and religious\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain leaders forgot the ancients. The ancients saw geometrical laws working in the heavens and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain on earth, in the macrocosm and the microcosm. The told us, "As above, so below?" That's\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain where astrology came in. They applied their designs to the solar system as well to the lower\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain world, and realized that by watching the laws of nature function in the upper world you can\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain know how those laws function in the lower world. The ancient astrologers were\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematicians and the ancient mathematicians were astrologers. There were no\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astronomers. They came later as the illegitimate children of the rape of astrology by the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain church.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The great mathematicians of today live in another world, Few people understand them. They\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain talk in symbols and a language that others do not understand. They reach a point where they\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain leave numbers behind and talk in symbols, each symbol expressing some broad principle of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the abstract world. It was in this way that they reached the secrets of the atom. They have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain merely been traversing the same world where the minds of the Greek mathematicians moved\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain about. Remember that it was the ancient Greeks, who originally conceived the idea of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain atom. We are told that the Greeks visualized the atom as something akin to a billiard ball in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain shape and design, but that is merely the modern academician's conception of how the Greeks\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain conceived of an atom. Billiard balls do not fit together into a solid. There is space in-between\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the balls. The ancients did not think along those lines. They knew all about geometrical\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain designs in three dimensions. They knew, for example, that twelve-sided objects having a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain pentagon,for each side would fit together into a solid. We do not exactly know just how they\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain conceived an atom, and our modern scientists do not know what an atom might look like if.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain they could see one. They know only how the atom functions mathematically and they can\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain visualize from there, but they keep changing their views as to what an atom is like. Only\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain recently, they have discovered what they call "strange particles", something new about the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain atom that they didn't take into their previous visualization.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Whether we are dealing with astrology or some other science, progress seems dependent\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain upon the discovery of the secrets of design. It all seems a matter of discovering the, cosmic\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain design of, the abstract world. In the Secondary Chart, we have a great secret that has been\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain passed down to us by the ancients. It is a very useful chart, disclosing many things which\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain cannot otherwise be disclosed, but what we must grasp is not just the method of erecting\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain such a chart, we must realize the vast possibilities that it op ens up to us. It produces entirely\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain new means of astrological measurement. It illustrates that we can employ geometrical\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrology pattern for purposes of measurement. We find that the natal horoscope is filled\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain with invisible things we knew nothing about.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Consider the case of identical twins born 16 minutes apart. The ascendent would differ in the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain two charts by about four degrees. The planets, even the Moon, would be in practically the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain same zodiacal position, but the secondary position of these planets would all vary by four\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain degrees, like the ascendant and house cusps. If Mars hit secondary Uranus by transit in one\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain chart, it would be a number of days before it would reach secondary Uranus in the other\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain chart, Thus, while transits to the natal positions would be identical for the two twins-born 16\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain minutes apart, they would not coincide where the secondary planetary positions were\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain concentric in the case where two people were born 12 hours apart, the secondary positions\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain would differ by roughly 180 degrees.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain When we stop to realize that astrology is a mere study of abstract mathematical design, the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain greatest possibility of all opens up for us. That is the indication that the greatest\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematical secrets of all as they relate to all branch's of science, are a actually hidden\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain behind the curtain of the astrological chart. Figure out the truth here, and you are likely to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain find it elsewhere. Yet, you have to stop thinking in terms of cause-and-effect where astrology\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is concerned, because until you do, you will not be likely to think in terms of mathematical\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain design or in terms of cosmic design. Any study of number theory will prove helpful in getting\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain away from a causal hypothesis. When we leave this over-ripe hypothesis behind insofar as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrology is concerned, then there is no reason why we should not find the mathematical key\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain repeated in many places. It is no longer unreasonable to find a mathematical pattern in the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain horoscope, and it is no longer unreasonable if we should also find it in the palm of a person's\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain hand.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Our experience has often indicated that the female mind more easily grasps the conception\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that things can fall into a mathematical pattern without the need for any causal factor.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Perhaps that has been one of our difficulties. For thousands of years, we have tried to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain convince ourselves that the male mind is superior to that of the female. All the dogma of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain last several thousand years has been brought to us by the male. It is only in our own time that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain we have allowed women to vote. They were not regarded as sufficiently intelligent to vote\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain fifty years ago, and even the writer can remember hearing men argue the point. The first\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain election where women were allowed to vote was anticipated with great apprehension. Most\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of the first women voters voted only as their husbands directed them. A good wife obeyed\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain her husband because he knew best. The interest of women was supposed to be limited to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain housework and babies.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The husband belittles his wife if she believes in palmistry, one of the oldest beliefs on earth,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain but for the palm of a hand to hold the key to a mathematical pattern that is expressed in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain many places is no more irrational than to believe that all snowflakes freeze with six sides.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In many cases, what we have termed a woman's intuition has merely been her ability to think\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in terms of patterns, and in principle these patterns are no different from mathematical\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain patterns. They can be patterns of abstract reality, and although the woman can also be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain wrong, this can apply to the mathematician. It is possible for him to make an error\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain somewhere. He may not have grasped a pattern accurately, and the woman may not have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain grasped the pattern accurately.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In "The River of Life", by Rutherford Platt, we find a biologist thinking in terms of abstract\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain patterns. Platt is not limited in his thinking by an academic status. He works as an advisor to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Walt Disney. He speaks of the "bee animal." Since we are accustomed to thinking of a bee as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain an insect and not an animal, this requires a bit of explanation. His language and his use of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain term "bee animal" helps to get his views across. He does not regard the bee as an animal. By\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain "bee animal", he means the abstract pattern of the whole hive. He refers to the whole swarm\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain as an animal. He compares individual bees to the individual cells of the human body, pointing\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain out how individual cells sacrifice themselves for the welfare of the body as a whole, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain demonstrating a parallel where individual bees do likewise and are automatically sacrificed in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the interests of the swarm as a whole unit, the bee animal might refer to this as work of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Social Survival Dynamic if we were dealing with the human pattern.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain If we think of the whole unit as the bee animal, then we find that there is a pattern. We can\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain go from hive to hive and we find that all bee animals behave in a similar manner. In all bee\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain animals there is one queen bee. Other female bees never become queens because they are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain fed on pollen mush for only two days, and after that they are fed on nothing but honey. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain queen is fed pollen mush for her entire life because pollen mush is necessary to develop her\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain sexually. The other girl bees do not develop sexually. The behavior of one bee animal is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain exactly the same as the behavior of another bee animal a thousand miles away. There is a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain pattern, an abstract pattern, and all bee animals behave in accord with this abstract pattern.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Just as all cells of a body behave in accord with an abstract pattern, members of a society\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain behave in accord with an abstract pattern. Whether we deal with mathematics, geology,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain biology or atoms, we find that behavior conforms to abstract patterns. This principle applies\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to the behavior of minerals as they form themselves into crystals. It applies to the behavior of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain cells in the human body. It applies to the behavior of bee animals or ant animals. It applies\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain where there is life and where there is no life. It applies to the pattern of thought of a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain particular individual. One person is conventional and another is unconventional because that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain was the pattern of birth.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Since the very beginning of this Course, it has been obvious that women have been able to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain grasp the overall pattern of our discussion more readily than men. In many cases, they appear\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to have less in the way of mental blocks. Often the individual with little education grasps\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain things better than the person with a well-rounded education. This conforms with Charles\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Kettering's statement that the greater a man's education, the less apt he is to become an\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain inventor. This does not argue that education is not a requisite. Instead, it points out the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain weakness and evils of an educational system which teaches people to memorize rather than\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to understand.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Whether you are to study astrology or mathematics, it is important to learn to think in terms\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of abstract patterns. Such thinking is a shortcut. You become familiar with a pattern where it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain applies in one place in nature. You get to understand it, and then you meet up with that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain pattern again and again in far removed places where there is no possible material\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain connection. In the horoscope the relationship of all planets to each other becomes a pattern.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It is like a brand. All of the automatic behavior of the individual conforms to this pattern or\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain brand. This does not mean that the individual, through understanding of his own automatic\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain behavior, cannot begin to behave consciously according to a design of his own conscious\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain making, and when he does this, he is discovering his own powers of free will and employing\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain them to replace his own automatic behavior. The behavior of the bee animal is automatic.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Otherwise, it would not be so exactly the same as the behavior of all other bee animals\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain wherever found. Despite the well organized civilization in which the individual bees live, they\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain appear to have done nothing about developing free will. Even the queen herself is a slave to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the interests of the hive. All queen bees behave in exactly the same manner. When it Is time\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to do so, the queen leaves the hive followed by a swarm of males who follow her high into\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the air. Ultimately, one catches up to her or she allows one to catch up. At this high altitude,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the queen has her one taste of sex. This completed, she kills the satisfying male. He has\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain served his purpose as far as the interests of society are concerned. It is now his fate to die.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There is no longer need for the other male bees. They are driven from the hive or killed. If\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain they are not killed, it is their fate td starve to death. The queen returns to the hive her sex life\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is over. Never again will she have romantic contact with a male. This one act of sex has done\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the job well, and so long as she is fed pollen mush, she will continue to lay eggs. Her duty to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain society is to lay eggs.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Perhaps we have gone far afield from the Secondary Chart, but it is necessary to understand\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain why the Secondary Chart can be an abstract reality and become as important as the natal\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain chart itself. It is necessary to understand why transits to mathematical points can become as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain important as transits to points which were actually occupied by material planets at the time\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of birth. Of course, this is no different than transits to house cusps, because house cusps are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mere mathematical points. It is no different than transits through signs of the zodiac, because\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the division of one sign from another is a mere mathematical point. We begin with the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain planets and from them arises a whole superstructure of abstract mathematical points. A\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain whole "society" of mathematical points ultimately becomes a mathematical pattern. We have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to give a name to the whole society of mathematical points, and just as Platt invented a term\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain for the bee animal the ancients invented a word for the whole mathematical pattern, and they\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain called it a horoscope.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Realize that if a person is born with the Sun exactly on the Eastern horizon, so that half of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Sun is above the horizon and half the Sun is below the horizon (Mountains do not count),\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain then the Natal Chart and the Secondary Chart are one and the same, because the Sun and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the ascendent are one and the same. By the time the Sun is one degree above the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Ascendent, the Natal and Secondary Charts have parted by one degree. All of the planets,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain like the Sun, have moved one degree westward (as the earth turned eastward), but in the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Secondary Chart, they have not changed, but this is only insofar as their relationship to the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ascendent and house cusps are concerned. It depends upon what you are employing as your\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain frame of reference. If you employ the zodiac as your frame of reference, then all the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain secondary bodies have moved forward in the zodiac by one degree. In other words, in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain relation to the ascendent and house cusps, all the Secondary planets will remain as they were\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain at sunrise, but in relation to the zodiacal signs, all the planets will move forward in the zodiac\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain as the Sun rises. (Of course, this will be slightly altered to the extent that the planets will have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain some additional motion of their own during the day, but this is slight. It can be great where\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the Moon is concerned.)\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We have tried to explain this Secondary Chart from a number of different points of view in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain order that the student may understand it instead of being dependent upon any memorized\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain formula. However, if you want a formula, all you have to do is take the natal chart, measure\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the distance, east or west, of each body from the Sun and insert it in the Secondary Chart\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that same distance from the ascendent. If Mercury is ten degrees west of the Sun, insert it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ten degrees west of the ascendent, etc. This should be simple enough. If your birth time is in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain error by ten degrees on the ascendent, then all the secondary positions will be out by ten\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain degrees. You can check transits to the secondary positions. You may find out that they do not\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain work accurately. They may work early or late. This is your key. Constant checking of transits\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to the secondary positions of the planets in your chart will enable you to correct your time of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain birth just as constant checking of transits to your house cusps will do the same. When you\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain have the chart exactly right, you will find that all transits to all of these mathematical points\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain will click with precision.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Realize that the planetary pattern in the Secondary Chart is exactly the same as the planetary\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain pattern in the Natal Chart. The relationship of any material planet to all other material bodies\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is exactly the same in both charts. If Mars was 132 degrees east of Jupiter in one chart, it is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain also 132 degrees east of Jupiter in the other chart. All we have done is to twist the planetary\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain dial exactly as we twist a radio dial when we are tuning the radio. A small twist of the radio\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain dial may bring us music from New York instead of music from Chicago. If twins are born four\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain minutes apart, all the secondary positions of the second twin have been altered by\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain approximately a degree. Yet, the natal planets can be considered as exactly the same in both\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain charts insofar as the zodiac is concerned.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In closing, let us come back to a short discussion of this difference between the male and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain female ways of thinking. Our experience with male and female students has been extremely\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain interesting to us and should be interesting to all. We have had a whole series of female\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain students who, after starting this Course, suddenly developed an appetite to know more about\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematics which, up until that time, was repulsive to them. These students are also now\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain studying mathematics and enjoying the study to the full. This tendency has not been near so\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain apparent among male students. This might be accounted for by the fact that on the average\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain our female students have more time. In addition, many of our male students are engineers\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and already have a mathematical education beyond that of our female students.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Nevertheless, we cannot escape the fact that our female students have responded with far\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain more enthusiasm to the whole idea that we live in accord with abstract cosmic design and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that both astrology and mathematics are mere studies of abstract cosmic design. We cannot\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain escape the conclusion that female students respond readily to the idea of thinking in terms of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain abstract patterns, while male students are ever clinging to a more materialistic conception of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain things. It would appear that our lady students have found it easier to break away from old\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain frames of reference from old thought patterns. Yet, we must also point out that male students\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain with a mathematical background grasp these views much more rapidly than male students\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain without that mathematical background, and we actually do have male students who have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain begun the study of mathematics anew and with a new enthusiasm for the subject. Among\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain both sexes, there have been signs of a completely new outlook on life, and this we like.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Nothing has proved a greater reward to us than those letters coming from some students\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain who state that the Course has altered their whole viewpoint on life for the better.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Many of the reactions of students are valuable, and we cannot bring all of these reactions\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain into the Lessons themselves, but we hope, through STUDENT FORUM, to help students to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain help each other by the exchange of views on these subjects.\par
\pard\f0\fs22\b SUPPLEMENT TO LESSON XXI\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain
\pard\f0\fs22\b The Secondary Ascendent\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain
\pard\f1\fs20\plain A year or more after Lesson XXI was written, there was an important development. I was off\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain on a hike on the desert one day while the principles of the secondary chart were kicking\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain around in my mind. Suddenly a question came into my mind:\par
\pard\f0\fs22\b Why shouldn't the secondary chart have its own ascendent?\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It dawned on me that the same formula employed to find the planets in the secondary chart\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain could be used to produce a secondary ascendent. I turned around and headed for home.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain This was an idea that I wanted to check out right away. Reaching home, I went right to work\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and I drew the first secondary chart with its own ascendent. -my own.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain I got quite a surprise. It gave me a secondary ascendent of 8 Leo with Uranus at 6 Leo. This\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain was most interesting to me because all my life I had found that most astrologers were able to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain guess my Sagittarius ascendent from my personal appearance, but a few failed and when\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain they failed, they guessed it as Leo. It had always puzzled me because I felt I had Leo\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain characteristics. When young, I always had a flair for showmanship which smacked of Leo.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain This plus the fact that some astrologers seemed to see Leo in me presented a problem that I\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain should have considered a clue because I did not have one planet in Leo.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In the new secondary chart, the ascendent, Moon and Uranus were all in Leo.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain I wrote a letter to all of my students telling them of this experience and asking them to test\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain out the new concept. There was a quick response. They all thought I had hit on something\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that was for REAL. It explained many things they had not been able to explain.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain However, the new discovery simplified everything and made most of the calculations of\par
\pard\f0\fs22\b Lesson XXI unnecessary, for I soon spotted something else.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain
\pard\f1\fs20\plain With my primary and secondary charts side by side, the planets were in exactly the same\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain house positions. It was as if the primary chart had been left alone but the zodiac in the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain background had been twisted a given number of degrees.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain This gives us a much simpler formula for drawing the secondary chart than the one given in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Lesson XXI. So, here it is, but remember that the secondary chart is correct and useful ONLY\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain if the given time of birth is correct:\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 1--Measure the distance from the Sun to the ascendent.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 2--Now, go in the opposite direction from the ascendent the same number of degrees. In\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain other words, if your natal Sun was 20 degrees above the ascendent, go 20 degrees below the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ascendent. That degree is the secondary ascendent.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 3--Put this degree on the ascendent of a new chart. Fill in the cusps with the other zodiacal\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain signs at equal 30 degree intervals.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 4--Place the planets in this chart in exactly the same house positions as they appear in the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain primary chart. If a planet is 10 degrees past the 3rd cusp in the primary chart, place it 10\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain degrees past the 3rd cusp in the secondary chart.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain That's all there is to it.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain How does the secondary chart differ. Everybody asks that question.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Actually, they are both part of the same horoscope. We make two charts of it because if we\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain place all the data in one chart it becomes too complicated and impossible to read. As to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain which chart is more important. I do not know.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain As to how they differ, I don't know. I have never been able to decide. In most cases, the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain primary ascendent seems to have more to do with personal appearance than the secondary\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain chart, but sometimes the opposite seems true. I think it best to consider the two charts of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain equal importance. This can have a great deal to do with twins because it explains why twins\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain born quite close can be so different. For example, two girls both have Sagittarius on\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ascendent. One is blonde, the other a brunette. The first girl has a Capricorn secondary\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ascendent, the second girl an Aquarius secondary ascendent. The first girl has Mars conjunct\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the primary ascendent. The second girl has Jupiter conjunct the ascendent. This makes the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain whole combination completely different from the primary chart?\par
