\pard\f1\fs20\plain Child TrainingThe horoscope of a child is very important .We hear a lot about juvenile delinquency these\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain days, and most of it could have been avoided. It is another case where we hold the sins of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain society against the individual We may have a few spoiled brats, but the ratio is pretty low,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and even the so-called spoiled brats have not had the right kind of an understanding allowed\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain them. The surprising thing is that so many children come into the world and survive in spite of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain parents teachers and other adults. A rabbit enters a world where he may have to do a lot of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain running or jumping if he wants to survive, but the human child enters a world of hypocrisy\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and neurosis unknown to rabbits.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Although some children are over-protected by the parents, in a very large number of cases,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain child training means training the child in a way that will be the most convenient for the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain parents. A child is denied trial by any jury of its peers. He is seldom allowed much in the way\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of a voice in his own affairs, but he often finds out that he does get consideration if he\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain throws tantrums because folks don't want to listen to him. He is taught to always tell the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain truth, but he may soon discover that this rule is only for him, not his parents. They tell him all\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain kinds of falsehoods. He soon catches on but has learned that it is best to observe and keep\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain his mouth shut about it. If he has any good ideas or conceptions of his own, he soon\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain discovers that he is not supposed to think, because the rules have already been made. He\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain came too late. When he enters the world, he is not a property owner and he can't vote.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain He may get beat up occasionally, and he is apt to discover that this may not be connected\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain with what he does or doesn't do so much as how older people feel on a given day. If they are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain happy, he can get away with anything. If they are unhappy, there is going to be trouble and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain maybe pain. He discovers that there is such a thing as dogma.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In many cases, the child is trained to fit into a generation that is already over or on its way\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain out. He goes to school where he is taught all kinds of falsehoods. He is supposed to worship\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mysterious authorities who he is never allowed to pin down. He gets high marks If he can\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain memorize all the falsity, hypocrisy and dogma that have found their way into textbooks. If the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain truth within his own nature revolts against all this, he is apt to be classified as a juvenile\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain delinquent. He appears to be brought into the world to be a slave of society, and his training\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain must be along those lines. Slaves are classified. The more training the individual has in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain orthodoxy, the more degrees he is given and there is a strong probability that these will\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain entitle him to higher wages, although this is not necessarily guaranteed, and it does not\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain always work out that way. In the end, the slaves who obtain the highest wages are those who\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain learn the art of hypnotizing subjects, as salesmen or advertising copywriters. Whether\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain president of a corporation or a university, the qualifications required involve one's ability to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain raise money through hypnotic or other means. If one can influence the behavior of others in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain such a way that it benefits an employer financially, one can belong to a higher caste of slaves.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Whether by accident or design, the principal training that the child is given, until he finally\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain begins to fill his role as a slave, is to give society assurance that he will never think for\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain himself. He must merely reflect the mob pattern of society. He is supposed to think those\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain same thoughts that are "accepted." If he can completely avoid the use of his own greater\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mind, he is classified as respectable. He is supposed to reflect the thoughts of others who\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain have lived before him. He is told to honor his father, his mother, his teachers and ultimately\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain his bosses, only because this is more convenient for his father, his mother, his teachers and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain his bosses.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In the September, 1957, issue of Student Forum, is the story of Dr. Malcolm H. Tallman,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematician extraordinary, who was given marks of zero in his early years of school,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain because he knew and employed better, shorter and more efficient methods of solving\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mathematical problems than those known to his instructors. He was not supposed to be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain brilliant. He was merely supposed to reflect ways that had been "accepted" and which were\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain therefore "respectable" This is what any brilliant child is up against in the world. Parents do\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not want children who are smarter than they are. Teachers do not want students who are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain more brilliant than they. Like monkeys, children are supposed to imitate, and they do, but\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain difficulties arise due to the fact that children imitate both the sins as well as the so-called\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain virtues of adults. Then this is not considered as great an evil as thinking.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain An inventor is not an imitator. The inventor is the strange being who actually creates from his\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain own individual mind, and we are told by no less successful a figure than Charles Kettering,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain retired vice-president of General Motors, that the more education a man has the less\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain possibility there is of his ever becoming an inventor. Of course, Mr. Kettering refers to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain orthodox education, and he has degrees from 30 universities, but 29 of these institutions\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain were never attended by Mr. Kettering. They were honorary degrees granted AFTER Mr.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Kettering became successful, possibly because, in his position in life, he was able to help\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain these universities gain endowments. When you can't get degrees one way you can buy them\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in another way.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In some parts of the country, corporal punishment of children in schools is illegal, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain therefore criminal. In other parts of the country it is advocated, and a neurotic teacher is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain given powers of brutality extraordinary. Hearing of such a case where the parents of a child\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain complained because their child was marked by a beating, the writer decided. to investigate a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain little on his own. He went to interview the teacher, a man weighing over 250 pounds. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain child involved was 12 years old and weighed no more than 80 pounds The teacher justified\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain his position by explaining that the boy had beaten up a smaller boy, and, what was he to do\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to protect smaller children under the circumstances? The writer investigated further, found\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that the other boy was also 12 years old,was actually a few pounds lighter, but here we ran\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain into a puzzle. We found that the teacher also flogged the second boy. Why? Obviously, the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain teacher's story was a falsehood. Perhaps what interested us most about this case was the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain obvious fact that the teacher was completely filled with, almost paralyzed by, fear.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Throughout the interview, 250 pounds of flesh trembled from head to feet. Higher school\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain authorities explained that the teacher was not considered as qualified for the job, but in view\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of a shortage of teachers, it was necessary to place such authority in the hands of this\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain person.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain This teacher employed another policy that is often encountered. Inferior teachers find it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain embarrassing to have parents or other adults making inquiries. Children are discouraged from\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain discussing such matters with parents. If they do have such discussions, they are ridiculed,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain called babies and sissies by the teachers in front of a whole class. They soon learn they are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain supposed to accept whatever injustice exists quietly. The child is never allowed a trial by jury\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain or any other kind of a trial.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Our schools are improving. We have far superior schools and teachers today to those of 40\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain years ago, but progress has but touched the surface. We could have better schools and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain better teachers, but we would prefer to spend billions of dollars on atomic bombs, armies, air\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain forces and navies. These agencies must also spend great sums of money on propaganda to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain prevent any changes in this basic system We are rapidly developing government by\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain bureaucracy, where the principal parts of the government are run by persons never elected\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain by the people, but appointed and then protected for life by civil service laws. Improvement\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain can be achieved only by death.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Whatever injustices the child learns in school or at home, he is quite likely to imitate them. As\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain he matures, since he has been trained not to think, but only to reflect the ideas of those who\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain came before him, he is almost certain to practice the same injustices upon the weak that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain were practiced on him when he was weak. We call a man educated when he can imitate. He\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain can always defend himself by saying, "We have always done it this way." It is not a matter of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain what is right or wrong. It is merely a matter of following tradition.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We often find that a teacher has quite different views from those he is teaching, but he feels\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain it is necessary to keep these to himself. There is fear. He might lose his job if his true views\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain were known. He must conform. A certain hypocrisy is necessary. It is a part of the social\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain system. If some truths were generally known, it would be necessary to reprint the textbooks,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and no such risk must be taken because this could very well cut down the profits of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain publishers of textbooks. The book Worlds in Collision proved an unexpected success, but the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain publisher also published textbooks and the publisher found it necessary to sell out his\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain interest in the book to another publisher, because authorities in the fields of astronomy and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrophysics let it be known that they found the volume offensive and in conflict with their\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain routine of thinking, which meant they would soon be buying textbooks elsewhere. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain publisher found it more profitable to conform.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Our greatest motivation is insecurity. We have insecure teachers who must have social\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain security as well as a guarantee that they cannot be discharged, and insecurity is the principal\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain thing we teach children. To conform to what is known to be wrong is supposed to give\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain security That is part of our education.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We mentioned Charles Franklin Kettering. Mr. Kettering has also stated that an inventor can\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain be wrong 999 times out of 1000, if he is right the other time. This is quite different from what\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain we are taught elsewhere. Mr. Kettering was right more than once, but the first time was when\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain he designed and patented a self-starter for an automobile. Mr. Kettering was born near\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Loudonville, Ohio, on August 29th, 1876, and this is a chart that may puzzle students,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain because all of the planets but one, that being Uranus in Leo, are in Earth and Water signs. We\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain are immediately forced to the conclusion that Mr. Kettering could never have developed\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain along the lines he did unless Uranus in Leo was near the ascendant of his birth chart at birth.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Although brilliant in most respects, he was still a conformist in many ways. He graduated in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mechanical engineering in 1904 when little in the way of mechanical engineering had ever\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain been accomplished. The automotive era was just ahead of him. His first job was with a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain telephone company, then National Cash Register Company, and on to General Motors. He\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain always managed to associate with the right people. He didn't actually go too far away from\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain orthodoxy, except in his thinking. He accepted degrees from 29 orthodox institutions. He was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain a master salesman. He had Sun and Mars trine Neptune, in opposition to Saturn, while Saturn\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain sextiled Neptune.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain All of these remarks are to lead us to our question How shall we train children in order to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain improve this situation, and how can astrology help us in training children?\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain First, let us tell you of an interesting trick we picked up from a very brilliant professional\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain psychologist in New York. This man was always fascinated by children. He liked children and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain spent a great deal of time with them and studying them. He liked to study their mental\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain characteristics and abilities. Very small children interested him the most, those who had not\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain been subjected to much in the way of education. It is characteristic of children that they ask\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain questions, and when you supply them with answers, they are quite likely to come back with\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain another question, "WHY?"\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain This psychologist liked to listen to the questions of children, but he asked questions too.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain When they asked, "Why?" he would ask, "What do you think?" He actually encouraged\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain children to think. We do not need to tell you the results. You can find out for yourself. Just\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain encourage small children to think for themselves in the above manner and you will be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain surprised at the results. They may give you just as sound ideas as any you will get from an\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrophysicist, and perhaps far more interesting ones.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain This experiment works best on children of pre-school age. By the time children have passed\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain through a few grades or have attended high school or a university, mental crystallization has\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain already set in.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Let us make it our first aim to encourage children to think, rather than to imitate or accept\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain no-account authorities Without that aim, we are going to be seriously handicapped in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain bringing forth the greatest and most valuable hidden aims the child may have.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It may be necessary to be a bit subtle. A child does have to go to public school. He is no\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain worse off than the other children who have to go to that same school. Although society\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain demands a certain amount of conformance, it could be a lot worse, and it is in other\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain countries. We don't want to place the child in an embarrassing position. The school will teach\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the child many things he must know. The danger lies in trying to fit all the children into one\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mold, and where schools are influenced by modern psychologists, this danger is being\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain overcome. The outlook for the future is much brighter. We want to do nothing that is going to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain cause any unnecessary conflict between the child and his teachers Yet, we want to bring out\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain what is inside the child's mind. We want to bring about a perfectly normal and healthy\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain expression of the child's inner nature. That does not mean that the child is to be encouraged\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in throwing rocks through plate glass windows, or that he is to bully others in any way. It may\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain mean that we have to treat the child more as an equal. We may have to drop the assumption\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that we know so much more than the child, or that our judgment is so superior. We will have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to start out by being open-minded as to the child's potential. Instead of telling the child what\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain he must do and what he must think, let us find out what he wants to do and what he wants to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain think. Then, we must determine what this means in the light of his horoscope. You will soon\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain see that he is expressing the dynamics illustrated and outlined by the horoscope. It will be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain important to determine to what extent the child's views and behavior are influenced by\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain subconscious fear. Fear is always dangerous. That does not mean that caution is never a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain virtue but caution is usually a conscious function, while fear is more likely to be an\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain unconscious motivation. We want to substitute consciousness for unconsciousness. We want\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to help the child to understand himself. If he is afraid, we want to help him to know why he is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain afraid. The moment we can understand that fear is unwarranted, the fear no longer exists.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The child must not fear that which does not exist. A large ratio of adults fear the non-\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain existent, and it is often because of childhood experiences, but the difficulty lies in the fact\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that the fear is on the unconscious level, and people do not know exactly what they fear.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Ron Hubbard, whose work has not been properly explored by any form of orthodoxy, was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain first to put forth the conception that the unconscious functions mathematically and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain automatically; that the subconscious accepts equations that are erroneous and then responds\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in accord with those equations which are untrue. The result is the same as an engineer who is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain applying untruthful equations In building a bridge. It can be disastrous. To give a crude\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain example of the principle involved, let us say that the individual may have once suffered\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain extreme pain at a time when he was in a room excessively decorated with green. His\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain attention may have been on other things. He may never have noted how much green there\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain was in the room, but this was carefully noted unconsciously and recorded in the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain subconscious. The subconscious accepts an equation. Hubbard calls it an engram. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain equation reads GREEN EQUALS PAIN. The individual has no conscious knowledge of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain existence of this equation or engram, because he cannot consciously recall details of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain room. Yet, he walks into a green room and suddenly has some very unpleasant mental and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain emotional experiences. He fears something but he does not know what he fears. Consider\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the trembling of a 250-pound teacher that we mentioned earlier. He did not control his\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain trembling, and it is doubtful whether he knew what caused it.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Many adults are unable to explain their own behavior. They are driven by urges they do not\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain understand. Some of them are neurotic. Others become psychotic. We are told that mental\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain illness is constantly on the increase. We are sympathetic toward adults who have such\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain problems, but should we not be more sympathetic and understanding toward children with\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain similar problems? In the past, it has been the conception that there is no such illness that a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain good beating would not cure. Even today, insane patients are beaten in many mental\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain institutions (although never in the better ones) in order to help cure their illness. During the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain past five years, a case was brought to our attention where the jaw of a patient was broken by\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain an attendant in a state hospital. Immediately thereafter, the patient was submitted to shock\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain treatment without the doctors noting the broken jaw. For a long time thereafter, it was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain impossible to feed the patient orally.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain If we consider that most of the child's behavior is a matter of motor-like actions and is not\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain based on any conscious motives, we are in a better position to begin our work. Whether we\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain are dealing with a child or an adult, once we discover, through the horoscope, the real cause\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of motivation, our best method of getting our knowledge into the mind of the subject is to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ask questions. Don't put things into the mind. Let them come out. Much must come out and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain never go back. Human minds on all age levels are filled with untruths that should be allowed\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to come out and stay out. They don't come out easily because they are on the unconscious\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain level, where the subject does not know about them. He does not understand they for what\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain they are. Working with the child, we have a distinct advantage in that he has not had time to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain accumulate as much in the way of untruths. He has accepted fewer erroneous equations. A\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain very young child has a distinct advantage over his parents in that he has an open mind.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain A parent or a teacher often decides what the career of a child should be. This can be all\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain wrong, and yet, we want to point out that there are public schools today that are employing\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the very best in psychologists and psychiatrists in reaching their conclusions. It is too early to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain evaluate this work, but from here, it looks good, and the very least we can say about it is that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain it is an improvement.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain An Aries or Pluto parent is too apt to know all of the answers. From the moment a child is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain born, the Aries parent may have decided the child's whole career, and from that day on, the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain child may have very little to say about the matter until he becomes of age, when he usually\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain makes a complete break with the parent and goes off on his own. The parent, whose\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain intentions were the best, is never able to understand this. He did everything for the child,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain according to his view, and is now inclined to disinherit him. Yet, if the child turns out to be a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain success, it is noted that the parent is quick to claim credit for the success. It was the child's\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain early training and there is the conviction that the success would have been even greater had\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the child stayed under the domination of the parent.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain What is the child best fitted to do? In the first place, he is best fitted to do that which he\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain wants to do. The idea that the best way is the hardest way may be all right if the only aim is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the building of muscles, but we have the fact that the life span of athletes is below average.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There are parents who believe that a child should be made to work the moment he is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain physically able and that from then on, he should always be made to work to keep his mind on\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain other things. After observing results for more than 40 years, we are forced to the conclusion\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that this policy is a complete failure insofar as the welfare of the child is concerned. He forms\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the habit of doing things the hard way, and never learns to enjoy the better things of life.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The writer has always been interested in what happened to children who were his own\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain companions in school. There were children mainly those of German parentage, who were\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain allowed almost no recreation. The moment they were out of school, they went to work. In no\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain case was this policy based on the need for the children's labor for they were children of well-\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to-do parents. In no case did one of these children make any degree of marked success in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain later life. They started as slaves and usually went through life as slaves, gaining very little out\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of life in return. One died of pneumonia before he was 20. It would have been nice if he\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain could have enjoyed those few years a little. Another broke out and received 40 years in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Atlanta for holding up a mail train. He was pardoned and put on a farm by his German\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain parents to work the rest of his life in considerable seclusion.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Here is a child who was never given a chore to do by his parents. He became a nationally\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain famous cartoonist. As a child, he liked to draw silly pictures, and his parents allowed him to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain go on drawing silly pictures. His silly pictures are well known today, and they pay well. He\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain entertains people. It has been this writer's experience that the children who were never\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain taught the hard way usually went on finding the easy way and fared better.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Here are two brothers. Not only were these two lads never asked to do any work, they were\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain given extraordinary amounts of money to spend. Yet, their father was an immigrant from\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Russia, who came here penniless. One of the boys died a few years ago, but he left over a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain million dollars behind him. His brother is one of the very top names in the moving plectra\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain business. Why do so many parents feel that their children must be trained as slaves? Isn't it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain about time that we caught onto the easier ways? It might be different if we were living in an\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain era of shortages, but we can produce more of everything than we need, and now we are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain worried because this might produce unemployment. If the slaves do not keep on working,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain they might start to think. We find a quotation from James J. Davis which reads, "The person\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain who thinks that the object of living is nothing but work must regard the workhouse or the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain prison as a stepping stone to the ideal. He should not have been born a man but a bee or an\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ant."\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Everywhere, we see the ingenuity of children stifled. We have heard such sayings as,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain "Children should be seen and not heard." There is that one about sparing the rod and spoiling\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the child. A child is supposed to honor his father and his mother, regardless of what their\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain character may be. These statements had to be uttered by the most ignorant of people, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain yet, we hear them quoted daily by more ignorant people who know no other way than to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain imitate. Even when we pass Child Labor Laws, we have to make exceptions for the farmer.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Despite the prosperity that the last 25 years have brought to the farmers of the country, their\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain children do not appear to have benefited. The parents are being paid large sums by the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain government to work less and plant less acreage, but the farmer does not catch on He accepts\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain all the benefits, goes on training his children as slaves, complains about school taxes, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain points to the little red schoolhouse where he obtained his education. What was good enough\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain for him should be good enough for his children. This does not apply to all farmers, but it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain applies to enough of them so that politicians have to make an exception where Child Labor\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Laws are concerned. Therefore, the ratio must be high.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The interpretation of the child's horoscope is accomplished no differently from the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain interpretation of the adult's horoscope, but when we are interpreting a child's horoscope, let\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain us look to tomorrow and away from the evils of yesterday. Let us realize that it is NOT\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain absolutely necessary that we keep on imitating the errors and evils of yesterday We have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain lived in the dark ages long enough. Let's emerge into the light of tomorrow.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Generally speaking, we must start by determining whether the child's general tendency is to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain be dominated by fear (Water and Earth signs) or by the urge to create (Fire and Air signs).\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Bear In mind that, as would appear to be the case of Kettering, mentioned earlier, planets\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain near the ascendent can often dominate a chart Where unconscious fear is sufficiently strong\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in a chart, the child will be inclined to follow along in the parental footsteps. He may be glad\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to accept authorities, because his demand for security makes him reason that this is the safe\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain way. He wants to believe there is a safe way. He wants to believe that there are mental giants\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in the form of men who know all and can be imitated to the end of finding safety and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain security. He wants to believe that his parents are some of these mental giants. This child must\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain be taught that he has a mind of his own if he will but trust it and use it. He must learn that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain there is another door to his mind where true knowledge and wisdom can come in. He can\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain grasp this best when he is very young. The older he gets, the more difficult will be the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain discovery.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In the case of the Fire and Air signs, there will be less desire to imitate. The use of creative\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain forces will come more naturally, but in the case of the Fire signs, the child may be more\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain difficult to handle, unless he is understood and allowed to direct these forces into\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain constructive channels. It is customary to regard the child as ALWAYS WRONG when he does\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not want to conform to the rules that others make. Before judging the child, let us see\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain whether the rules themselves are intelligent or stupid. Give the child a hearing If he thinks the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain rules are stupid, give him a fair chance to present his case. He may surprise you. He might\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain prove his case if he has a fair jury. in that respect, however, don't overlook the fact that there\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is nothing that hurts an adult more than to be proved stupid by a child. For that reason, it is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain very diffIcult to find an unbiased jury if the jury is made up of adults.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In desperation, an adult will often say, "But, don't you think a child must be taught to respect\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain adults?" We must get the facts before we can answer this question.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We must first know whether there is anything about the adults that deserves respect. If there\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is not, and in a very large number of cases there is not, why should we teach the child to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain respect the adult? Why not teach the adult how to be worthy of children's respect? It has\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain been our experience that children do respect adults if they can find any excuse whatsoever\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain for doing so, but if they can find no excuse, why should we continue deceiving the child? In\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain doing so, we are damaging a future generation.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It is preposterous when we stop to realize that the majority of people live in fear of insecurity\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in old age. When they are old, nobody will want them as slaves any more. We have had to set\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain up a social security program. What is more preposterous than the fact that one of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain principal groups who must have a guarantee of security in old age is that group made up of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain teachers? If they have not learned how to take care of themselves, what have they learned,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and what can they teach? Teachers want a guarantee that they can't be discharged and a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain guarantee that security will be provided in old age. That is why they struggle so hard for\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain degrees. We do not consider gamblers as very respectable people, but did you ever find a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain gambler demanding security in his old age? The gambler has what the churches try to tell us\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain we should have. He has faith.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We are doing our best to imitate the ants and the bees. The individual wants to be a pawn of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the state. He is willing to give up freedom for security. The basic principle is Communism or\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Socialism, although we can give it other names. In following this course, we are doing\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain everything in our power to do away with faith in anything but the state.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It is always distasteful for the writer to have to bring in his own experiences to illustrate a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain point, but the most important turning point in the writer's life came when he realized for the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain first time that all the advice ever given him by elders and teachers was the exact reverse of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the truth. It was at this same moment that he made the decision to thoroughly investigate\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain astrology personally. The course of his whole life changed at that moment. Looking back, the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain writer has to observe something that is obvious. At every point in his life when he completely\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain tossed security to the winds, something happened. An opportunity came from nowhere.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Having been born with the Moon in Capricorn,a very insecure configuration, even now it is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain diffIcult to accept this as a fact. How could it be true? There it is! There is the record. To\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain make a success of anything, the principal thing you need is a plan. Next, you need the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain cooperation of others in carrying out that plan. What the writer had to learn was that the way\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to gain the cooperation of others is to assume they are going to give it to you and then ask\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain for it. It is rather amazing to see now far people will go if you just ask. However the person\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain with a Saturnian personality will ask and get NO for an answer, but this is only because of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain depressive characteristics of the Saturnian personality. The modern art of salesmanship is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain based on these factors. Too often, however, modern salesmanship includes a complete lack\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of consideration for the rights of the other party, in other words, a lack of ethics. One of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain largest electric companies of the country with many service guarantee policies trains its\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain repair men not to repair a refrigerator but to convince the owner that there is nothing wrong\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain with it and that it is all right as it is. A very large number of the clientele are sufficiently timid\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to let it go at that. The company increases its profits in this way at the expense of the timid.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain In many instances, the very qualities that are responsible for juvenile delinquency are the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain qualities that could be channeled into constructive effort, but nobody inquires. The child is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain neglected because nobody is interested. He is a nonconformist, and folks are unwilling to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain recognize the fact that nonconformity is the first qualification necessary for genius. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain people who have actually advanced civilization were the nonconformists. There would be no\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain USA if men like Washington and Franklin were conformists. The juvenile delinquent finds\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain reason to resent society and everything connected with it. Unless parents happen to be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain wealthy, in which case he can get away with much more, he may wind up in a reform school,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain where he is not likely to be too well treated. This may be the door of prisons to come. Most\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain prison wardens of today are sympathetic men. They would like to do something to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain rehabilitate the prisoners in their charge, but society is unwilling to finance such efforts.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Society still believes that the way to cure all evils is to subject individuals to punishment,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain pound them down, make them suffer, until conditioned reflexes are created. We have been\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain taught that pain builds character. What do you think has filled prisons and insane asylums?\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Because a few people are able to survive unusual pain without the destruction of character,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain these exceptions to the rule are employed in an endeavor to prove an untruth. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain underworld itself is merely where beaten-down nonconformists congregate. Occasionally,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain one of these nonconformists grows more powerful than society itself, for society is not\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain actually very powerful if we examine it carefully, and then we have a Hitler, and society\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain suffers for its own sins.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Child training in the past has been principally based on the idea of the conditioned reflex.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Any conditioned reflex has to be based on pain. We teach people fear. We teach children to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain be afraid of one thing or another. To teach caution is another matter. In bringing these\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain various evils to light, we must not overlook the fact that the worlds of psychology and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain psychiatry have already made wide progress. The people making up these worlds recognize\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain many of these evils and are trying to produce remedies. In few other places have they been\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain recognized, however, or it might be possible to create something other than a slave world.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Many years back,while with American Astrology Magazine, the writer accumulated over\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 100,000 birth dates of persons and classified them by profession, and although much was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain learned from this study, it does not provide the final answer we are seeking. We know that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the sign Capricorn produces the most doctors and lawyers, but if we solve our real problems\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain we will need neither doctors nor lawyers. They will be able to go home. We know that Cancer\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain produces the best money accumulators, but if we solve our real problems and overcome\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain insecurity, it will be unnecessary for Cancer people to hoard money. The hoarding of money\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain by one individual does not help other individuals. It does not help society. Cecil Fagan has\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain shown that Taurus and Libra produce the most successful military men. We have made\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain independent investigation with different data, and we obtain the same results as Mr. Fagan in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain this respect. Of course, Mr Fagan has used this evidence to try and prove that his Sidereal\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Zodiac is best. We do not agree with this conclusion. Modern military men are not the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Martian type. It is not their job to create violence but to control violence and keep it directed\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain at a target. We do not find the generals in the front line. They don't fight with swords any\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain more. Taurus and Libra are the only signs having the so-called Martian signs, Scorpio and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Aries, as the 7th Cusp.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain A mother approached us with the horoscope of her son. She wanted to know for what\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain profession he should be trained. It was a most interesting chart, and after studying it for a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain while, we were forced to tell the mother, "You can't train this child for his future profession,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain because it does not yet exist." The mother was somewhat bewildered, and we had to explain\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that there was no school into which the parents of the Wright Brothers could have placed\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain their children to train them in the ways of aviation. There were no schools that taught radio in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 1910. There were no schools that taught radar in 1930. There are no schools today that teach\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the professions of tomorrow.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The important message that we must get across in this lesson on youth training is that we\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain must not try to fit youth into yesterday. The answers are not in our minds. They were not in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the minds of our fathers. They are hidden away in the minds of our children. If we want to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain know more about the future of our children, we must ask them. We can't tell them, because\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain we don't know. Let us admit that we don't know. Let us realize that the giants of tomorrow\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain are walking around our feet. Let us stop looking down on them. They can tell us things we do\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not know. Let us cease our false teachings and deception, for all this is merely an expression\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of our own inferiority. Let us cease retarding our children by telling them that they must\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain worship the past, that they must look up to us and have respect for adults. Actually, we\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain should be ashamed of our stupidity. We have little of which we should be proud. Let us ask\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain ourselves now whether we should honor ourselves for selling our children into slavery.\par
