\pard\qc\f0\fs28\b Correspondence Course in Astrology\par
\pard\qc\f1\fs22\i by Carl Payne Tobey\par
\pard\qc\f0\fs26\b Lesson #24\par
\pard\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Human RelationshipsThe only real freedom is found in solitude, but solitude is not insurance of freedom, because\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in solitude the average person is thinking in terms of the outside world. The great seers and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain religious leaders would go into the mountains to peer within, and the mathematician finds his\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain greatest truths within himself. The work of the creative artist comes from within, to be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain imitated by others. Most of the population spends all its time imitating. There but a few\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain creative souls. However, the majority of the work that an astrologer is called upon to perform\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain deals in human relationships, and that brings us to comparison or charts. Boris Sidis, the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain psychologist, once head of the New York State Pathological Hospitals, was of the view that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain as you increase the number of people in a group you lower the average intelligence. They\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain start imitating each other. They begin conforming, and the intelligence level continually\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain drops. That would be to say that if you would be intelligent, be alone, and think for yourself.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain By the time that an astrologer can read charts, he should also be able to compare charts, for\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the procedure and basic principles are the same. One person is born with Mars conjunct\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Uranus, while another is not, but if the second selects a marital mate with Uranus at the same\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain zodiacal degree as his Mars, he will take on the same characteristics as the first man who was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain born with Mars conjunct Uranus. Associating with other people is one way of completely\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain changing your horoscope and your life. It can often be the means of shortening one's life, or\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain it might be the way of accumulating fortune and a life of ease. If you are working with\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain enough people, you are no longer an individual. You are like one cell in a biological system or\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain body. You must, from that time on, obey the plan or pattern of that group, which may be a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain very unintelligent plan. You become a slave to the group unless you can be sufficient of a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain leader to alter the pattern of the functioning unit. In this, few people succeed, principally\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain because they never try. It is easier to copy, imitate, and accept the will of the majority.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain People think they want freedom, but they do not accept it because of their fear of insecurity\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain whereas there can be no real security without freedom. Real security is found only within\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain one's self, for without freedom there is no vital force, and without vital force there is no\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain security. A man may cling to his boss for reasons of security. He may do all of his dirty work,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain but in the end the boss can and will fire him when he is no longer of value to the boss.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain When you have handled personal relationship problems for thirty years, you will realize that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain most human relationships that hang together are based on fear and insecurity. The marriages\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that last longest are not based on love but on insecurity. People live together because of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain their fears. They fight like tigers. They irritate each other, but not enough to overcome fear of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain insecurity. They don't dare live alone. There are marked exceptions to this, but they are few.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The most important thing we should strive for is human relationships that are not based on\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain fear of insecurity.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We are obsessed by the idea that we must accept what society thinks about human relations,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and society is stupid, knowing little or nothing about such matters. We copy. What do others\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain do? What did Moses say? What did he tell us we must do?\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain What is there to indicate that Moses was any more intelligent than Jim Smith? True, he was a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain leader, but how intelligent a leader? In what field of knowledge did he excel? Why are we so\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain dull as to accept his word as that of God? Have his rules ever worked? Have they cleared up\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the problems of society or human relations? Most decidedly they have not. Have they given\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain happy marriages? They have not. Are we to underestimate the intelligence of God to the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain point that we accept the rules of Moses as the level of intelligence of God?\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain If you are to solve human problems, you must toss all these obsolete rules to the dogs and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain start thinking for yourself. Throw them all out and start from the beginning. What do YOU\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain think? What do you HONESTLY think? Start there.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain People put up a front. A marriage may appear to be a very happy one from the outside, but\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain when wife or husband consults an astrologer, the other side of the story comes out. Each may\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain try to convince the other that he or she is happy. Unhappiness may be a deep inner secret,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain something one tries to keep to one's self, but there it is. The fact is that close and intimate\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain relationships become a strain. They lead to all sorts of ailments. Conceal your true inner\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain feelings and put up a front for relatives and the public, and you get one form of illness or\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain another. Sex becomes merely a means of easing a tension. Alcohol becomes the anesthetic to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain dull the pain.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Are there no happy marriages? Yes, there are, but these are the ones where individualism is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain allowed, where intellectual interests predominate, where individual creativeness is allowed to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain exist, and where mates are not dependent on each other for security, where neither party is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain draining the other of vitality and life.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Square aspects develop the greatest emotionalism and introduce the factors of family\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain survival. Mars and Scorpio, Taurus and its ruler, wherever it is, would do the same. Trine\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain aspects introduce creativeness, sextile aspects intellectuality. The conjunction will depend on\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the sign occupied, as well as the planets involved. The opposition aspect introduces change\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of one form or another. The semisextile and quincunx aspects develop insecurity.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain One of the great problems of marriage as we know it is that it subdues individualism, for one\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain party or both. It is better if we respect each other's right to individualism, and that we\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain develop our own individualism. Some conjunctions, most sextiles and trines, and some\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain oppositions will help this process along, but more so when Fire and Air signs are involved\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain rather than Earth and Water signs. We refer to "some" conjunctions and oppositions, because\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain combinations between Saturn and Neptune are seldom if ever beneficial.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Change is one of the unrecognized necessities of life and good health. That is why vacations-\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain are sometimes helpful. The marital institution often does not recognize the necessity for\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain change. You are supposed to have a steady job for security reasons. You 'are supposed to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain own your own home as soon as possible. That will keep you in one place, tie you down, keep\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain you busy making repairs, and help life to become stable, monotonous, boring, routine,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain frustrated and unhealthy. Children might help you break out of the rut if you don't subdue\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain them by beating their brains out. Children have youth and are born with a lack of knowledge\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of conventions. They are not yet ready to settle down in the tomb. Oh yes, if it is what is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain recognized as a good secure marriage, you also make certain to buy a cemetery lot, for isn't\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain that the most appropriate place for such a marriage?\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain A good astrologer has to listen to the client. It is well to let him or her get it all out of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain system first. That is why it is also good to tolerate 10-page, single-space letters.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain If someone wants to get married, first try and find out why. You'll get some pretty good\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain answers on this one. Probe a little. Don't accept the answer, "Because I am in love." That is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain seldom the case. The young girl is often seeking freedom from her parents. Next, she must\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain seek freedom from her husband. One lady tells us that her deceased husband always came\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain home and tossed his salary in her lap. She would like a man to come home and toss money in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain her lap. Many people get married because that is what you are supposed to do. They accept\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the least of all evils insofar as they are able to estimate in advance. Many people are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain lonesome and need company. This is a terrible affliction, for they have never discovered their\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain own inner selves and probably never will.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Some people get married because they want to raise children, and this seems to be the one\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain lofty and only legitimate reason for marriage. If both parties are interested in the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain development of the children, that keeps them from getting in each other's hair. Without the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain desire to have children, people would be better off to live together as long as they want to,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and go on their way when it becomes too monotonous, as it usually does. They could still be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain individuals, without all that com- plete frustration.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Aside from children (Aries), the next loftiest reason for marriage is an appreciation for beauty\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain (Libra). When two people can help each other to seethe beautiful in the design of nature,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain there can be mutual happiness. A young client put this very nicely. "When I see something\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain beautiful, like a beautiful sunset, I like to share it with someone." That helps when the other\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain person has an appreciation for beauty, but many people have none. They may bluff along, but\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain their aesthetic sense has never been developed. This could apply to many of our modern\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain artists who see only the grotesque, and portray it. They are not lifting anyone up. They are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain dragging them down.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain If you want to judge the effect of one personality on another, merely take the first person's\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain chart and insert the other person's planets in that chart in another color of ink. Read them\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain just as if they had been there at birth. There you have it. It is as simple as that, but first, you\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain must be able to read a birth chart. Reverse the procedure, and do the same with the second\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain chart. Practice on cases you know well. You will find a lot of explanations for things. Try it out\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain on all the marriages you know.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Uranus aspects are often most prominent in bringing about divorce. The divorce rate\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain increases to the point where some people are alarmed. They are alarmed because people\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain didn't used to get divorces. What's wrong with people nowadays? People didn't used to ride\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain in automobiles, either. What's wrong with automobiles?\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Marriage is supposed to have been much different years back. People didn't get divorces.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There was never any quarreling. That was because the man was king in his home. The wife\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain did not argue. It was her role only to obey. If she didn't, she got it. There were some\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain restrictions. There is still an old statute in Connecticut which says that a man can beat his wife\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain only with a stick the size of his thumb. This was a great advantage to fat men. Their wives\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain behaved. However, this would seem to indicate that the wives may have been quite sturdy,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain when a man couldn't handle one with his fists. He needed a club.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain There is no foundation for the belief that we must think of marriage as a holy institution. It is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain a man-made institution. Its original purpose was to make certain that children were\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain supported by fathers and would not become a burden on society. It was also a way of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain supporting women, who were supposed to be the weaker sex. Women were property, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain we have always protected property rights first. In some places, women were purchased as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain property. In others, parents paid dowries to get men to relieve them of their daughters and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain support them. Holy matrimony has always been a pretty cold-blooded economic affair. Our\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain modern less holy matrimony is less cold-blooded.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The complexion of marriage within the last fifty years has changed greatly. Girls are educated\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain now. They vote. They take jobs. They smoke cigarettes and drink cocktails. When the writer\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain was a boy, there was a woman in the community who drank beer at home. Not one woman in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain a community of 2000 people ever spoke to or mixed with her. She was isolated from all\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain except her husband and three sons. This was but two miles out side the limits of the City of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain New York. It was whispered that any woman who would take a drink was a prostitute.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Human relations have changed. They will change more. Rules and regulations will change as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain people become enlightened. However, we must review these matters if we are to consider\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain human relations astrologically. We must start with no misconceptions. We must realize that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain one of the worst obstacles involving human relations is the outmoded conception that we are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain battling to maintain. We must realize that up till now some form of selfishness is the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain foundation upon which most of our conventions are built. We must realize that hypocrisy and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain frustrations have been accepted as virtues. It was long accepted that you put up a front, but\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain what you did behind closed doors was all right. There is the old story, told many years ago, of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the elder Morgan of Wall street calling the younger Morgan on the carpet for having been\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain seen out with a woman, not his wife. The younger Morgan is supposed to have pointed out to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the father that he was doing nothing that the father was not doing except that the father did\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain it behind closed doors. The elder man is supposed to have replied, "Young man, that is what\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain closed doors are for."\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Younger people are facing the facts of life. Doctors, psychologists, psychiatrists, lawyers,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain judges and welfare workers are facing the facts. They are no longer viewing marriage as a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain holy institution, but we still have to protect children.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain One of our greatest aims should be to stimulate greater freedom in all human relationships\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and allow people to get rid of their fears, conscious and unconscious. A girl with a good job\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain is more careful in the selection of a mate than the girl who is trying to get out from under the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain pressure of the retarded conceptions of her parents. Marriage is not likely to be happy when\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain it is a form of escape from something. Good Uranus aspects between charts provide\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain liberalism and relationships which grant greater freedom and individualism.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain When Neptune gets involved in marriage, there are strange results. If the aspect is an\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain unfavorable one, there can be that which we call - scandal. Scandal is that which is contrary\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to accepted standards, that which is not looked upon as "holy." Dr. Worden, one of our\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain students, has stirred up considerable discussion about Neptune and its sex factor, which has\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain opened up a new conception of sex as embodying the entire water triplicity of Scorpio,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Cancer and Pisces, which also means Mars, Moon and Neptune. Neptunian people have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain different ideas about marriage, some very unselfish ideas, but scandalous according to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain almost any standards. The idea that marriage should be based on unselfishness is more than\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain society could bear at this time. It is more acceptable that it should be based on passion rather\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain than upon compassion. We find passion in Scorpio and Mars, compassion in Pisces and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Neptune, and the profit motive in Cancer and the Moon.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The Cancer type of marriage can be a financial success and can supply ample frustration. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Scorpio type of marriage can supply passion, jealousy, lots of fights, personal injuries and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain sometimes murder. The Pisces type of marriage can supply unselfishness, compassion,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain sympathy and scandal. All can supply children. The ancients described the Water signs as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain fruitful.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Jupiter will always help any relationship because it leads to education and social revolution,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain something we need badly. It leads to enlightenment. This is true of Sagittarius, but watch the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain points of the Venus and Uranus nodes in Sagittarius and Gemini. They alter things. They\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain become more involved. Favorable aspects between Jupiter and Neptune but particularly the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain conjunction between charts, are excellent. They lift things. Mars-Jupiter combinations are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain passionate but harmonious. They ultimately contribute to great liberalism, although jealousies\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain may have to be passed through at the start.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Pluto-Aries indications lead to greater independence. Saturnian combinations lead to the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain greatest of all frustrations plus every kind of hypocrisy. The same for Capricorn. Venus and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Libra will stir interest in beauty, art, music, good clothes, and at the highest point, in the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain abstract.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It has always been customary to look to the 7th House where marriage is concerned. This is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain justifiable because the 7th House relates to the type of people to whom you are attracted.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Any planet in the 7th House will help to describe the person who attracts you. The sign it is in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain will be important too. The sign on the cusp of the 7th will be important, as well as the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain condition of the planet that rules the 7th House. However, let us not stop there. After a while,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain unless you have very stimulating aspects, marriage will become a routine affair including\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain budget and economic discussions. The gilt wears off. What was previously interesting is less\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain interesting when you see it all of the time. Of course, if you have Saturn in the 7th or Venus in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Capricorn, you may suffer and bear it. Venus conjunct Saturn, or Mars conjunct Saturn, would\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain help along the same lines. The important thing is that once marriage has become a matter of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain routine, it no longer has any relationship to the 7th House It shifts to the 8th and becomes a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Saturnian affair itself. But, if you had one or more planets in the 7th House at birth, there are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain bound to arise new interests. You will be attracted to the new again, unless the planet is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Saturn, Mercury or "Y" (ruler of Taurus). These would tend to tone things down and keep\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain them on the conventional side.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Seventh House factors, and these are to include all opposition aspects, but particularly those\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain between charts, tend to introduce third parties. Unconsciously, a husband may introduce the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain very men to whom his wife is naturally attracted. Of course, it works the other way, too. Signs\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of the zodiac occupied by the planets involved are always important, because the Earth signs\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain will always try to keep things on a practical basis. The woman with Saturn in her 7th will be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain attracted to those she meets through her husband, but only from a point of view of duty. She\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain will serve them, but she wouldn't be likely to have an affair with them. Other planets can\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain produce different results. An opposition of Venus between charts will very often produce\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain adultery.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Venus was long known as the goddess of love. It all depends on what you mean by love.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Venus seeks the beautiful wherever she can find it. She knows nothing about monogamy.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Never heard of it, in fact, unless she happened to get involved with Saturn. Venus enjoys\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain beautiful women or handsome men wherever she finds them. She is social. She is refined. She\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain desires beauty everywhere, in art, in the human form, in music, in clothes. Her personal\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain interest is not really in sex, but she will go along with it. She will try to refine it and raise it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain above any taint of the gross or vulgar. It is Mars that can be gross or vulgar. Venus is not\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain passionate. She can love many if there is the beautiful. She is seeking something higher, much\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain higher, something few people ever understand. It was an astrological chart that first caused\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the writer to begin to delve more deeply into the nature of Venus and Libra, the sign it rules.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Why had he awakened with the complete solution to a mathematical problem that had never\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain entered his head before? A whole flock of planets in Libra. The whole thing was nothing but\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain a matter of balance. The ancients had symbolized Libra with the scales of balance.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Everywhere in nature there is balance until we, ourselves, tip the scales. In the solar system\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the centrifugal just happens to balance gravitation, although the centrifugal and gravitation\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain are merely names for something science doesn't really understand any more than it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain understands electricity or atoms. Balance, everywhere in nature, if you but open your eyes to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain see it, but without a good Venus, or a developed Venus, you will neither see nor understand\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain it. Kepler's laws of planetary motion, design, balance, all represented by Venus. Venus can\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain make a good mathematician. Everywhere in mathematics, there is balance. With the equal\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain sign, you form a mathematical equation. It is only an equation when there is balance. Kepler\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain and Newton understood balance. The great mathematicians all understood balance. They all\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain described mathematics as beautiful. A beautiful woman is one with balanced features. What\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain does all this have to do with the goddess of love? What does it have to do with love? The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain young man who had to have someone with whom to share beauty. When people can share\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain beauty, they are in love. Love, an 11th House matter, not of the 5th or 7th, as so many\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain supposed, the 5th being the 7th of the 11th, the 11th the 5th of the 7th. This is a different\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain kind of love. There is no passion. It is a love of beauty and of sharing. The 11th was the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain House of Friends. Those are friends with whom you can share beauty, even if you are married\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to one of them. Here is the acme of human relations, the sharing of the beauty of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain universe and everything in it. Everything runs according to mathematical laws, even human\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain dynamics, the solids, the crystals, the hexagons, the snowflakes. Even the wild mob in Little\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Rock, Arkansas, is obeying a mathematical pattern. It erupts the first time, after Neptune\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain enters Scorpio, when the Sun conjoins Mars, ruler of Scorpio. Snowflakes obey geometrical\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain laws. Bees obey geometrical laws, while the mob of Little Rock obeys geometrical laws.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Where do we find the highest expression of love? Strangely, in the Family Reform Dynamic\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Guide, strongly suggesting that the whole family relationship needs to be revised. The whole\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain basic principle of the "family" relationship is to pit group against group -- the Hatfields and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the McCoys -- race against race -- the whites against the Negroes, the Arabs against the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Jews. Big mechanized wars belong to Pluto and Aries. Smaller family or racial wars belong to\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Mars and Scorpio. The Little Rock mob erupted when Neptune reached Scorpio and when the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Sun conjoined Mars.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Under any circumstances, the education and philosophy of the individual is to be considered\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain important. These are something others cannot take away from you. They are not like money.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain You can be drained of your money or your nerve force, but you can't be drained of your\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain education and philosophy. We might add religion to these, but in a broad sense, they include\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain it. The person who puts these above money and the grosser considerations of life is\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain protected against many things. He doesn't gravitate into the same kind of relationships that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain he might otherwise.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain We must not forget the ascendent of a chart. For a planet in one chart to be at the ascendent\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of another one is one of the most important possible factors. If the planet be either Venus or\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Jupiter, the results are excellent, unless the ascendent itself or the planet involved is badly\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain afflicted.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain As we have pointed out elsewhere, Mars-Uranus afflictions between charts can hold possible\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain strains, dangers and broad changes. Mars-- Neptune afflictions can hold the worst in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain emotional disturbances. Mars- Saturn afflictions are frustrating. Either of the last two\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain combinations can result in ill health. Mars-Neptune, like Saturn Neptune afflictions, can often\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain lead to some form of neuroticism or mental illness, as well as to other forms of ill health,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain which are probably mental and emotional at their base.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Without going into all the details that we have covered, it is simplification to say that good\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain aspects help a marriage or partnership, while negative aspects hurt it -- all this on the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain unconscious level. Under any circumstances, creative and intellectual aspects will give you a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain lift, while insecure and restrictive aspects will drain your vitality and do away with what we\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain might call your divine protection.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain It is important to realize that marriage, as we know it, or as the churches know it, is not holy\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain matrimony. It isn't holy when it costs money for a license and to pay the minister to make it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain acceptable. These are business aspects. The drive-in chapels give the best rates. The big\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain churches are for people in the higher brackets. All ceremonies help marriage to become more\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of a fetish. There are so many business aspects, wedding gowns, flowers, cocktails, fancy\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain food and all that sort of thing. Rings appeal to the savage and the mercenary qualities in\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain people. A big diamond shows a girl must have gotten something worthwhile. In a pinch she\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain can always hock it for a small part of its cost. Wedding presents, the loot, and a tomb to store\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain it away. People actually seek these things as a part of marriage, and forever after, they have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain to tie themselves to the people who presented them.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The marriage that is made in heaven is the one that helps folks discover heaven within\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain themselves, beauty within themselves -- the one that helps them to contact the abstract\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain within themselves. When they discover these qualities within themselves they can reproduce\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain them in the outside world. This is no different in process from a partnership of two engineers,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain where the engineers utilize abstract mathematical principles, abstract natural law and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain engineering principles and erect a perfectly balanced, well designed and beautiful bridge.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain You cannot build a happy and successful marriage on low and gross motives as a foundation.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain If people understood the higher principles, they would not want to. People do not understand\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the higher principles. If they did, the marital institution would not be what it is today.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Marriage would be too personal a matter to submit to government of social intervention or\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain supervision. Certain groups are allowed to perform marriages. They get paid for it. Put\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain together your own group. Form some new religion, and you can perform marriages. Just\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain become a minister of your own church and you are in business. Somewhat ridiculous, is it not?\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Isn't a marriage actually too personal a matter to take in all these outsiders? Nevertheless, it\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain has to be done for now. Otherwise, it isn't legal (Saturn). As things stand now, in a great ratio\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of cases, marriage is a means of a woman gaining support, a solution to her economic\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain problems. This is her way of earning a living. It is an accepted method. If the marriage proves\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain unbearable for both parties, some honest minded women will gladly walk out and ask no\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain further compensation, but a large ratio will want payments indefinitely continued in the form\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of alimony. In most places, society goes along with this idea because of a purely selfish\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain motive. There is the fear that the woman may become a burden to the state or to society\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain itself. In most states, a judge will grant temporary alimony without listening to any evidential\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain phases of the case. Legal authorities make it plain that this is because of the fear that society\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain itself might have a responsibility to the woman. Community property laws in many states are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain quite equitable. In some, any profit that has been made since marriage occurred is split\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain equally, and each party is again an individual and on his or her own. Whether going into or\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain out of marriage, the whole thing is put on an economic basis. One of the boring things about\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain marriage, as we know it, is that it is merely a branch of economics.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Let us suppose that you are a lofty spirit wanting to rise in the intellectual and perfectly\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain designed world of the abstract, and let us suppose that you are married, and that you find\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain another member of the opposite sex who can lift you in that new world. You are likely to be\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain suspect. There might be sex up there somewhere. There are apt to be jealousies. If there are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain no jealousies, society is going to suspect all parties involved. It must be some strange cult\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain like those to be found in deepest Africa. Society condemns what it does not understand, and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain it understands little. It will have to go back a few thousand years into the deep dark past and\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain consult Moses.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Marriage should bring intellectual benefits to both parties. Otherwise, it may be too much\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain like breeding cattle. When there is no longer mutual intellectual benefit, what is left but\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain frustration and death, the Saturnian variety of death. Is it then unwise to seek the help of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Uranus in seeking change? Is this disgraceful? Are we to progress or go retrograde? Are we\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain going on to create a better future, or are we going back, down the backward scale of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain evolution, maybe down to monkeys or fish? The future holds hope for the creative mind. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain past holds frustration. Which way are we going?\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Marriage often holds a purpose. Most any human relationship can have a purpose. The\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain purpose of one marriage may be fulfilled in a year. Perhaps another takes a lifetime. When\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain the purpose of a marriage is served, should the remainder of life be taken up with the funeral\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain procession and the mourning? Should the wails echo night after night? Should life be a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain perpetual funeral? Should it be made up as a salad of frustration? Where there are children,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain they must be provided for. They must be educated. They should have love and affection.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain They should be guided, but can these things be successfully accomplished in a home that is a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain tomb?\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Marriage is not the only human relationship. There are business relationships Nobody blames\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain a man for switching jobs, bosses or corporations when he can better himself, although even\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain this was not always the case. A man was once looked upon with suspicion if he changed jobs\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain too often. He wasn't steady or stable. He couldn't stick at one thing. The first question asked\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain was, "Why did you leave your last job?" If you answered that it was because your former boss\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain was a big, unethical pirate you wouldn't have much chance of getting a new job, because no\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain other big, unethical pirate would want to hire you. To be a business man in those days, it was\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain pretty well recognized that you had to be a big, unethical pirate. That isn't so long ago. Forty\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain years would do it. All the big, unethical pirates have not departed yet.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain The marriage institution has not been handled like other human relationships, because of the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain factor of children. This was justifiable. It can't be handled just the same. You can't quit\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain children like you quit a job, although children often do plenty of suffering under the present\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain setup. It is odd that the 5th House, which represents children (Aries) is in opposition to the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain 11th House, which represents the higher phases of love and friendship (Libra). Yet, the\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain opposition need not be considered as unfavorable. It brings change. We can't have\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain improvement without change. Ultimately, we should be able to deliver from the abstract\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain world a more perfect design for marriage. The present one is quite faulty. We can't find\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain perfection in anything molded to that design because the design is defective.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain As an overall policy bent on the improvement of human relationships, we should look for help\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain from Venus, Jupiter, and at times Uranus. Perhaps we should also look to "Z", ruler of Gemini,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain which we suspect is about 20-Pisces in 1957 and progressing at the approximate rate of a\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain degree in 5.3 years. Our suspicions might be wrong, but we appear to get more and more\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain verification for this suspicion as we continue research on the subject.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Let us repeat something we said at the outset. If you are to solve problems of human\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain relationships, toss the obsolete rules to the dogs and start thinking for yourself. Toss out\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain everything and start from the beginning. What do YOU think? What do you HONESTLY\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain think? Don't be swayed by us any more than you think you should. Don't let Moses do your\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain thinking for you, but don't let us do it either. In so far as astrology is concerned, we think your\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain experience will bear out the astrological conceptions we have presented, but don't stop here.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Don't allow our views to become Saturnian crystallization in your mind. Go on from here. Let\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Uranus, Venus and Jupiter work for you too. Utilize your own God-given intellectual qualities.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Improve on our conceptions wherever and whenever you can. We are not like Moses. We are\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain not telling you that this is the word of God. That expression is merely a crutch. The word of\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain God can be misinterpreted and probably always has been, except in the case of those who\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain have discovered beautiful mathematical designs in nature, mental and emotional as well as\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain physical natural laws, for these are truly the word of God.\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain Two years have elapsed since we began writing this Course, and with this 24th Lesson, we\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain have completed the originally outlined design. We finish at 10:30 PM on September 24th,\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain l957 (Mountain Standard Time). Sun, Mars and the Moon are all in Libra. With the exception\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain of three of the Lessons, they were all written with the Moon in Libra, in order to catch that\par
\pard\f1\fs20\plain abstract cosmic design. Jupiter was in Leo when we started, but it is in Libra as we finish.#clean\par
}